  ["feature.blessed-strikes.tce2014.cleric.grave.8"]={title="Blessed Strikes",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn."},
  ["feature.blessed-strikes.xphb2024.cleric.base.7"]={title="Blessed Strikes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 71\n\nDivine power infuses you in battle. You gain one of the following options of your choice (if you get either option from a Cleric subclass in an older book, use only the option you choose for this feature)."},
  ["optionalfeature.blessed-warrior.tce2014"]={title="Blessed Warrior",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\nYou learn two cantrips of your choice from the spells. They count as paladin spells for you, and Charisma is your spellcasting ability for them. Whenever you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of these cantrips with another cantrip from the cleric spell list."},
  ["feat.blessed-warrior.xphb2024"]={title="Blessed Warrior",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou learn two spells of your choice. XPHB and XPHB are recommended. The chosen cantrips count as Paladin spells for you, and Charisma is your spellcasting ability for them. Whenever you gain a Paladin level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another Cleric cantrip."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-bloody-might.bmt2014"]={title="Blessing of Bloody Might",subtitle="Recompensa - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\nYour Strength score increases by 2, to a maximum of 22.\n\nConsequence\n\nThe character is cursed with werewolf MM (see the MM) until the blessing ends on them. On nights when the moon is full, the cursed character flies into a rage that lasts until dawn; while in this state, the character becomes an NPC under the DM's control."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-dumathoin.pabtso2014"]={title="Blessing of Dumathoin",subtitle="Recompensa - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nYour eyes become keen enough to pick out hidden secrets. You gain darkvision. If you already had darkvision, you can see in color in the dark. In addition, you can use an action to gain truesight for 1 minute. Once you gain truesight in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-health.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Health",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nYour Constitution score increases by 2, up to a maximum of 22."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-health.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Health",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 98\n\nYour Constitution score increases by 2, up to a maximum of 22."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-lonely-genius.bmt2014"]={title="Blessing of Lonely Genius",subtitle="Recompensa - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\nYour Intelligence score increases by 2, to a maximum of 22.\n\nConsequence\n\nThe character's intellect rubs old friends the wrong way. Three NPCs of the DM's choice become indifferent or hostile toward the character, and the character automatically fails any Charisma check made to improve their attitudes."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-magic-resistance.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Magic Resistance",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-magic-resistance.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Magic Resistance",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 98\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects."},
  ["feature.blessing-of-moonlight.frhof2014.bard.moon.6"]={title="Blessing of Moonlight",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared.\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can modify the spell so that you glow faintly while the spell is active. While glowing, you shed XPHB out to 5 feet, and whenever a creature fails its saving throw against the effects of this Moonbeam, another creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of yourself regains 2d4 XPHB.\n\nOnce you use this feature to modify a casting of Moonbeam, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-protection.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Protection",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to AC and saving throws."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-protection.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Protection",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to AC and saving throws."},
  ["feature.blessing-of-the-forge.xge2024.cleric.forge.1"]={title="Blessing of the Forge",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 18\n\nAt 1st level, you gain the ability to imbue magic into a weapon or armor. At the end of a long rest, you can touch one nonmagical object that is a suit of armor or a items. Until the end of your next long rest or until you die, the object becomes a magic item, granting a +1 bonus to AC if it's armor or a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls if it's a weapon.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-the-frostmaiden.idrotf2014"]={title="Blessing of the Frostmaiden",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nYour eyes become as cold as ice. You gain immunity to cold damage. In addition, you can cast the cone of cold spell (save 15) once. You regain the ability to cast this spell when you finish a long rest."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-the-lone-champion.drde2014"]={title="Blessing of the Lone Champion",subtitle="Recompensa - DrDe - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\nYou gain the following benefits:\n\n• Heroic Inspiration\n\n• Temporary Hit Points"},
  ["reward.blessing-of-the-morninglord.idrotf2014"]={title="Blessing of the Morninglord",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nYou gain 10 temporary hit points each day at dawn."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-the-solipsistic-mind.pabtso2014"]={title="Blessing of the Solipsistic Mind",subtitle="Recompensa - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 177\n\nYou access esoteric truths from an ancient tome by focusing deeply on your own thoughts. You can take an action to focus your inner mind. This focus lasts for 1 hour. While your inner mind is focused, you can't take reactions. For the duration, when you make an Intelligence check, Wisdom check, Intelligence saving throw, or Wisdom saving throw, you can roll a d8 and add the number rolled to the ability check or saving throw. You regain the ability to focus your inner mind when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.blessing-of-the-trickster.phb2014.cleric.trickery.1"]={title="Blessing of the Trickster",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nStarting when you choose this domain at 1st level, you can use your action to touch a willing creature other than yourself to give it advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. This blessing lasts for 1 hour or until you use this feature again."},
  ["feature.blessing-of-the-trickster.xphb2024.cleric.trickery.3"]={title="Blessing of the Trickster",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["reward.blessing-of-understanding.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Understanding",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nYour Wisdom score increases by 2, up to a maximum of 22."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-understanding.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Understanding",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nYour Wisdom score increases by 2, up to a maximum of 22."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-unearned-riches.bmt2014"]={title="Blessing of Unearned Riches",subtitle="Recompensa - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\nThe next time you search among or retrieve something from your belongings, you find an unmarked PHB containing five 1,000 gp gemstones.\n\nConsequence\n\nThe character's new fortune garners unwanted attention from a guild of violent mercenaries, who claim to have been robbed of exactly 5,000 gp worth of gems the same day as the character found the windfall. Every night for the next 7 days, the character is attacked by 1d4 neutral evil Veteran. When the attacks end, so does this blessing."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-valhalla.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Valhalla",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nThis blessing grants you the power to summon spirit warriors, as if you had blown a horn of valhalla, silver. Once you use this blessing, you can't use it again until 7 days have passed."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-valhalla.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Valhalla",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nThis Blessing grants you the power to summon spirit warriors, as if you are blowing a XDMG. Once you use this Blessing, you can't use it again until 7 days have passed."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-weapon-enhancement.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Weapon Enhancement",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nOne nonmagical weapon in your possession becomes a +1 weapon whenever you wield it."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-weapon-enhancement.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Weapon Enhancement",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nOne nonmagical weapon in your possession becomes a XDMG while you wield it."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-wound-closure.dmg2014"]={title="Blessing of Wound Closure",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nThis blessing grants you the benefits of a periapt of wound closure."},
  ["reward.blessing-of-wound-closure.xdmg2024"]={title="Blessing of Wound Closure",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nThis Blessing grants you the benefits of a XDMG."},
  ["feature.blessings-of-knowledge.frhof2014.cleric.knowledge.3"]={title="Blessings of Knowledge",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\nYou gain proficiency with one type of XPHB of your choice and in two of the following skills of your choice: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. You have XPHB in those two skills."},
  ["feature.blessings-of-knowledge.phb2014.cleric.knowledge.1"]={title="Blessings of Knowledge",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["deity.blibdoolpoolp.phb2014"]={title="Blibdoolpoolp",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["spell.blight.phb2014"]={title="Blight",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nNecromantic energy washes over a creature of your choice that you can see within range, draining moisture and vitality from it. The target must make a Constitution saving throw. The target takes 8d8 necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs.\n\nIf you target a plant creature or a magical plant, it makes the saving throw with disadvantage, and the spell deals maximum damage to it.\n\nIf you target a nonmagical plant that isn't a creature, such as a tree or shrub, it doesn't make a saving throw, it simply withers and dies."},
  ["spell.blight.xphb2024"]={title="Blight",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 247\n\nA creature that you can see within range makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 8d8 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A Plant creature automatically fails the save.\n\nAlternatively, target a nonmagical plant that isn't a creature, such as a tree or shrub. It doesn't make a save; it simply withers and dies."},
  ["item.blight-ichor.egw2014"]={title="Blight Ichor",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis bitter chartreuse concoction is distilled from a fungus native to the Blightshore badlands. The sickly green liqueur harbors potent psychedelic properties. Provided it is neither a construct nor undead, a creature subjected to a dose of blight ichor gains advantage on Intelligence and Wisdom checks, as well as vulnerability to psychic damage, for 1 hour. For each dose of blight ichor consumed, the creature must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1d6 hours and suffer the effects of a confusion spell for 1 minute. An undead creature subjected to a dose of blight ichor gains advantage on all Dexterity checks and is immune to the frightened condition for 1 hour."},
  ["creature.blight-totem-elemental.psx2014"]={title="Blight Totem Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.blind-artist.toa2014"]={title="Blind Artist",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 164\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 0\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, poisoned"},
  ["optionalfeature.blind-fighting.tce2014"]={title="Blind Fighting",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 41\n\nYou have blindsight with a range of 10 feet. Within that range, you can effectively see anything that isn't behind Cover, even if you're blinded or in darkness. Moreover, you can see an invisible creature within that range, unless the creature successfully hides from you."},
  ["feat.blind-fighting.xphb2024"]={title="Blind Fighting",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 209\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 10 feet."},
  ["psionic.blind-spot.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Blind Spot",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nAs an action, you erase your image from the mind of one creature you can see within 120 feet of you; the target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or you are invisible to it until the end of your next turn."},
  ["condition.blinded.phb2014"]={title="Blinded",subtitle="Condicao - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 290\n\n• A blinded creature can't see and automatically fails any ability check that requires sight.\n\n• Attack rolls against the creature have advantage, and the creature's attack rolls have disadvantage."},
  ["condition.blinded.xphb2024"]={title="Blinded",subtitle="Condicao - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 361\n\nWhile you have the Blinded condition, you experience the following effects.\n\nCan't See\n\nYou can't see and automatically fail any ability check that requires sight.\n\nAttacks Affected\n\nXPHB rolls against you have XPHB, and your attack rolls have XPHB."},
  ["creature.blinded-troll.wdh2014"]={title="Blinded Troll",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 114\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 4\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20"},
  ["creature.blindheim.mff2014"]={title="Blindheim",subtitle="Criatura - MFF - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 26 (4d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 8 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRadiant Eyes\n\nWhile its eyes are open, a blindheim projects bright light in a 60-foot cone and dim light for an additional 60 feet. It sets the orientation of this cone at the end of each of its turns. All creatures that can see the blindheim have disadvantage on attack rolls while in the area of bright light and within 15 feet of the blindheim. Creatures with the Sunlight Sensitivity trait that can see the blindheim have disadvantage on attack rolls anywhere in the area of bright light.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. Hit: 5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nRadiant Blast\n\nRadiant energy erupts from the blindheim's eyes in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or take 7 (2d6) radiant damage and be blinded until the end of the blindheim's next turn. Creatures with the Sunlight Sensitivity trait have disadvantage on this saving throw."},
  ["spell.blinding-smite.phb2014"]={title="Blinding Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nThe next time you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack during this spell's duration, your weapon flares with bright light, and the attack deals an extra 3d8 radiant damage to the target. Additionally, the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or be blinded until the spell ends.\n\nA creature blinded by this spell makes another Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns. On a successful save, it is no longer blinded."},
  ["spell.blinding-smite.xphb2024"]={title="Blinding Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 247\n\nThe target hit by the strike takes an extra 3d8 Radiant damage from the attack, and the target has the XPHB condition until the spell ends. At the end of each of its turns, the XPHB target makes a Constitution saving throw, ending the spell on itself on a success."},
  ["spell.blindness-deafness.phb2014"]={title="Blindness/Deafness",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nYou can blind or deafen a foe. Choose one creature that you can see within range to make a Constitution saving throw. If it fails, the target is either blinded or deafened (your choice) for the duration. At the end of each of its turns, the target can make a Constitution saving throw. On a success, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.blindness-deafness.xphb2024"]={title="Blindness/Deafness",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 248\n\nOne creature that you can see within range must succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or it has the XPHB or XPHB condition (your choice) for the duration. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."},
  ["feature.blindsense.phb2014.rogue.base.14"]={title="Blindsense",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.blink.phb2014"]={title="Blink",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nRoll a d20 at the end of each of your turns for the duration of the spell. On a roll of 11 or higher, you vanish from your current plane of existence and appear in the Ethereal Plane (the spell fails and the casting is wasted if you were already on that plane). At the start of your next turn, and when the spell ends if you are on the Ethereal Plane, you return to an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of the space you vanished from. If no unoccupied space is available within that range, you appear in the nearest unoccupied space (chosen at random if more than one space is equally near). You can dismiss this spell as an action.\n\nWhile on the Ethereal Plane, you can see and hear the plane you originated from, which is cast in shades of gray, and you can't see anything there more than 60 feet away. You can only affect and be affected by other creatures on the Ethereal Plane. Creatures that aren't there can't perceive you or interact with you, unless they have the ability to do so."},
  ["spell.blink.xphb2024"]={title="Blink",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 248\n\nRoll 1d6 at the end of each of your turns for the duration. On a roll of 4-6, you vanish from your current plane of existence and appear in the Ethereal Plane (the spell ends instantly if you are already on that plane). While on the Ethereal Plane, you can perceive the plane you left, which is cast in shades of gray, but you can't see anything there more than 60 feet away. You can affect and be affected only by other creatures on the Ethereal Plane, and creatures on the other plane can't perceive you unless they have a special ability that lets them perceive things on the Ethereal Plane.\n\nYou return to the other plane at the start of your next turn and when the spell ends if you are on the Ethereal Plane. You return to an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of the space you left. If no unoccupied space is available within that range, you appear in the nearest unoccupied space."},
  ["creature.blink-dog.mm2014"]={title="Blink Dog",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 318\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Blink Dog, understands Sylvan but can't speak it\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe dog has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nTeleport {@recharge 4}\n\nThe dog magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 40 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. Before or after teleporting, the dog can make one bite attack."},
  ["language.blink-dog.mm2014"]={title="Blink Dog",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 318"},
  ["creature.blink-dog.xmm2024"]={title="Blink Dog",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Blink Dog, understands Elvish and Sylvan but can't speak them\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport {@recharge 4}\n\nThe dog teleports up to 40 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["language.blink-dog.xmm2024"]={title="Blink Dog",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 46"},
  ["creature.blistercoil-weird.ggr2014"]={title="Blistercoil Weird",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFeed on Fire\n\nIf the weird takes fire damage from a spell or other magical effect, its size increases by one category. If there isn't enough room for the weird to increase in size, it attains the maximum size possible in the space available. While the weird is Large or bigger, it makes Strength checks and saving throws with advantage. If the weird starts its turn at Gargantuan size, the weird releases energy in an explosion. Each creature within 30 feet of the weird must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The explosion ignites flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried. The weird's size then becomes Medium.\n\nForm of Fire and Water\n\nThe weird can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing. In addition, the weird can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. The first time the weird enters another creature's space on a turn, that creature takes 5 (1d10) fire damage and catches fire; until someone takes an action to douse the fire, the burning creature takes 5 (1d10) fire damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\nHeated Body\n\nA creature that touches the weird or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 5 (1d10) fire damage.\n\nIllumination\n\nThe weird sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage, or 11 (2d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) fire damage if the weird is Large or bigger."},
  ["traphazard.blizzard.idrotf2014"]={title="Blizzard",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nThe blizzards that ravage Icewind Dale and harry travelers on the mountain pass are reflections of Auril's self-imposed isolation. A blizzard in Icewind Dale typically lasts 2d4 hours, and whenever the characters are caught in one, the following rules apply until it ends.\n\nA blizzard's howling wind limits hearing to a range of 100 feet and imposes disadvantage on ranged weapon attack rolls. It also imposes disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing. The wind extinguishes open flames, disperses fog, erases tracks in the snow, and makes flying by nonmagical means nearly impossible. A creature falls at the end of its turn if it is flying by nonmagical means and can't hover.\n\nVisibility in a blizzard is reduced to 30 feet. Creatures without goggles or other eye protection have disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight due to blowing snow.\n\nAny creature that is concentration on a spell in a blizzard must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw at the end of its turn or lose its concentration on the spell unless the creature is sheltered against the elements (for example, in an igloo).\n\nVeering Off Course\n\nIt's easy to veer off course while traveling through a blizzard, and it's also easy for party members to become separated from one another, which is why the wisest course of action is to stay put and wait for the blizzard to pass.\n\nIf the characters travel during a blizzard, have the players designate one party member as the navigator. At the end of each hour of travel through the blizzard, the DM makes a 15 Wisdom (Survival) check on behalf of the navigator. On a successful check, the party stays on course. On a failed check, the party wanders off course, putting its members no closer to their destination than they were at the start of that hour. If the check fails by 5 or more and the party members aren't tied together, one randomly determined party member becomes lost in the blizzard and separated from the others. If the group tries to reunite with its missing member, have the party members (including the missing one) make a 15 Wisdom (Survival) group check at the end of each hour. If this group check succeeds, the missing party member is found, but no progress is made toward reaching the group's intended destination that hour. The group check can be repeated after each hour spent searching for the missing party member."},
  ["creature.blob-of-annihilation.xmm2024"]={title="Blob of Annihilation",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 47\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 448 (23d20 + 207)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 28 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAstral Implosion\n\nIf the blob is reduced to 0 XPHB, it implodes and ejects any creatures and objects engulfed by it into the Astral Sea. The blob itself vanishes, leaving behind a layer of slime on everything that was within 600 feet of it. In 1d20 years, the blob reconstitutes on a random world in the Material Plane.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the blob fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe blob has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe blob makes two Pseudopod attacks and uses Engulf. It can replace one attack with a use of Restraining Glob.\n\nPseudopod\n\nm 15, reach 30 ft. h24 (3d10 + 8) Force damage.\n\nEngulf\n\nThe blob moves up to its XPHB and can move through the spaces of Huge or smaller creatures and objects. str 23, each creature or object whose space the blob enters for the first time during this move. actSaveFail The target is engulfed. While engulfed, a target has XPHB against attacks and other effects outside the blob, and when the blob moves, the engulfed target moves with it. A nonmagical object is destroyed after spending 1 minute engulfed.\n\nWhile engulfed, a creature takes 21 (6d6) Force damage at the start of each of its turns, is suffocating, has the XPHB condition, and repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. An engulfed creature that is reduced to 0 XPHB dissolves into ash, which is ejected into the Astral Sea. actSaveSuccess The target escapes and enters the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nRestraining Glob\n\nThe blob lobs a slimy glob at one Large or smaller creature it can see within 600 feet of itself. dex 23, the targeted creature. actSaveFail 18 (3d6 + 8) Acid damage. The glob rolls the target 60 feet straight toward the blob, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, when the glob harmlessly dissolves. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDecay\n\nThe blob deals 14 (4d6) Necrotic damage to each creature engulfed by it. The blob can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nGrasping Glob\n\nThe blob uses Restraining Glob. The blob can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nLashing Goop\n\nThe blob makes one Pseudopod attack."},
  ["item.block-and-tackle.phb2014"]={title="Block and Tackle",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA set of pulleys with a cable threaded through them and a hook to attach to objects, a block and tackle allows you to hoist up to four times the weight you can normally lift."},
  ["item.block-and-tackle.xphb2024"]={title="Block and Tackle",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA XPHB allows you to hoist up to four times the weight you can normally lift."},
  ["magicitem.blod-stone.skt2014"]={title="Blod Stone",subtitle="Item Magico - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis diamond contains the blood of a creature—blood that appears in the form of the blod (blood) rune. While the item is on your person, you can use your action to divine the location of the creature nearest to you that is related to the blood in the item and that isn't undead. You sense the distance and direction of the creature relative to your location. The creature is either the one whose blood is in the item or a blood relative.\n\nThis item is made from a large diamond worth at least 5,000 gp. When the blood of a creature is poured onto it during the creation process, the blood seeps into the heart of the gem. If the gem is destroyed, the blood evaporates and is gone forever. A vengeful being might use a blod stone to hunt down an entire bloodline. Such stones are sometimes given as gifts to siblings or handed down from parent to child."},
  ["magicitem.blood-amulet.au2014"]={title="Blood Amulet",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis delicate amulet looks like a diminutive beating heart impaled with spikes. It has 3 charges and regains 1d3 charges daily at dawn.\n\nWhenever you deal damage to a creature, you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic damage to the target and force it to make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target gains 1 XPHB level."},
  ["creature.blood-drinker-vampire.ggr2014"]={title="Blood Drinker Vampire",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 18 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe vampire makes three melee attacks, only one of which can be a bite attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one willing creature, or a creature that is grappled by the vampire, incapacitated, or restrained. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage. If the target is humanoid, it must succeed on a 15 Charisma saving throw or be charmed by the vampire for 1 minute. While charmed in this way, the target is infatuated with the vampire. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the necrotic damage taken, and the vampire regains hit points equal to that amount. The reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0.\n\nRapier\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage. The vampire can also grapple the target (escape 14) if it is a creature and the vampire has a hand free.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe vampire adds 3 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the vampire must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["magicitem.blood-fury-tattoo.tce2014"]={title="Blood Fury Tattoo",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nProduced by a special needle, this magic tattoo evokes fury in its form and colors.\n\nTattoo Attunement\n\nTo attune to this item, you hold the needle to your skin where you want the tattoo to appear, pressing the needle there throughout the attunement process. When the attunement is complete, the needle turns into the ink that becomes the tattoo, which appears on the skin.\n\nIf your attunement to the tattoo ends, the tattoo vanishes, and the needle reappears in your space.\n\nBloodthirsty Strikes\n\nThe tattoo has 10 charges, and it regains all expended charges daily at dawn. While this tattoo is on your skin, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can expend a charge to deal an extra 4d6 necrotic damage to the target, and you regain a number of hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt.\n\n• When a creature you can see damages you, you can expend a charge and use your reaction to make a melee attack against that creature, with advantage on your attack roll."},
  ["creature.blood-hawk.mm2014"]={title="Blood Hawk",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 319\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight\n\nThe hawk has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe hawk has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the hawk's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBeak\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.blood-hawk.xmm2024"]={title="Blood Hawk",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 350\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 7 (2d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe hawk has XPHB on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the hawk's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBeak\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage if the target is XPHB."},
  ["creature.blood-hunter.egw2014"]={title="Blood Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 284\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 9 | WIS 16 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Curse of Binding (1/Day)\n\nAs a bonus action, the blood hunter targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or have its speed reduced to 0 and be unable to take reactions. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe blood hunter has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe blood hunter has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe blood hunter attacks twice with a weapon.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) fire damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h6 (1d10 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["item.blood-of-the-lycanthrope.imr2014"]={title="Blood of the Lycanthrope",subtitle="Item - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis poison is created from blood harvested from a dead or incapacitated lycanthrope in its animal or hybrid form. A creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with MM (see the Monster Manual). The curse lasts until removed by the remove curse spell or similar magic.\n\nThe type of lycanthropy depends on the lycanthrope used to create the poison. To determine the type of lycanthropy randomly, roll a d6:\n\nd6 | Lycanthropy\n\n1-3 | Wererat\n\n4-5 | Werewolf\n\n6 | Wereboar"},
  ["magicitem.blood-of-the-lycanthrope-antidote.imr2014"]={title="Blood of the Lycanthrope Antidote",subtitle="Item Magico - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis clear potion has dark red flecks within, resembling clotted blood. When you drink this potion, it removes the curse of lycanthropy from you if that curse was imposed by a lycanthrope's bite or similar effect."},
  ["magicitem.blood-spear.cos2014"]={title="Blood Spear",subtitle="Item Magico - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nKavan was a ruthless chieftain whose tribe lived in the Balinok Mountains centuries before the arrival of CoS. Although he was very much alive, Kavan had some traits in common with vampires: he slept during the day and hunted at night, he drank the blood of his prey, and he lived underground. In battle, he wielded a spear stained with blood. His was the first blood spear, a weapon that drains life from those it kills and transfers that life to its wielder, imbuing that individual with the stamina to keep fighting.\n\nWhen you hit with a melee attack using this magic spear and reduce the target to 0 hit points, you gain 2d6 temporary hit points.\n\nAny creature can wield the spear, but only the character CoS to wield it gains a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."},
  ["creature.blood-witch.ggr2014"]={title="Blood Witch",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 13 | WIS 9 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal plus any one language (usually Common)\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Witch Dance\n\nThe witch can use a bonus action to control the movement of one creature cursed by its hex spell that it can see within 30 feet of it. The creature must succeed on a 15 Charisma saving throw or use its reaction to move up to 30 feet in a direction of the witch's choice.\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the witch's darkvision.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe witch makes two attacks: one with its longsword and one with its shortsword.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.blood-toll-harpy.mot2014"]={title="Blood-Toll Harpy",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 227\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 13 | CON 10 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe harpy has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nDark Devotion\n\nThe harpy has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe harpy makes two melee attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["magicitem.bloodaxe.egw2014"]={title="Bloodaxe",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic axe. The axe deals an extra 1d6 necrotic damage to creatures that aren't constructs or undead. If you reduce such a creature to 0 hit points with an attack using this axe, you gain 10 temporary hit points.\n\nThis axe is forged from a dark, rust-colored metal and once belonged to the goliath barbarian Grog Strongjaw of Vox Machina."},
  ["creature.bloodfray-giant.ggr2014"]={title="Bloodfray Giant",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / H\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 103 (9d12 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 9 | CON 20 | INT 7 | WIS 8 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nChain\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 17). Until the grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the giant can't use this attack on anyone else.\n\nRock\n\nrw 9 to hit, range 60/240 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFurious Defense\n\nAfter a creature the giant can see is dealt damage by a foe within 20 feet of the giant, the giant makes a chain attack against that foe."},
  ["feat.bloodlust.abh2014"]={title="Bloodlust",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nPowerful Recovery\n\nWhen you roll a XPHB to regain XPHB, you can treat any roll of 1 or 2 as a 3.\n\nSanguine Feast\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a XPHB creature that isn't a Construct or Undead with an attack roll, you can expend a XPHB, roll it, and regain a number of XPHB equal to the number rolled plus your Constitution modifier.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.bloodrage-greataxe.bmt2014"]={title="Bloodrage Greataxe",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 66\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic greataxe while you have half your hit points or fewer."},
  ["item.bloodstone.dmg2014"]={title="Bloodstone",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque dark gray with red flecks gemstone."},
  ["item.bloodstone.xdmg2024"]={title="Bloodstone",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA dark gray with red flecks gemstone."},
  ["feature.bloodthirst.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.3"]={title="Bloodthirst",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nWhen an enemy you can see within 30 feet of yourself takes damage and is XPHB after taking that damage but not killed outright, you can take a XPHB and XPHB to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of that enemy. You can then make one melee attack. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["item.blowgun.phb2014"]={title="Blowgun",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.blowgun.xphb2024"]={title="Blowgun",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.blowgun-needle.phb2014"]={title="Blowgun Needle",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.blowgun-needles-50.phb2014"]={title="Blowgun Needles (50)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.blue-abishai.mpmm2014"]={title="Blue Abishai",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 50\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 22 | WIS 23 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the abishai's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe abishai has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe abishai makes three Bite or Lightning Strike attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) lightning damage.\n\nLightning Strike\n\nrs 12 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h36 (8d8) lightning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport\n\nThe abishai teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that it can see."},
  ["creature.blue-abishai.mtf2014"]={title="Blue Abishai",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 161\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 195 (26d8 + 78)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 50\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 22 | WIS 23 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the abishai's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe abishai has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe abishai's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe abishai makes two attacks: one with its quarterstaff and one with its bite.\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) lightning damage."},
  ["magicitem.blue-chromatic-rose.wbtw2014"]={title="Blue Chromatic Rose",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Chromatic Rose|WBtW"},
  ["magicitem.blue-dragon-mask.rotos2014"]={title="Blue Dragon Mask",subtitle="Item Magico - RoTOS - 2014",body="Pagina: 4\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis mask of glossy azure has spikes around its edges and a ridged horn in its center. The mask reshapes to fit a wearer attuned to it. While you are wearing the mask and attuned to it, you can access the following properties.\n\nDamage Absorption\n\nYou have resistance against lightning damage. If you already have resistance to lightning damage from another source, you instead have immunity to lightning damage. If you already have immunity to lightning damage from another source, whenever you are subjected to lightning damage, you take none of that damage and regain a number of hit points equal to half the damage dealt of that type.\n\nDraconic Majesty\n\nWhile you are wearing no armor, you can add your Charisma bonus to your Armor Class.\n\nDragon Breath\n\nIf you have a breath weapon that requires rest to recharge, it gains a recharge of 6.\n\nDragon Sight\n\nYou gain darkvision out to 60 feet, or to an additional 60 feet if you already have that sense. Once per day, you can gain blindsight out to 30 feet for 5 minutes.\n\nDragon Tongue\n\nYou can speak and understand Draconic. You also have advantage on any Charisma check you make against Blue Dragons.\n\nLegendary Resistance\n\n(1/Day) If you fail a saving throw, you can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLingering Shock\n\nIf you deal lightning damage to a creature, it can't take reactions until its next turn."},
  ["magicitem.blue-dragon-scale-mail.dmg2014"]={title="Blue Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nDragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them to humanoids. Other times, hunters carefully skin and preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, dragon scale mail is highly valued. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to lightning damage.\n\nAdditionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest blue dragon within 30 miles of you. This special action can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.blue-dragon-scale-mail.xdmg2024"]={title="Blue Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Dragon Scale Mail|XDMG"},
  ["creature.blue-dragon-wyrmling.mm2014"]={title="Blue Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 91\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, fly: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales lightning in a 30-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.blue-dragon-wyrmling.xmm2024"]={title="Blue Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, fly: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Lightning damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 12, each creature in a 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 21 (6d6) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.blue-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Blue Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 533 (26d20 + 260)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 14 | CON 30 | INT 21 | WIS 20 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChromatic Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 425 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use the options in the \"Mythic Actions\" section for 1 hour. Award a party an additional 105,000 XP (210,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Chromatic Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 20) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled this way at a time.\n\nTail\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales a blast of energy in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 78 (12d12) lightning damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw or Tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm beats its wings. Each creature within 30 feet of it must succeed on a 26 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The greatwyrm can then fly up to half its flying speed.\n\nArcane Spear (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm creates four spears of magical force. Each spear hits a creature of the greatwyrm's choice it can see within 120 feet of it, dealing 12 (1d8 + 8) force damage to its target, then disappears.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nBite\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack.\n\nChromatic Flare (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm flares with elemental energy. Each creature in a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on the greatwyrm must succeed on a 26 Dexterity saving throw or take 22 (5d8) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.blue-guard-drake.vgm2014"]={title="Blue Guard Drake",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (7d8 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak it\n\nResistencias: lightning\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe drake attacks twice, once with its bite and once with its tail.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.blue-quartz.dmg2014"]={title="Blue Quartz",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent pale blue gemstone."},
  ["item.blue-quartz.xdmg2024"]={title="Blue Quartz",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA pale blue gemstone."},
  ["item.blue-sapphire.dmg2014"]={title="Blue Sapphire",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent blue-white to medium blue gemstone."},
  ["item.blue-sapphire.xdmg2024"]={title="Blue Sapphire",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA medium blue gemstone."},
  ["creature.blue-slaad.mm2014"]={title="Blue Slaad",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 123 (13d10 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 7 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Slaad, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe slaad regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe slaad makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage. If the target is a humanoid, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be infected with a disease called chaos phage. While infected, the target can't regain hit points, and its hit point maximum is reduced by 10 (3d6) every 24 hours. If the disease reduces the target's hit point maximum to 0, the target instantly transforms into a red slaad or, if it has the ability to cast spells of 3rd level or higher, a green slaad. Only a wish spell can reverse the transformation."},
  ["creature.blue-slaad.xmm2024"]={title="Blue Slaad",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 285\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 133 (14d10 + 56)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 7 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Slaad; telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe slaad regains 10 XPHB at the start of each of its turns if it has at least 1 XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe slaad makes three Mutating Claw attacks.\n\nMutating Claw\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h12 (2d6 + 5) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage. If the target is a Humanoid not cursed by a slaad, it is subjected to the following effect. con 15. actSaveFail The target is cursed. The cursed target can't regain XPHB, and its XPHB maximum decreases by 10 (3d6) after every 24 hours and doesn't return to normal after finishing a XPHB. If the curse reduces the target's XPHB maximum to 0, the curse ends, and instead of dying, the target instantly transforms into a XMM or, if it can cast spells of level 3 or higher, a XMM. Only a XPHB spell can reverse this transformation."},
  ["item.blue-spinel.dmg2014"]={title="Blue Spinel",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent deep blue gemstone."},
  ["item.blue-spinel.xdmg2024"]={title="Blue Spinel",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA deep blue gemstone."},
  ["spell.blur.phb2014"]={title="Blur",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nYour body becomes blurred, shifting and wavering to all who can see you. For the duration, any creature has disadvantage on attack rolls against you. An attacker is immune to this effect if it doesn't rely on sight, as with blindsight, or can see through illusions, as with truesight."},
  ["spell.blur.xphb2024"]={title="Blur",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 248\n\nYour body becomes blurred. For the duration, any creature has XPHB on attack rolls against you. An attacker is immune to this effect if it perceives you with XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["creature.blurg.oota2014"]={title="Blurg",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 18"},
  ["creature.bluto-krogarov.cos2014"]={title="Bluto Krogarov",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.boar.mm2014"]={title="Boar",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 319\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 2 | WIS 9 | CHA 5\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the boar moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a tusk attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 3 (1d6) slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 11 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nRelentless (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the boar takes 7 damage or less that would reduce it to 0 hit points, it is reduced to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTusk\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.boar.xmm2024"]={title="Boar",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 350\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 9 | CHA 5\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBloodied Fury\n\nWhile XPHB, the boar has XPHB on attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature and the boar moved 20+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 3 (1d6) Piercing damage and has the XPHB condition."},
  ["magicitem.bob.toa2014"]={title="Bob",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis +1 battleaxe floats on water and other liquids, and grants its bearer advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made to swim."},
  ["magicitem.bobbing-lily-pad.wbtw2014"]={title="Bobbing Lily Pad",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis magic vehicle is a 10-foot-diameter leaf that floats on water. It has tendrils that propel it across land and across the water's surface (but not underwater), as well as through the air. It has a walking, flying, and swimming speed of 20 feet, and it can hover. It moves according to your spoken directions while you are riding it.\n\nThe lily pad can transport up to 300 pounds without hindrance. It can carry up to twice this weight, but it moves at half speed if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["deity.boccob.phb2014"]={title="Boccob",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["deity.boccob.xdmg2024"]={title="Boccob",subtitle="Divindade - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 148"},
  ["creature.bodak.mpmm2014"]={title="Bodak",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Gaze\n\nWhen a creature that can see the bodak's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of the bodak, the bodak can force it to make a 13 Constitution saving throw if the bodak isn't incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is reduced to 0 hit points unless it is immune to the frightened condition. Otherwise, a creature takes 16 (3d10) psychic damage on a failed save.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it has disadvantage on attack rolls against the bodak until the start of its next turn. If the creature looks at the bodak in the meantime, that creature must immediately make the saving throw.\n\nSunlight Hypersensitivity\n\nThe bodak takes 5 radiant damage when it starts its turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe bodak doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFist\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage.\n\nWithering Gaze\n\nOne creature that the bodak can see within 60 feet of it must make a 13 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAura of Annihilation\n\nThe bodak activates or deactivates this deathly aura. While active, the aura deals 5 necrotic damage to any creature that ends its turn within 30 feet of the bodak. Undead and Fiends ignore this effect."},
  ["creature.bodak.vgm2014"]={title="Bodak",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, necrotic\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Annihilation\n\nThe bodak can activate or deactivate this feature as a bonus action. While active, the aura deals 5 necrotic damage to any creature that ends its turn within 30 feet of the bodak. Undead and fiends ignore this effect.\n\nDeath Gaze\n\nWhen a creature that can see the bodak's eyes starts its turn within 30 feet of the bodak, the bodak can force it to make a 13 Constitution saving throw if the bodak isn't incapacitated and can see the creature. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the creature is reduced to 0 hit points, unless it is immune to the frightened condition. Otherwise, a creature takes 16 (3d10) psychic damage on a failed save.\n\nUnless surprised, a creature can avert its eyes to avoid the saving throw at the start of its turn. If the creature does so, it has disadvantage on attack rolls against the bodak until the start of its next turn. If the creature looks at the bodak in the meantime, it must immediately make the saving throw.\n\nSunlight Hypersensitivity\n\nThe bodak takes 5 radiant damage when it starts its turn in sunlight. While in sunlight, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFist\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 9 (2d8) necrotic damage.\n\nWithering Gaze\n\nOne creature that the bodak can see within 60 feet of it must make a 13 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.bodhi-irenicus.mabjov2014"]={title="Bodhi Irenicus",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 77\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 212 (25d8 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 20 | CON 18 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Bodhi fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nRegeneration\n\nBodhi regains 20 hit points at the start of her turn if she has at least 1 hit point and isn't in sunlight. If she takes radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of her next turn.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf Bodhi is destroyed, her body immediately appears in her resting place. She is paralyzed until she regains at least 1 hit point. After spending 24 hours in her resting place with 0 hit points, she regains 1 hit point. While paralyzed in this manner, if a creature within 60 feet says her name 9 times, Bodhi is permanently destroyed.\n\nSneak Attack (1/Turn)\n\nBodhi deals an extra 28 (8d6) damage when she hits a target with a weapon attack and has advantage on the attack roll, or when the target is within 5 feet of an ally of Bodhi that isn't incapacitated and Bodhi doesn't have disadvantage on the attack roll.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nBodhi can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSummoned By Name (1/Day)\n\nIf a creature says Bodhi Irenicus's full name 9 times in a row, Bodhi hears her name and becomes aware of the creature. Bodhi knows the exact location and name of the creature that spoke her name. She can then choose, as a free action, to teleport to a location adjacent to the creature. She must choose to do this within 1 minute of hearing her name. This power works even if the creature is on a different plane of existence. 1 minute after teleporting, Bodhi teleports back to where she was located when she heard her name spoken. This occurs even if Bodhi is unwilling and even if she is in an antimagic effect.\n\nVampire Weaknesses\n\nBodhi Irenicus has the following flaws:\n\n• Elvish Song\n\n• Stake to the Heart\n\n• Sunlight Hypersensitivity\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Vampire Form Only)\n\nBodhi makes three Unarmed Strike attacks, one of which can be a Bite attack instead.\n\nUnarmed Strike (Vampire Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h9 (1d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage. Instead of dealing damage, Bodhi can grapple a Medium-sized or smaller target (escape 18).\n\nBite (Panther or Vampire Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h8 (1d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) necrotic damage. The target's hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the necrotic damage taken, and Bodhi regains hit points equal to that amount. The reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if this effect reduces its hit point maximum to 0. A Humanoid slain in this way and then buried in the ground rises the following night as a vampire spawn under Bodhi's control.\n\nChange Shape\n\nIf Bodhi isn't in sunlight, she can polymorph into a Medium panther or back into her true form. While in panther form, Bodhi Irenicus can't speak, her walking speed is 40 feet, and she has a climb speed of 30 feet. Her statistics, other than her size and speed, are unchanged. Anything she is wearing transforms with her, but nothing she is carrying does. She reverts to her true form if she dies.\n\nCharm\n\nBodhi targets one Humanoid she can see within 30 feet of her. If the target can see Bodhi, the target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by Bodhi. The charmed target regards Bodhi as a trusted friend to be heeded and protected. Although the target isn't under Bodhi's control, it takes Bodhi's requests or actions in the most favorable way it can. Each time Bodhi or her allies do anything harmful to the target, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. Otherwise, the effect lasts 24 hours or until Bodhi is destroyed, is on a different plane of existence than the target, or takes a bonus action to end the effect.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nMove\n\nBodhi moves up to her speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nBodhi makes one Unarmed Strike.\n\nBite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nBodhi makes one Bite attack."},
  ["feature.body-and-mind.xphb2024.monk.base.20"]={title="Body and Mind",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 103\n\nYou have developed your body and mind to new heights. Your Dexterity and Wisdom scores increase by 4, to a maximum of 25."},
  ["feature.body-of-the-astral-self.tce2014.monk.astral-self.11"]={title="Body of the Astral Self",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n11th-level Way of the Astral Self feature\n\nWhen you have both your astral arms and visage summoned, you can cause the body of your astral self to appear (no action required). This spectral body covers your physical form like a suit of armor, connecting with the arms and visage. You determine its appearance.\n\nWhile the spectral body is present, you gain the following benefits.\n\nDeflect Energy\n\nWhen you take acid, cold, fire, force, lightning, or thunder damage, you can use your reaction to deflect it. When you do so, the damage you take is reduced by 1d10 + your Wisdom modifier (minimum reduction of 1).\n\nEmpowered Arms\n\nOnce on each of your turns when you hit a target with the Arms of the Astral Self, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to your Martial Arts die."},
  ["creature.bodytaker-plant.rhw2014"]={title="Bodytaker Plant",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10, swim: 10\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 20 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 18\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft.\n\nVulnerabilidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, exhaustion, frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPodling Link\n\nThe plant can see through and communicate telepathically with any of its podlings within 10 miles of it. When the plant dies, its podlings also die.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf the plant dies, it revives with all its XPHB in 1d10 days. This trait doesn't function if the plant is reduced to 0 XPHB by Poison damage or its remains are sprinkled with salt.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe plant makes three Vine attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Entrapping Pod.\n\nVine\n\nm 7, reach 20 ft. h17 (3d8 + 4) Slashing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from one of four vines.\n\nEntrapping Pod\n\nstr 15, one Large or smaller creature the plant is grappling. actSaveFail The target is pulled into the plant's space, is no longer XPHB, and is trapped in the plant's pod. While trapped, the target has the XPHB and XPHB conditions, and it has XPHB against attacks and other effects outside the pod. After 2d4 hours, the trapped target dies, and if it was a Humanoid, a Bodytaker Podling resembling it emerges from the pod.\n\nA creature outside the pod and within 5 feet of the plant can take an action to make a 14 Strength (XPHB) check. On a successful check, the target is removed from the pod, falls in a space within 5 feet of the plant, and has the XPHB condition. If the plant dies, the trapped target is no longer XPHB or XPHB and can escape from the pod using 5 feet of movement, exiting XPHB.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nTransfer Harm\n\nactTrigger An attack roll hits the plant while a podling is within 5 feet of the plant. actResponse The plant halves the damage it takes from that attack, and the podling takes the other half of the damage."},
  ["creature.bodytaker-plant.vrgr2014"]={title="Bodytaker Plant",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 92 (8d12 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10, swim: 10\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 20 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 18\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nVulnerabilidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPodling Link\n\nThe plant can see through and communicate telepathically with any of its podlings within 10 miles of it.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nWhen the plant dies, it returns to life in the place where it died 1d12 months later, unless the ground where it took root is sown with salt or soaked with poison.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe plant doesn't require sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe plant makes three Vine Lash attacks.\n\nVine Lash\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 15). Until the grapple ends, the target is restrained. The plant has four vines, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nEntrapping Pod\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature grappled by the plant. h22 (4d8 + 4) acid damage, and the target is pulled into the plant's space and enveloped by the pod, and the grapple ends. While enveloped, the target is restrained, and it has Cover against attacks and effects originating outside the pod. The enveloped target must also immediately succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be stunned by the plant's sapping enzymes until it is removed from the pod or the plant dies. The enveloped target doesn't require air and gains 1 level of exhaustion for each hour it spends in the pod. If the target dies while enveloped, it immediately emerges from the pod as a living podling, wearing or carrying all of the original creature's equipment.\n\nAs an action, a creature within 5 feet of the bodytaker plant that is outside the pod can open the pod and pull the target free with a successful 15 Strength check. If the plant dies, the target is no longer restrained and can escape from the pod by spending 10 feet of movement, exiting prone. The plant has one pod, which can envelop one creature at a time."},
  ["creature.bodytaker-podling.rhw2014"]={title="Bodytaker Podling",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 236\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / S/M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 26 (4d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech plus one other language\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSemblance of Life\n\nThe podling is a physical copy of a creature digested by a Bodytaker Plant. The podling has XPHB on Charisma (XPHB) checks made to pass as the digested creature. The podling melts into a slurry when it dies.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["species.boggart.lfl2014"]={title="Boggart",subtitle="Especie - LFL - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.boggle.mpmm2014"]={title="Boggle",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 65\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 18 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPummel\n\nmw 1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nOil Puddle\n\nThe boggle creates a puddle of nonflammable oil. The puddle is 1 inch deep and covers the ground in the boggle's space. The puddle is difficult terrain for all creatures except boggles and lasts for 1 hour. The oil has one of the following additional effects of the boggle's choice:\n\n• Slippery Oil Any non-boggle creature that enters the puddle or starts its turn there must succeed on a 11 Dexterity saving throw or fall prone.\n\n• Sticky Oil Any non-boggle creature that enters the puddle or starts its turn there must succeed on a 11 Strength saving throw or be restrained. On its turn, a creature can use an action to try to extricate itself, ending the effect and moving into the nearest unoccupied space of its choice with a successful 11 Strength check.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBoggle Oil\n\nThe boggle excretes nonflammable oil from its pores, giving itself one of the following benefits of its choice until it uses this bonus action again:\n\n• Slippery Oil The boggle has advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks made to escape bonds and end grapples, and it can move through openings large enough for a Tiny creature without squeezing.\n\n• Sticky Oil The boggle has advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made to grapple and any ability check made to maintain a hold on another creature, a surface, or an object. The boggle can also climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nDimensional Rift\n\nThe boggle creates an invisible and immobile rift within an opening or frame it can see within 5 feet of it, provided that the space is no bigger than 10 feet on any side. The dimensional rift bridges the distance between that space and a point within 30 feet of it that the boggle can see or specify by distance and direction (such as \"30 feet straight up\"). While next to the rift, the boggle can see through it and is considered to be next to the destination as well, and anything the boggle puts through the rift (including a portion of its body) emerges at the destination. Only the boggle can use the rift, and it lasts until the end of the boggle's next turn."},
  ["creature.boggle.vgm2014"]={title="Boggle",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 18 | CON 13 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBoggle Oil\n\nThe boggle excretes nonflammable oil from its pores. The boggle chooses whether the oil is slippery or sticky and can change the oil on its skin from one consistency to another as a bonus action.\n\nSlippery Oil: While coated in slippery oil, the boggle gains advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks made to escape bonds, squeeze through narrow spaces, and end grapples.\n\nSticky Oil: While coated in sticky oil, the boggle gains advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made to grapple and any ability check made to maintain a hold on another creature, a surface, or an object. The boggle can also climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nDimensional Rift\n\nAs a bonus action, the boggle can create an invisible and immobile rift within an opening or frame it can see within 5 feet of it, provided that the space is no bigger than 10 feet on any side. The dimensional rift bridges the distance between that space and any point within 30 feet of it that the boggle can see or specify by distance and direction (such as \"30 feet straight up\"). While next to the rift, the boggle can see through it and is considered to be next to the destination as well, and anything the boggle puts through the rift (including a portion of its body) emerges at the destination. Only the boggle can use the rift, and it lasts until the end of the boggle's next turn.\n\nUncanny Smell\n\nThe boggle has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPummel\n\nmw 1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nOil Puddle\n\nThe boggle creates a puddle of oil that is either slippery or sticky (boggle's choice). The puddle is 1 inch deep and covers the ground in the boggle's space. The puddle is difficult terrain For all creatures except boggles and lasts for 1 hour.\n\nIf the oil is slippery, any creature that enters the puddle's area or starts its turn there must succeed on a 11 Dexterity saving throw or fall prone.\n\nIf the oil is sticky, any creature that enters the puddle's area or starts its turn there must succeed on a 11 Strength saving throw or be restrained. On its turn. a creature can use an action to try to extricate itself from the sticky puddle, ending the effect and moving into the nearest safe unoccupied space with a successful 11 Strength check."},
  ["object.boilerdrak.dsotdq2014"]={title="Boilerdrak",subtitle="Objeto - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\nThis wagon-sized device is designed to look roughly like a dragon. Before it can be used, the boilerdrak must be lit and aimed. It takes 1 action to light the weapon, 1 action to aim it, and 1 action to fire it. When you use your action to fire it, roll a d20. If you roll a 2 or higher, use the Flames action. If you roll a 1, use the Explosion action."},
  ["creature.bol-bara.egw2014"]={title="Bol'bara",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 261\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13/15\n\nPV: 40 (9d6 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDark One's Blessing\n\nWhen Bol'bara reduces a hostile creature to 0 hit points, she gains 6 temporary hit points.\n\nNimble Escape\n\nBol'bara can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of her turns.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBol'bara makes two melee attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nEldritch Blast (Cantrip)\n\nrs 4 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h7 (1d10 + 2) force damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nIncorporeal Dash\n\nBol'bara moves up to her speed. She can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. She takes 5 (1d10) force damage if she ends her turn inside an object.\n\nZone of Calamity (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nA 15-foot-radius sphere of magical confusion extends from a point Bol'bara can see within 60 feet of her and spreads around corners. Each creature that starts its turn in that area is treated as if targeted by the confusion spell (save 12). The sphere lasts as long as Bol'bara maintains concentration, up to 1 minute (as if concentration on a spell)."},
  ["deity.boldrei.erlw2014"]={title="Boldrei",subtitle="Divindade - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\nBoldrei is the Sovereign of Hall and Hearth. She guides and protects communities and families, inspiring people to work together for the common good."},
  ["deity.boldrei.phb2014"]={title="Boldrei",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["feature.bolstering-flames.frhof2014.sorcerer.spellfire.3"]={title="Bolstering Flames",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nYou or one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself gains XPHB equal to 1d4 plus your Charisma modifier."},
  ["feature.bolstering-magic.tce2014.barbarian.wild-magic.6"]={title="Bolstering Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\n6th-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nYou can harness your wild magic to bolster yourself or a companion. As an action, you can touch one creature (which can be yourself) and confer one of the following benefits of your choice to that creature:\n\n• For 10 minutes, the creature can roll a d3 whenever making an attack roll or an ability check and add the number rolled to the d20 roll.\n\n• Roll a d3. The creature regains one expended spell slot, the level of which equals the number rolled or lower (the creature's choice). Once a creature receives this benefit, that creature can't receive it again until after a long rest.\n\nYou can take this action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["item.bolt.xphb2024"]={title="Bolt",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nCrossbow bolts are used with a weapon that has the ammunition property to make a ranged attack. Each time you attack with the weapon, you expend one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). At the end of the battle, you can recover half your expended ammunition by taking a minute to search the battlefield.\n\nBolts are typically stored in a XPHB (bought separately)."},
  ["item.bolts-20.xphb2024"]={title="Bolts (20)",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nCrossbow bolts are used with a weapon that has the ammunition property to make a ranged attack. Each time you attack with the weapon, you expend one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). At the end of the battle, you can recover half your expended ammunition by taking a minute to search the battlefield.\n\nBolts are typically stored in a XPHB (bought separately)."},
  ["item.bomb.dmg2014"]={title="Bomb",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs an action, a character can light this bomb and throw it at a point up to 60 feet away. Each creature within 5 feet of that point must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or take 3d6 fire damage."},
  ["item.bomb.xdmg2024"]={title="Bomb",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs an action, you can light a Bomb and throw it at a point up to 60 feet away, where it explodes. Each creature in a 5-foot-radius XPHB centered on that point makes a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["item.bombard.aag2014"]={title="Bombard",subtitle="Item - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nRaridade: none\n\nBombards are built by giff. The major feature of each ship is an enormous cannon that fires massive cannon balls capable of blowing other ships to smithereens. (The cannon is included in the cost of the ship.) A bombard can carry up to fourteen giant cannon balls, each of which weighs 10 tons. These cannon balls make up most of the weight of the ship's cargo. A winch mounted on the aft deck is used to load the cannon balls on board.\n\nA bombard can float and sail on water, but it can't land safely on the ground (its keel would cause it to roll on its side)."},
  ["vehicle.bombard.aag2014"]={title="Bombard",subtitle="Veiculo - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 26"},
  ["feat.bomber.abh2014"]={title="Bomber",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nFar Lobber\n\nWhen you use the XPHB action to throw a vial or flask, you can target an object or creature you can see within 40 feet of yourself.\n\nLong Shots\n\nAttacking at long range doesn't impose XPHB on your attack rolls with XPHB weapons."},
  ["feature.bond-of-fang-and-scale.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.7"]={title="Bond of Fang and Scale",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n7th-level Drakewarden feature\n\nThe bond you share with your drake intensifies, protecting you and stoking the drake's fury. When you summon your drake, it grows wings on its back and gains a flying speed equal to its walking speed.\n\nIn addition, while your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:\n\n• Drake Mount The drake grows to Medium size. Reflecting your special bond, you can use the drake as a mount if your size is Medium or smaller. While you are riding your drake, it can't use the flying speed of this feature.\n\n• Magic Fang The drake's Bite attack deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence.\n\n• Resistance You gain resistance to the damage type chosen for the drake's Draconic Essence."},
  ["optionalfeature.bond-of-the-talisman.tce2014"]={title="Bond of the Talisman",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\nWhile someone else is wearing your talisman, you can use your action to teleport to the unoccupied space closest to them, provided the two of you are on the same plane of existence. The wearer of your talisman can do the same thing, using their action to teleport to you. The teleportation can be used a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and all expended uses are restored when you finish a long rest."},
  ["creature.bone-devil.mm2014"]={title="Bone Devil",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 71\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 142 (15d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the devil's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe devil has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe devil makes three attacks: two with its claws and one with its sting.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nSting\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 17 (5d6) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 1 minute. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.bone-devil.xmm2024"]={title="Bone Devil",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 52\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 161 (17d10 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft. (unimpeded by magical {@variantrule Darkness|XPHB})\n\nIdiomas: Infernal; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDiabolical Restoration\n\nIf the devil dies outside the Nine Hells, its body disappears in sulfurous smoke, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere in the Nine Hells.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe devil has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe devil makes two Claw attacks and one Infernal Sting attack.\n\nClaw\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\nInfernal Sting\n\nm 8, reach 10 ft. h15 (2d10 + 4) Piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the devil's next turn. While XPHB, the target can't regain XPHB."},
  ["creature.bone-knight.erlw2014"]={title="Bone Knight",subtitle="Criatura - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 316\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 84 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\nResistencias: necrotic, poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCommander of Bones\n\nAs a bonus action, the knight can target one skeleton or zombie it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must make a 14 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target must obey the knight's commands until the knight dies or until the knight releases it as a bonus action. The knight can command up to twelve undead at a time this way.\n\nMaster of the Pallid Banner\n\nWhile within 60 feet of the knight, any undead ally of the knight has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns undead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe knight attacks twice with one of its weapons.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.bone-naga.xmm2024"]={title="Bone Naga",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 53\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 65 (10d10 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 15\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe naga makes two Bite attacks. It can replace any attack with a use of Serpentine Gaze.\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 10 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Necrotic damage.\n\nSerpentine Gaze\n\nwis 13, one creature the naga can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 13 (3d6 + 3) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the naga's next turn."},
  ["creature.bone-naga-guardian.mm2014"]={title="Bone Naga (Guardian)",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 58 (9d10 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 15 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.bone-naga-spirit.mm2014"]={title="Bone Naga (Spirit)",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 58 (9d10 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 15 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage."},
  ["creature.bone-roc.veor2014"]={title="Bone Roc",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 133 (14d12 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15, fly: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 20 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 17 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bone roc makes one Beak attack and two Talons attacks.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nTalons\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.bone-whelk.bgdia2014"]={title="Bone Whelk",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 27 (5d10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15, climb: 15\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 5 | CON 11 | INT 6 | WIS 9 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAdhesive\n\nThe bone whelk can cause Medium or smaller objects to adhere to it. A Medium or smaller creature that touches the bone whelk is grappled by it (escape 10).\n\nDeath Scream\n\nWhen the bone whelk dies, it emits a blood-curdling shriek than can be heard out to a range of 120 feet. This shriek causes nonmagical, organic material within 10 feet of the bone whelk to rot. Each creature within 10 feet of the bone whelk when it dies takes 9 (2d8) necrotic damage.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe bone whelk can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d8) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.boneclaw.mpmm2014"]={title="Boneclaw",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 66\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 150 (20d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 13 | WIS 15 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one language spoken by its master\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRejuvenation\n\nWhile its master lives, a destroyed boneclaw gains a new body in 1d10 hours, with all its hit points. The new body appears within 1 mile of the boneclaw's master.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe boneclaw doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe boneclaw makes two Piercing Claw attacks.\n\nPiercing Claw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, the boneclaw can pull the target up to 10 feet toward itself, and the target is grappled (escape 14). The boneclaw has two claws. While a claw grapples a target, the claw can attack only that target.\n\nShadow Jump {@recharge 5}\n\nIf the boneclaw is in dim light or darkness, each creature of the boneclaw's choice within 15 feet of it must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or take 34 (5d12 + 2) necrotic damage.\n\nThe boneclaw then teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. It can bring one creature it's grappling, teleporting that creature to an unoccupied space it can see within 5 feet of its destination. The destination spaces of this teleportation must be in dim light or darkness.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the boneclaw takes the Hide action.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeadly Reach\n\nIn response to a creature entering a space within 15 feet of it, the boneclaw makes one Piercing Claw attack against that creature."},
  ["creature.boneclaw.mtf2014"]={title="Boneclaw",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 121\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 127 (17d10 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 13 | WIS 15 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus the main language of its master\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRejuvenation\n\nWhile its master lives, a destroyed boneclaw gains a new body in 1d10 hours, with all its hit points. The new body appears within 1 mile of the boneclaw's master.\n\nShadow Stealth\n\nWhile in dim light or darkness, the boneclaw can take the Hide action as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe boneclaw makes two claw attacks.\n\nPiercing Claw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, the boneclaw can pull the target up to 10 feet toward itself, and the target is grappled (escape 14). The boneclaw has two claws. While a claw grapples a target, the claw can attack only that target.\n\nShadow Jump\n\nIf the boneclaw is in dim light or darkness, each creature of the boneclaw's choice within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or take 34 (5d12 + 2) necrotic damage.\n\nThe boneclaw then magically teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. It can bring one creature it's grappling, teleporting that creature to an unoccupied space it can see within 5 feet of its destination. The destination spaces of this teleportation must be in dim light or darkness.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeadly Reach\n\nIn response to a visible enemy moving into its reach, the boneclaw makes one claw attack against that enemy. If the attack hits, the boneclaw can make a second claw attack against the target."},
  ["magicitem.bonecounter.sdw2014"]={title="Bonecounter",subtitle="Item Magico - SDW - 2014",body="Raridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis weapon is a magical +2 mace called Bonecounter. Whenever this weapon is used to destroy an undead creature, a single silver piece appears in the wielder's pocket."},
  ["creature.boneless.rhw2014"]={title="Boneless",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 238\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAbduct\n\nThe boneless needn't spend extra movement to move a creature it is grappling.\n\nCompression\n\nThe boneless can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h7 (2d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 12). Until the grapple ends, the target has the XPHB and XPHB conditions, is suffocating, and takes 7 (2d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the boneless's turns. The boneless can smother only one creature at a time. While grappling a target, the boneless can't take this action again.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nUnraveling Flesh (1/Day)\n\nwis 11, each creature within 30 feet that can see the boneless. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccessOrFail The boneless moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB."},
  ["creature.boneless.vrgr2014"]={title="Boneless",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 26 (4d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages it knew in life but can't speak\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCompression\n\nThe boneless can move through any opening at least 1 inch wide without squeezing. It can also squeeze to fit into a space that a Tiny creature could fit in.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe boneless doesn't require sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe boneless makes two Slam attacks. If both attacks hit a Large or smaller creature, the creature is grappled (escape 13), and the boneless can use Crushing Embrace.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nCrushing Embrace\n\nThe boneless wraps its body around a Large or smaller creature grappled by it. While the boneless is attached, the target is blinded and is unable to breathe. The target must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw at the start of each of the boneless' turns or take 5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage. If something moves the target, the boneless moves with it. The boneless can detach itself by spending 5 feet of its movement. A creature, including the target, can use its action to try to detach the boneless and force it to move into the nearest unoccupied space, doing so with a successful 13 Strength check. When the boneless dies, it detaches from any creature it is attached to."},
  ["spell.bones-of-the-earth.xge2024"]={title="Bones of the Earth",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 150\n\nYou cause up to six pillars of stone to burst from places on the ground that you can see within range. Each pillar is a cylinder that has a diameter of 5 feet and a height of up to 30 feet. The ground where a pillar appears must be wide enough for its diameter, and you can target the ground under a creature if that creature is Medium or smaller. Each pillar has AC 5 and 30 hit points. When reduced to 0 hit points, a pillar crumbles into rubble, which creates an area of difficult terrain with a 10-foot radius that lasts until the rubble is cleared. Each 5-foot-diameter portion of the area requires at least 1 minute to clear by hand.\n\nIf a pillar is created under a creature, that creature must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or be lifted by the pillar. A creature can choose to fail the save.\n\nIf a pillar is prevented from reaching its full height because of a ceiling or other obstacle, a creature on the pillar takes 6d6 bludgeoning damage and is restrained, pinched between the pillar and the obstacle. The restrained creature can use an action to make a Strength or Dexterity check (the creature's choice) against the spell's save DC. On a success, the creature is no longer restrained and must either move off the pillar or fall off it."},
  ["creature.bonnie.wdh2014"]={title="Bonnie",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 4\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20"},
  ["feature.bonus-cantrip.phb2014.cleric.light.1"]={title="Bonus Cantrip",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\nWhen you choose this domain at 1st level, you gain the light cantrip if you don't already know it. This cantrip doesn't count against the number of cleric cantrips you know."},
  ["feature.bonus-cantrip.phb2014.druid.land.2"]={title="Bonus Cantrip",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\nYou learn one additional druid cantrip of your choice. This cantrip doesn't count against the number of druid cantrips you know."},
  ["feature.bonus-cantrips.xge2024.warlock.celestial.1"]={title="Bonus Cantrips",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 54\n\nAt 1st level, you learn the sacred flame and light cantrips. They count as warlock cantrips for you, but they don't count against your number of cantrips known."},
  ["feature.bonus-disciplines.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.avatar.1"]={title="Bonus Disciplines",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\nAt 1st level, you learn two additional psionic disciplines of your choice. They must be chosen from among the psionics."},
  ["feature.bonus-disciplines.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.awakened.1"]={title="Bonus Disciplines",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\nAt 1st level, you learn two additional psionic disciplines of your choice. They must be chosen from among the psionics."},
  ["feature.bonus-disciplines.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.immortal.1"]={title="Bonus Disciplines",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\nAt 1st level, you learn two additional psionic disciplines of your choice. They must be chosen from among the psionics."},
