  ["feature.bonus-proficiency.xge2024.fighter.samurai.3"]={title="Bonus Proficiency",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.bonus-unarmed-strike.xphb2024.monk.base.1"]={title="Bonus Unarmed Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 101\n\nYou can make an XPHB as a XPHB."},
  ["item.book.phb2014"]={title="Book",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA book might contain poetry, historical accounts, information pertaining to a particular field of lore, diagrams and notes on gnomish contraptions, or just about anything else that can be represented using text or pictures. A book of spells is a phb."},
  ["item.book.xphb2024"]={title="Book",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Book contains fiction or nonfiction. If you consult an accurate nonfiction Book about its topic, you gain a +5 bonus to Intelligence (XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB) checks you make about that topic."},
  ["optionalfeature.book-of-ancient-secrets.phb2014"]={title="Book of Ancient Secrets",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou can now inscribe magical rituals in your Book of Shadows. Choose two spells. The spells needn't be from the same spell list. The spells appear in the book and don't count against the number of spells you know. With your Book of Shadows in hand, you can cast the chosen spells as rituals. You can't cast the spells except as rituals, unless you've learned them by some other means. You can also cast a warlock spell you know as a ritual if it has the ritual tag.\n\nOn your adventures, you can add other ritual spells to your Book of Shadows. When you find such a spell, you can add it to the book if the spell's level is equal to or less than half your warlock level (rounded up) and if you can spare the time to transcribe the spell. For each level of the spell, the transcription process takes 2 hours and costs 50 gp for the rare inks needed to inscribe it."},
  ["magicitem.book-of-exalted-deeds.dmg2014"]={title="Book of Exalted Deeds",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThe definitive treatise on all that is good in the multiverse, the fabled Book of Exalted Deeds figures prominently in many religions. Rather than being a scripture devoted to a particular faith, the book's various authors filled the pages with their own vision of true virtue, providing guidance for defeating evil.\n\nThe Book of Exalted Deeds rarely lingers in one place. As soon as the book is read, it vanishes to some other corner of the multiverse where its moral guidance can bring light to a darkened world. Although attempts have been made to copy the work, efforts to do so fail to capture its magical nature or translate the benefits it offers to those pure of heart and firm of purpose.\n\nA heavy clasp, wrought to look like angel wings, keeps the book's contents secure. Only a creature of good alignment that is attuned to the book can release the clasp that holds it shut. Once the book is opened, the attuned creature must spend 80 hours reading and studying the book to digest its contents and gain its benefits. Other creatures that peruse the book's open pages can read the text but glean no deeper meaning and reap no benefits. An evil creature that tries to read from the book takes 24d6 radiant damage. This damage ignores resistance and immunity, and can't be reduced or avoided by any means. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by this damage disappears in a blinding flash and is destroyed, leaving its possessions behind.\n\nBenefits granted by the Book of Exalted Deeds last only as long as you strive to do good. If you fail to perform at least one act of kindness or generosity within the span of 10 days, or if you willingly perform an evil act, you lose all the benefits granted by the book.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Book of Exalted Deeds has the following random properties:\n\n• 2 dmg\n\n• 2 dmg\n\nIncreased Wisdom\n\nAfter you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book, your Wisdom score increases by 2, to a maximum of 24. You can't gain this benefit from the book more than once.\n\nEnlightened Magic\n\nOnce you've read and studied the book, any spell slot you expend to cast a cleric or paladin spell counts as a spell slot of one level higher.\n\nHalo\n\nOnce you've read and studied the book, you gain a protective halo. This halo sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. You can dismiss or manifest the halo as a bonus action. While present, the halo gives you advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to interact with good creatures and Charisma (Intimidation) checks made to interact with evil creatures. In addition, fiends and undead within the halo's bright light make attack rolls against you with disadvantage.\n\nDestroying the Book\n\nIt is rumored that the Book of Exalted Deeds can't be destroyed as long as good exists in the multiverse. However, drowning the book in the River Styx removes all writing and imagery from its pages and renders the book powerless for 1d100 years."},
  ["magicitem.book-of-exalted-deeds.xdmg2024"]={title="Book of Exalted Deeds",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 237\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThe definitive treatise on all that is good in the multiverse, the Book of Exalted Deeds figures prominently in many religions. Rather than being a scripture devoted to a particular faith, the book's authors filled the pages with their own visions of true virtue, providing guidance for defeating evil.\n\nThe Book of Exalted Deeds rarely lingers in one place. As soon as the book is read, it vanishes to some other corner of the multiverse where its moral guidance can bring hope to an endangered world. Although attempts have been made to copy the work, efforts to do so fail to capture its magical nature or translate the benefits it offers to those pure of heart and firm of purpose.\n\nA heavy clasp, wrought to look like angel wings, keeps the book's contents secure. Only a creature that is attuned to the book can release the clasp that holds it shut. Once the book is opened, the attuned creature must spend 80 hours reading and studying the book to digest its contents and gain its benefits.\n\nOther creatures that peruse the book's open pages can read the text but glean no deeper meaning and reap no benefits. A Fiend, an Undead, or a servant of a god from the Lower Planes that tries to read from the book takes 24d6 Radiant damage. This damage ignores XPHB and XPHB, and it can't be reduced or avoided by any means. A creature reduced to 0 XPHB by this damage disappears in a flash and is destroyed, leaving its possessions behind. The book then vanishes, and the creature's XPHB to it ends.\n\nBenefits granted by the Book of Exalted Deeds last only as long as you strive to do good. If you fail to perform at least one act of kindness or generosity within the span of 10 days, or if you willingly perform an evil act, you lose all the benefits granted by the book.\n\nCelestial Calm\n\nWhile attuned to the book, you have XPHB to the XPHB and XPHB conditions and XPHB to Psychic damage. These benefits become permanent after you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book.\n\nDivine Wisdom\n\nAfter you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book, your Wisdom increases by 2, to a maximum of 24. You can't gain this benefit from the book more than once.\n\nEnlightened Magic\n\nAfter you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book, any spell slot you expend to cast a spell counts as a spell slot of one level higher.\n\nHalo\n\nAfter you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book, you gain a protective halo. This halo sheds XPHB in a 10-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 10 feet. You can dismiss or manifest the halo as a XPHB. While present, the halo gives you XPHB on Charisma (XPHB) checks. In addition, Fiends and Undead within the halo's XPHB make attack rolls against you with XPHB.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Book of Exalted Deeds has the following random properties:\n\n• 2 XDMG properties\n\n• 2 XDMG properties\n\nDestroying the Book\n\nThe Book of Exalted Deeds can't be destroyed. However, drowning the book in the River Styx removes all writing and imagery from its pages and renders the book powerless for 1d100 years."},
  ["magicitem.book-of-vile-darkness.dmg2014"]={title="Book of Vile Darkness",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThe contents of this foul manuscript of ineffable wickedness are the meat and drink of those in evil's thrall. No mortal was meant to know the secrets it contains, knowledge so horrid that to even glimpse the scrawled pages invites madness.\n\nMost believe the lich-god Vecna authored the Book of Vile Darkness. He recorded in its pages every diseased idea, every unhinged thought, and every example of blackest magic he came across or devised. Vecna covered every vile topic he could, making the book a gruesome catalog of all mortal wrongs.\n\nOther practitioners of evil have held the book and added their own input to its catalog of vile knowledge. Their additions are clear, for the writers of later works stitched whatever they were writing into the tome or, in some cases, made notations and additions to existing text. There are places where pages are missing, torn. or covered so completely with ink, blood, and scratches that the original text can't be divined.\n\nNature can't abide the book's presence. Ordinary plants wither in its presence, animals are unwilling to approach it, and the book gradually destroys whatever it touches. Even stone cracks and turns to powder if the book rests on it long enough.\n\nA creature attuned to the book must spend 80 hours reading and studying it to digest its contents and reap its benefits. The creature can then freely modify the book's contents, provided that those modifications advance evil and expand the lore already contained within.\n\nWhenever a non-evil creature attunes to the Book of Vile Darkness, that creature must make a 17 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, the creature's alignment changes to neutral evil.\n\nThe Book of Vile Darkness remains with you only as long as you strive to work evil in the world. If you fail to perform at least one evil act within the span of 10 days, or if you willingly perform a good act, the book disappears. If you die while attuned to the book, an entity of great evil claims your soul. You can't be restored to life by any means while your soul remains imprisoned.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Book of Vile Darkness has the following random properties:\n\n• 3 dmg\n\n• 1 dmg\n\n• 3 dmg\n\n• 2 dmg\n\nAdjusted Ability Scores\n\nAfter you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book, one ability score of your choice increases by 2, to a maximum of 24. Another ability score of your choice decreases by 2, to a minimum of 3. The book can't adjust your ability scores again.\n\nMark of Darkness\n\nAfter you spend the requisite amount of time reading and studying the book, you acquire a physical disfigurement as a hideous sign of your devotion to vile darkness. An evil rune might appear on your face, your eyes might become glossy black, or horns might sprout from your forehead. Or you might become wizened and hideous, lose all facial features, gain a forked tongue, or some other feature the DM chooses. The mark of darkness grants you advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to interact with evil creatures and Charisma (Intimidation) checks made to interact with non-evil creatures.\n\nCommand Evil\n\nWhile you are attuned to the book and holding it, you can use an action to cast the dominate monster spell on an evil target (save 18). You can't use this property again until the next dawn.\n\nDark Lore\n\nYou can reference the Book of Vile Darkness whenever you make an Intelligence check to recall information about some aspect of evil, such as lore about demons. When you do so, double your proficiency bonus on that check.\n\nDark Speech\n\nWhile you carry the Book of Vile Darkness and are attuned to it, you can use an action to recite words from its pages in a foul language known as Dark Speech. Each time you do so, you take 1d12 psychic damage, and each non-evil creature within 15 feet of you takes 3d6 psychic damage.\n\nDestroying the Book\n\nThe Book of Vile Darkness allows pages to be torn from it, but any evil lore contained on those pages finds its way back into the book eventually, usually when a new author adds pages to the tome.\n\nIf a solar tears the book in two, the book is destroyed for 1d100 years, after which it reforms in some dark corner of the multiverse.\n\nA creature attuned to the book for one hundred years can unearth a phrase hidden in the original text that, when translated to Celestial and spoken aloud, destroys both the speaker and the book in a blinding flash of radiance. However, as long as evil exists in the multiverse, the book reforms 1d10 × 100 years later.\n\nIf all evil in the multiverse is wiped out, the book turns to dust and is forever destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.book-of-vile-darkness.xdmg2024"]={title="Book of Vile Darkness",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 238\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThe contents of this foul manuscript are the meat and drink of the wicked. It contains knowledge so horrid that to even glimpse the scrawled pages invites doom.\n\nMost believe the lich-god XDMG authored the Book of Vile Darkness. He recorded in its pages every horrid idea, every corrupt thought, and every example of foul magic he came across or devised.\n\nOther practitioners of evil have added their own input to the book's catalog of vile knowledge. Their additions are clear, for the writers of later works stitched whatever they were writing into the tome or, in some cases, made notations and additions to existing text. There are places where pages are missing, torn, or covered so completely with ink, blood, and scratches that the original text can't be divined.\n\nXPHB can't abide the book's presence. Ordinary plants wither in its presence, common animals are unwilling to approach it, and the book gradually destroys whatever it touches. Even stone cracks and turns to powder if the book rests on it long enough.\n\nWhenever a creature that isn't a Fiend or an Undead attunes to the Book of Vile Darkness, that creature makes a 17 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is magically transformed into a XMM under the DM's control. Only a XPHB spell can reverse this vile transformation.\n\nA creature attuned to the book must spend 80 hours reading and studying it to digest its contents and use its Adjusted Ability Scores, Tireless Form, Spells, Vile Lore, and Vile Speech properties.\n\nThe Book of Vile Darkness remains with you only as long as you strive to work evil in the world. If you fail to perform at least one evil act within the span of 10 days, or if you willingly perform a good act, the book disappears, your XPHB to it ends immediately, and you lose all benefits granted by it. If you die while attuned to the book, an entity of great evil claims your soul. You can't be restored to life by any means while your soul remains imprisoned.\n\nAdjusted Ability Scores\n\nOne ability score of your choice increases by 2, to a maximum of 24. Another ability score of your choice decreases by 2, to a minimum of 3. The book can't adjust your ability scores again.\n\nTireless Form\n\nWhile the book is on your person, you have XPHB to the XPHB condition.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Book of Vile Darkness has the following random properties:\n\n• 3 XDMG properties\n\n• 1 XDMG property\n\n• 3 XDMG properties\n\n• 2 XDMG properties\n\nSpells\n\nWhile holding the book and holding it, you can cast the following spells (save 18) from it:\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\nOnce you use the book to cast a spell, you can't cast that spell again from it until the next dawn.\n\nVile Lore\n\nYou can reference the Book of Vile Darkness whenever you make an Intelligence check to recall information about some aspect of evil, such as lore about demons. When you do so, you have XPHB on that check.\n\nAt the DM's discretion, the book might reveal secrets no mortal should know, such as the true names of powerful Fiends, foul rites that allow one to transform into a death knight or lich, or long-lost spells crafted by beings so evil their names ought never to be spoken aloud.\n\nVile Speech\n\nWhile the book is on your person, you can take a XPHB action to recite words from its pages in a foul, dead language. Each time you do so, you take 1d12 Psychic damage, and each creature within 15 feet of you takes 3d6 Psychic damage unless the creature is a Fiend or an Undead.\n\nDestroying the Book\n\nThe Book of Vile Darkness allows pages to be torn from it, but any evil lore contained on those pages finds its way back into the book eventually, usually when a new author adds pages to the tome.\n\nIf a XMM tears the book in two, the book is destroyed for 1d100 years, after which it re-forms in some far corner of the multiverse.\n\nA creature attuned to the book for 100 years can unearth a phrase hidden in the original text that, when translated to Celestial and spoken aloud, destroys both the speaker and the book in a flash of radiance. However, as long as evil exists in the multiverse, the book re-forms 1d10 × 100 years later."},
  ["item.book-of-vile-darkness-variant.kftgv2014"]={title="Book of Vile Darkness (Variant)",subtitle="Item - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 207"},
  ["magicitem.bookmark.toa2014"]={title="Bookmark",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis +3 dagger belongs to ToA. While you have the dagger drawn, you can use a bonus action to activate one of the following properties:\n\n• Cause a blue gem set into the dagger's pommel to shed bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional 20 feet, or make the gem go dark.\n\n• Turn the dagger into a compass that, while resting on your palm, points north.\n\n• Cast dimension door from the dagger. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\n• Cast compulsion (save 15) from the dagger. The range of the spell increases to 90 feet but it targets only spiders that are beasts. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.boomerang-shield.bmt2014"]={title="Boomerang Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 66\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nYou can make a ranged weapon attack with this magic shield. It has a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet, and it uses your Strength or Dexterity for the attack roll (your choice). If you're proficient with shields, you are proficient with attacks made using this shield. On a hit, it deals 1d6 slashing damage. If you throw the shield, it reappears in your hand the instant after it hits or misses a target."},
  ["spell.booming-blade.tce2014"]={title="Booming Blade",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 106\n\nYou brandish the weapon used in the spell's casting and make a melee attack with it against one creature within 5 feet of you. On a hit, the target suffers the weapon attack's normal effects and then becomes sheathed in booming energy until the start of your next turn. If the target willingly moves 5 feet or more before then, the target takes 1d8 thunder damage, and the spell ends.\n\nThis spell's damage increases when you reach certain levels. At 5th level, the melee attack deals an extra 1d8 thunder damage to the target on a hit, and the damage the target takes for moving increases to 2d8. Both damage rolls increase by 1d8 at 11th level (2d8 and 3d8) and again at 17th level (3d8 and 4d8)."},
  ["magicitem.boon-companions-bands.au2014"]={title="Boon Companions' Bands",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nBoon Companions' Bands come in pairs and bear matching engravings. While wearing one of the bands, when you cast a spell or use a feature that forces other creatures in its area of effect to make a saving throw, you can protect the creature wearing the matching band if the creature is in the effect's area. That creature automatically succeeds on its saving throw against the effect, and it takes no damage if it would normally take half damage on a successful save.\n\nOnce this property is used by either band, the bands can't be used again until the next dawn. If one of the bands in a pair is destroyed, the other one crumbles to dust."},
  ["feat.boon-of-blazing-dawn.abh2014"]={title="Boon of Blazing Dawn",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nBeloved of the Sun\n\nYou have XPHB to Radiant damage.\n\nBlazing Strike\n\nWhen you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the damage can be Radiant or the weapon's normal damage type (your choice).\n\nBurst of Sunlight\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with an attack that deals Radiant damage, you can emit XPHB in a 30-foot radius from yourself and XPHB for an additional 30 feet until the start of your next turn. This light is sunlight."},
  ["feat.boon-of-bloodshed.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Bloodshed",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nKiller's Fortune\n\nWhen an enemy you can see is reduced to 0 XPHB, you gain XPHB on the next attack roll you make before the end of your next turn.\n\nPower from Pain\n\nOnce per turn, when you make an attack roll while XPHB, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to your XPHB. The extra damage's type is the same as the attack's type."},
  ["feat.boon-of-bountiful-health.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Bountiful Health",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAugmented Health\n\nWhen you gain XPHB, increase the number of XPHB you gain by 5.\n\nSuperior Recuperation\n\nWhen you spend one or more XPHB to regain XPHB, you can instead use the highest number possible for each die."},
  ["reward.boon-of-combat-prowess.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Combat Prowess",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nWhen you miss with a melee weapon attack, you can choose to hit instead. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-combat-prowess.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Combat Prowess",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nPeerless Aim\n\nWhen you miss with an attack roll, you can hit instead. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until the start of your next turn."},
  ["feat.boon-of-communication.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Communication",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCunning Speaker\n\nYou don't have XPHB on ability checks to influence XPHB creatures.\n\nGifted Interpreter\n\nYou understand the literal meaning of any language you hear or see signed, and you can understand the literal meaning of any written language you see.\n\nMental Communication\n\nYou gain telepathy with a range of 120 feet."},
  ["feat.boon-of-desperate-resilience.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Desperate Resilience",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nDefense of Body and Mind\n\nWhile you are XPHB, you have XPHB to every damage type except Force."},
  ["reward.boon-of-dimensional-travel.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Dimensional Travel",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nAs an action, you can cast the misty step spell, without using a spell slot or any components. Once you do so, you can't use this boon again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-dimensional-travel.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Dimensional Travel",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nBlink Steps\n\nImmediately after you take the XPHB action or the XPHB action, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see."},
  ["feat.boon-of-energy-resistance.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Energy Resistance",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEnergy Resistances\n\nYou gain XPHB to two of the following damage types of your choice: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic, Poison, Psychic, Radiant, or Thunder. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can change your choices.\n\nEnergy Redirection\n\nWhen you take damage of one of the types chosen for the Energy Resistances benefit, you can take a XPHB to direct damage of the same type toward another creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself that isn't behind XPHB. If you do so, that creature must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (8 plus your Constitution modifier and XPHB) or take damage equal to 2d12 plus your Constitution modifier."},
  ["feat.boon-of-erupting-spellpower.au2014"]={title="Boon of Erupting Spellpower",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nSpell Overload\n\nWhen you cast a spell that deals damage using a spell slot, you can cause its magical energy to surge. You can treat any 1 or 2 on a damage die rolled for the spell as a 3, and creatures that took damage from the spell also have the XPHB condition. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you roll XPHB or finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["feat.boon-of-exquisite-radiance.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Exquisite Radiance",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEternal Rest\n\nCreatures you reduce to 0 XPHB can't become Undead.\n\nPowerful Radiance\n\nWhen you make a damage roll that deals Radiant damage, you can instead use the highest number possible for each damage die. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["reward.boon-of-fate.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Fate",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nWhen another creature that you can see within 60 feet of you makes an ability check, an attack roll, or a saving throw, you can roll a d10 and apply the result as a bonus or penalty to the roll. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-fate.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Fate",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImprove Fate\n\nWhen you or another creature within 60 feet of you succeeds on or fails a XPHB, you can roll 2d4 and apply the total rolled as a bonus or penalty to the d20 roll. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you roll XPHB or finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["feat.boon-of-fluid-forms.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Fluid Forms",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nShapechanger\n\nYou can take a XPHB action to shape-shift into a Beast, Humanoid, or Monstrosity with a XPHB no higher than 10. When you shape-shift, you gain a number of XPHB equal to the XPHB of the form. The shape-shifting effect lasts for 1 hour, and it ends early if you have no XPHB left or if you take a XPHB action to return to your true form.\n\nYour game statistics are replaced by the stat block of the chosen form, but you retain your creature type; alignment; personality; Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; XPHB; XPHB; proficiencies; and ability to communicate. If you have the Spellcasting or Pact Magic feature, you retain it too. Upon shape-shifting, you determine whether your equipment drops to the ground or changes in size and shape to fit the new form while you're in it.\n\nOnce you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nHardy Transformation\n\nWhen you gain XPHB when you shape-shift, increase that number of XPHB by 20."},
  ["reward.boon-of-fortitude.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Fortitude",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYour hit point maximum increases by 40."},
  ["feat.boon-of-fortitude.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Fortitude",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nFortified Health\n\nYour XPHB maximum increases by 40. In addition, whenever you regain XPHB, you can regain additional XPHB equal to your Constitution modifier. Once you've regained these additional XPHB, you can't do so again until the start of your next turn."},
  ["feat.boon-of-fortune-s-favor.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Fortune's Favor",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nSaving Throw Reroll\n\nWhen you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it and must use the new roll. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until the start of your next turn."},
  ["reward.boon-of-high-magic.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of High Magic",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou gain one 9th-level spell slot, provided that you already have one."},
  ["reward.boon-of-immortality.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Immortality",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou stop aging. You are immune to any effect that would age you, and you can't die from old age."},
  ["reward.boon-of-invincibility.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Invincibility",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nWhen you take damage from any source, you can reduce that damage to 0. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["reward.boon-of-irresistible-offense.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Irresistible Offense",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou can bypass the damage resistances of any creature."},
  ["feat.boon-of-irresistible-offense.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Irresistible Offense",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nOvercome Defenses\n\nThe Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage you deal always ignores XPHB.\n\nOverwhelming Strike\n\nWhen you roll a 20 on the d20 for an attack roll, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to the ability score increased by this feat. The extra damage's type is the same as the attack's type."},
  ["feat.boon-of-looming-shadows.abh2014"]={title="Boon of Looming Shadows",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nShadowy Stretch\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action, your reach for your Melee weapon attacks increases by 10 feet until the end of your turn.\n\nDancing Silhouette\n\nYou can take the XPHB action as a XPHB."},
  ["reward.boon-of-luck.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Luck",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou can add a d10 roll to any ability check, attack roll, or saving throw you make. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["reward.boon-of-magic-resistance.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Magic Resistance",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects."},
  ["feat.boon-of-magic-school-mastery.au2014"]={title="Boon of Magic School Mastery",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMastered School\n\nChoose one of the eight schools of magic: Abjuration, Conjuration, Divination, Enchantment, Evocation, Illusion, Necromancy, or Transmutation. Your choice grants you the following features:\n\n• Rote Casting Choose a level 1 spell from the chosen school that appears on your class's spell list. You always have that spell prepared and can cast it without a spell slot or spell components.\n\n• Signature Arcanum Choose a level 7 or lower spell from the chosen school. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can also cast these prepared spells using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level.\n\nRepeatable\n\nYou can take this feat more than once, but you must choose a different school of magic each time."},
  ["feat.boon-of-misty-escape.abh2014"]={title="Boon of Misty Escape",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nGaseous Form\n\nIf you drop to 0 XPHB but aren't killed outright, you can instead drop to 1 XPHB and cast XPHB without expending a spell slot (no action required). When you cast this spell this way, you can target only yourself, your XPHB is 20 feet, and you regain 10 XPHB at the start of each of your turns for the spell's duration. The spell's spellcasting ability is the ability increased by this feat.\n\nOnce you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["reward.boon-of-peerless-aim.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Peerless Aim",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou can give yourself a +20 bonus to a ranged attack roll you make. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["reward.boon-of-perfect-health.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Perfect Health",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou are immune to all diseases and poisons, and you have advantage on Constitution saving throws."},
  ["reward.boon-of-planar-travel.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Planar Travel",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nWhen you gain this boon, choose a plane of existence other than the Material Plane. You can now use an action to cast the plane shift spell (no spell slot or components required), targeting yourself only, and travel to the chosen plane, or from that plane back to the Material Plane. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-poison-mastery.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Poison Mastery",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAntitoxic\n\nYou have XPHB to Poison damage and the XPHB condition.\n\nPerfect Poisoner\n\nOnce per turn, when you roll dice to determine Poison damage a creature takes from your attack, spell, or feature, you can instead use the highest number possible for each die."},
  ["reward.boon-of-quick-casting.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Quick Casting",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nChoose one of your spells of 1st through 3rd level that has a casting time of 1 action. That spell's casting time is now 1 bonus action for you."},
  ["reward.boon-of-recovery.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Recovery",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou can use a bonus action to regain a number of hit points equal to half your hit point maximum. Once you use this boon, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-recovery.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Recovery",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nLast Stand\n\nWhen you would be reduced to 0 XPHB, you can drop to 1 XPHB instead and regain a number of XPHB equal to half your XPHB maximum. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nRecover Vitality\n\nYou have a pool of ten d10s. As a XPHB, you can expend dice from the pool, roll those dice, and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll's total. You regain all the expended dice when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["reward.boon-of-resilience.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Resilience",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou have resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage from nonmagical weapons."},
  ["feat.boon-of-revelry.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Revelry",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nInspire Dance\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level.\n\nWhen you cast the spell, it requires no spell components, and taking damage doesn't break your XPHB on it.\n\nSing Out\n\nWhile a creature that failed its saving throw against your XPHB has the XPHB condition from that spell, it can't cast spells with Verbal components, and it sings delightful nonsense if it can sing."},
  ["feat.boon-of-siberys.efa2014"]={title="Boon of Siberys",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 45\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAberrant Magic\n\nChoose a level 8 or lower spell from the spells or a spell from the Siberys Dragonmark Spells table (the table includes dragonmark suggestions if you'd like to associate a spell with one of the marks). You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot or spell components, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB or XPHB. You can also cast this spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you gain this feat).\n\nSpell | Suggested Dragonmark\n\nXPHB | Handling\n\nXPHB | Storm\n\nXPHB | Making\n\nXPHB | Hospitality\n\nXPHB | Warding\n\nXPHB | Sentinel\n\nXPHB | Passage\n\nXPHB | Shadow\n\nXPHB | Healing\n\nXPHB | Scribing\n\nXPHB | Finding\n\nXPHB | Detection"},
  ["feat.boon-of-skill.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Skill",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAll-Around Adept\n\nYou gain proficiency in all skills.\n\nExpertise\n\nChoose one skill in which you lack XPHB. You gain XPHB in that skill."},
  ["reward.boon-of-skill-proficiency.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Skill Proficiency",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou gain proficiency in all skills."},
  ["reward.boon-of-speed.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Speed",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYour walking speed increases by 30 feet. In addition, you can use a bonus action to take the Dash or Disengage action. Once you do so, you can't do so again until you finish a short rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-speed.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Speed",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEscape Artist\n\nAs a XPHB, you can take the XPHB action, which also ends the XPHB condition on you.\n\nQuickness\n\nYour XPHB increases by 30 feet."},
  ["reward.boon-of-spell-mastery.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Spell Mastery",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nChoose one 1st-level sorcerer, warlock, or wizard spell that you can cast. You can now cast that spell at its lowest level without expending a spell slot."},
  ["reward.boon-of-spell-recall.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Spell Recall",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou can cast any spell you know or have prepared without expending a spell slot. Once you do so, you can't use this boon again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feat.boon-of-spell-recall.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Spell Recall",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nFree Casting\n\nWhenever you cast a spell with a level 1-4 spell slot, roll 1d4. If the number you roll is the same as the slot's level, the slot isn't expended."},
  ["feat.boon-of-terror.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of Terror",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nFearless\n\nYou have XPHB to the XPHB condition.\n\nFlee, Fools!\n\nWhen a creature with the XPHB condition starts its turn within 60 feet of you, you can take a XPHB to stoke its terror, provided you can see the creature and it isn't behind XPHB. If you do so, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 plus your Charisma modifier and your XPHB) or spend its turn moving away from you by the fastest available means. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB.\n\nIntimidating\n\nYou gain XPHB in the XPHB skill if you don't already have it. You also gain XPHB in XPHB."},
  ["feat.boon-of-the-bright-sun.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of the Bright Sun",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nDaylight Presence\n\nAs a XPHB, you radiate a 30-foot XPHB of XPHB that is sunlight. If any of the XPHB's area overlaps with an area of XPHB created by a spell, that spell is dispelled. The XPHB lasts until you dismiss it (no action required), die, or have the XPHB condition.\n\nFortifying Light\n\nWhen your Daylight Presence is active, at the start of each of your turns, you and allies you can see in your Daylight Presence gain 10 XPHB."},
  ["reward.boon-of-the-fire-soul.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of the Fire Soul",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou have immunity to fire damage. You can also cast burning hands (save 15) at will, without using a spell slot or any components."},
  ["feat.boon-of-the-furious-storm.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of the Furious Storm",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEye of the Storm\n\nYou have XPHB to Lightning and Thunder damage. While you are XPHB, you have XPHB to Lightning and Thunder damage.\n\nStorm's Strength\n\nCreatures have XPHB on saving throws against your spells that deal Lightning or Thunder damage."},
  ["feat.boon-of-the-iron-mind.au2014"]={title="Boon of the Iron Mind",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nUnshakable Focus\n\nWhen you are maintaining XPHB on an effect, you lose XPHB only if you cast a spell or activate another effect that requires XPHB, if you have the XPHB or XPHB condition, or if you die."},
  ["reward.boon-of-the-night-spirit.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of the Night Spirit",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nWhile completely in an area of dim light or darkness, you can become invisible as an action. You remain invisible until you take an action or a reaction."},
  ["feat.boon-of-the-night-spirit.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of the Night Spirit",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMerge with Shadows\n\nWhile within XPHB or XPHB, you can give yourself the XPHB condition as a XPHB. The condition ends on you immediately after you take an action, a XPHB, or a XPHB.\n\nShadowy Form\n\nWhile within XPHB or XPHB, you have XPHB to all damage except Psychic and Radiant."},
  ["feat.boon-of-the-soul-drinker.frhof2014"]={title="Boon of the Soul Drinker",subtitle="Feat - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nGrave Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB to Cold damage and Necrotic damage.\n\nSiphon Life\n\nWhen an enemy within 120 feet of you is reduced to 0 XPHB, you can take a XPHB to regain 50 XPHB. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["reward.boon-of-the-stormborn.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of the Stormborn",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou have immunity to lightning and thunder damage. You can also cast thunderwave (save 15) at will, without using a spell slot or any components."},
  ["reward.boon-of-the-unfettered.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of the Unfettered",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou have advantage on ability checks made to resist being grappled. In addition, you can use an action to automatically escape a grapple or free yourself of restraints of any kind."},
  ["reward.boon-of-truesight.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Truesight",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou have truesight out to a range of 60 feet."},
  ["feat.boon-of-truesight.xphb2024"]={title="Boon of Truesight",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 211\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTruesight\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet."},
  ["reward.boon-of-undetectability.dmg2014"]={title="Boon of Undetectability",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\nYou gain a +10 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) checks, and you can't be detected or targeted by spells magic, including scrying sensors."},
  ["creature.boontu-monkey.awm2014"]={title="Boontu Monkey",subtitle="Criatura - AWM - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 12\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe Boontu monkey has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the boontu monkey's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 (1d4 - 1) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-elvenkind.dmg2014"]={title="Boots of Elvenkind",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, your steps make no sound, regardless of the surface you are moving across. You also have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks that rely on moving silently."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-elvenkind.xdmg2024"]={title="Boots of Elvenkind",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, your steps make no sound, regardless of the surface you are moving across. You also have XPHB on Dexterity (XPHB) checks.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-false-tracks.xdmg2024"]={title="Boots of False Tracks",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhile wearing these boots, you can have them leave tracks like those of any kind of Humanoid of your size."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-false-tracks.xge2024"]={title="Boots of False Tracks",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 136\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nOnly humanoids can wear these boots. While wearing the boots, you can choose to have them leave tracks like those of another kind of humanoid of your size."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-levitation.dmg2014"]={title="Boots of Levitation",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, you can use an action to cast the levitate spell on yourself at will."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-levitation.xdmg2024"]={title="Boots of Levitation",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, you can cast XPHB on yourself."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-speed.dmg2014"]={title="Boots of Speed",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, you can use a bonus action and click the boots' heels together. If you do, the boots double your walking speed, and any creature that makes an opportunity attack against you has disadvantage on the attack roll. If you click your heels together again, you end the effect.\n\nWhen the boots' property has been used for a total of 10 minutes, the magic ceases to function until you finish a long rest."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-speed.xdmg2024"]={title="Boots of Speed",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, you can take a XPHB to click the boots' heels together. If you do, the boots double your XPHB, and any creature that makes an XPHB against you has XPHB on the attack roll. If you click your heels together again, you end the effect.\n\nWhen you've used the boots' property for a total of 10 minutes, the magic ceases to function for you until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-striding-and-springing.dmg2014"]={title="Boots of Striding and Springing",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, your walking speed becomes 30 feet, unless your walking speed is higher, and your speed isn't reduced if you are encumbered or wearing heavy armor. In addition, you can jump three times the normal distance, though you can't jump farther than your remaining movement would allow."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-striding-and-springing.xdmg2024"]={title="Boots of Striding and Springing",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these boots, your XPHB becomes 30 feet unless your XPHB is higher, and your XPHB isn't reduced by you carrying weight in excess of your carrying capacity or wearing Heavy Armor.\n\nOnce on each of your turns, you can jump up to 30 feet by spending only 10 feet of movement."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-the-winding-path.efa2014"]={title="Boots of the Winding Path",subtitle="Item Magico - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these boots, you can take a XPHB to teleport up to 15 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. You must have occupied that space at some point during the current turn.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["optionalfeature.boots-of-the-winding-path.tce2014"]={title="Boots of the Winding Path",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nWhile wearing these boots, a creature can teleport up to 15 feet as a bonus action to an unoccupied space the creature can see. The creature must have occupied that space at some point during the current turn."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-the-winterlands.dmg2014"]={title="Boots of the Winterlands",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese furred boots are snug and feel quite warm. While you wear them, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• You have resistance to cold damage.\n\n• You ignore difficult terrain created by ice or snow.\n\n• You can tolerate temperatures as low as -50 degrees Fahrenheit without any additional protection. If you wear heavy clothes, you can tolerate temperatures as low as -100 degrees Fahrenheit."},
  ["magicitem.boots-of-the-winterlands.xdmg2024"]={title="Boots of the Winterlands",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThese furred boots are snug and feel warm. While wearing them, you gain the following benefits.\n\nCold Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB to Cold damage and can tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower without any additional protection.\n\nWinter Strider\n\nYou ignore XPHB created by ice or snow."},
  ["creature.booyahg-booyahg-booyahg.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Booyahg Booyahg",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.booyahg-caster.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Caster",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["creature.booyahg-slave-of-the-archfey.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Slave of the Archfey",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.booyahg-slave-of-the-fiend.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Slave of the Fiend",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.booyahg-slave-of-the-great-old-one.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Slave of the Great Old One",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.booyahg-whip.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Whip",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.booyahg-wielder.vgm2014"]={title="Booyahg Wielder",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.borborygmos.ggr2014"]={title="Borborygmos",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 238\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / H\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 270 (20d12 + 140)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 11 | CON 24 | INT 8 | WIS 17 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nResistencias: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Borborygmos fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nPoor Depth Perception\n\nBorborygmos has disadvantage on any attack roll against a target more than 30 feet away.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nBorborygmos deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBorborygmos can use his Frightful Presence. He also makes two attacks: one with his maul and one with his stomp.\n\nMaul\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h28 (6d6 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 21 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 13 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of Borborygmos's choice that is within 60 feet of him and can see or hear him must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of him for 1 minute. The frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to Borborygmos's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nBorborygmos makes a weapon attack.\n\nBellow (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nBorborygmos yells menacingly at one creature he can see within 60 feet of him. That creature must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of him for 1 minute. If the creature is already frightened, it becomes stunned instead. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to Borborygmos's Bellow for the next 24 hours.\n\nWide Berth (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nBorborygmos moves up to half his speed and can move through the space of any creature smaller than Huge. The first time Borborygmos enters a creature's space during this move, the creature must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw. If the saving throw succeeds, the creature is pushed 5 feet away from Borborygmos. If the saving throw fails, that creature is knocked prone, and Borborygmos can make a stomp attack against it."},
  ["item.borderlands-tabard.hotb2014"]={title="Borderlands Tabard",subtitle="Item - HotB - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhile you're wearing this tabard, NPCs in the Keep on the Borderlands are initially XPHB toward you."},
  ["creature.bore-worm.wdmm2014"]={title="Bore Worm",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / G\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 247 (15d20 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 7 | CON 22 | INT 1 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe worm can burrow through solid rock at half its burrow speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe worm regains 10 hit points at the start of each of its turns if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe worm makes two attacks: one with its grinding jaws and one with its stinger.\n\nGrinding Jaws\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d8 + 9) slashing damage.\n\nTail Stinger\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h19 (3d6 + 9) piercing damage, and the target must make a 19 Constitution saving throw, taking 42 (12d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.borivik-windheim.mabjov2014"]={title="Borivik Windheim",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 195 (30d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 20 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBolts of Undead Slaying\n\nBorivik has a half-dozen bolts of undead slaying. If he strikes an Undead creature with one of these magic bolts, it must make a 17 Constitution saving throw, taking an extra 33 (6d10) piercing damage on a failed save, or half as much extra damage on a successful one.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBorivik makes two Shortsword attacks or two Heavy Crossbow attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 9 to hit, ranged 100/400 ft., one target. h10 (1d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCrossbow Expert\n\nBorivik adds 1d10 to his next attack or damage roll with his Heavy Crossbow attack.\n\nNimble Escape\n\nBorivik can take the Disengage or Hide action.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nEnduring Response\n\nWhen Borivik takes acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage, he gains immunity to that damage type until the start of his next turn. Also, the first time he hits with a Shortsword attack on his next turn, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) of the triggering damage type."},
  ["feature.born-to-the-saddle.xge2024.fighter.cavalier.3"]={title="Born to the Saddle",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 30\n\nStarting at 3rd level, your mastery as a rider becomes apparent. You have advantage on saving throws made to avoid falling off your mount. If you fall off your mount and descend no more than 10 feet, you can land on your feet if you're not incapacitated.\n\nFinally, mounting or dismounting a creature costs you only 5 feet of movement, rather than half your speed."},
  ["creature.boromar-smuggler.efa2014"]={title="Boromar Smuggler",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 57\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 27 (6d6 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Halfling, Thieves' cant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHustle\n\nThe smuggler can move through the space of any creature that is of a larger size, but it can't stop there.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Poison damage.\n\nPistol\n\nr 4, range 30/90 ft. h7 (1d10 + 2) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.boromar-underboss.efa2014"]={title="Boromar Underboss",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 57\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 104 (19d6 + 38)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Halfling, Thieves' cant\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHustle\n\nThe underboss can move through the space of any creature that is of a larger size, but it can't stop there.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe underboss makes three attacks, using Poisoned Blade or Arcane Firearm in any combination.\n\nPoisoned Blade\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the underboss's next turn. If the target is already XPHB, it instead takes an extra 7 (2d6) Poison damage.\n\nArcane Firearm\n\nr 7, range 30/90 ft. h26 (4d10 + 4) Force damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nactTrigger The underboss is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The underboss halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["reward.boros-charm.ggr2014"]={title="Boros Charm",subtitle="Recompensa - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\nWhen you activate this charm, you can cast the crusader's mantle or haste spell. Alternatively, you can cast the guiding bolt spell, and if it hits, you regain a number of hit points equal to the damage it deals. The charm vanishes after you activate it."},
  ["magicitem.boros-guild-signet.ggr2014"]={title="Boros Guild Signet",subtitle="Item Magico - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis ring, adorned with the symbol of Boros, allows you to cast heroism. A guild signet is sometimes awarded to a guild member whose renown score in that guild is 5 or higher, as a reward for performing special services for the guild. Aside from its magical properties, the ring is also an indicator of Boros' recognition and favor.\n\nA signet has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge to cast the associated spell (save 13)."},
  ["magicitem.boros-keyrune.ggr2014"]={title="Boros Keyrune",subtitle="Item Magico - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 177\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nCarved from red sandstone with white granite elements to resemble a member of the Boros Legion, this keyrune can become a veteran (human) for up to 8 hours. In addition to fighting on your behalf, this veteran cheerfully offers tactical advice, which is usually sound. Anyone who talks with the transformed keyrune or examines it closely can easily recognize that it is an artificial human.\n\nWhen you use an action to speak the item's command word and place the keyrune on the ground in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you, the keyrune transforms into a veteran (human). If there isn't enough space for the veteran, the keyrune doesn't transform.\n\nThe creature is friendly to you, your companions, and other members of your guild (unless those guild members are hostile to you). It understands your languages and obeys your spoken commands. If you issue no commands, the creature takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger.\n\nAt the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its keyrune form. It reverts early if it drops to 0 hit points or if you use an action to speak the command word again while touching it. When the creature reverts to its keyrune form, it can't transform again until 36 hours have passed."},
  ["background.boros-legionnaire.ggr2014"]={title="Boros Legionnaire",subtitle="Background - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Legion Station\n\nYou have an established place in the hierarchy of the Boros Legion. You can requisition simple equipment for temporary use, and you can gain access to any Boros garrison in Ravnica, where you can rest in safety and receive the attention of medics. You are also paid a salary of 1 gp (a Boros-minted 1-zino coin) per week, which (combined with free lodging in your garrison) enables you to maintain a poor lifestyle between adventures.\n\nBoros Guild Spells\n\nPrerequisite: Spellcasting or Pact Magic class feature\n\nFor you, the spells on the Boros Guild Spells table are added to the spell list of your spellcasting class. (If you are a multiclass character with multiple spell lists, these spells are added to all of them.)\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\nCantrip | fire bolt, sacred flame\n\n1st | guiding bolt, heroism\n\n2nd | aid, scorching ray\n\n3rd | beacon of hope, blinding smite\n\n4th | death ward, wall of fire\n\n5th | flame strike\n\nYour magic often features dramatic bursts of flame or radiance. When you cast beneficial spells on your allies, they appear momentarily surrounded with halos of bright fire.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nThe Boros Legion is a zealous army, full of righteous energy tempered with military discipline. Its members share its leadership's devotion to the ideals of justice, or they find satisfaction in the more warfare-oriented aspects of the legion's work.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I approach every task with the same high degree of military precision.\n\n2 | I am always the first into the fray.\n\n3 | I bear any injury or indignity with stoic discipline.\n\n4 | My righteous wrath is easily inflamed by the slightest iniquity.\n\n5 | My honor is more important to me than my life.\n\n6 | Dangerous work is best accomplished by an orderly group working with common purpose.\n\n7 | I treat my weapons, uniform, and insignia with reverence, for they are gifts of the angels.\n\n8 | I pace when standing and fidget incessantly when forced to sit.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Guild. My guild is all that really matters. (Any)\n\n2 | Justice. Achieving justice requires establishing fair, equitable, and compassionate relationships within a community. (Good)\n\n3 | Protection. It isn't right for innocents to suffer because of the arrogance of the powerful. (Good)\n\n4 | Solidarity. It is most crucial to act with a single will, marching side by side in perfect accord. (Lawful)\n\n5 | Order. Society functions only if people do their duty and respect the chain of command. (Lawful)\n\n6 | Conviction. Anything worth doing is worth doing with your whole heart. (Lawful)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | I would lay down my life for Aurelia and the angels.\n\n2 | I owe my life to the Boros captain who took me in when I was living on the streets.\n\n3 | My fellow legionnaires are my family.\n\n4 | I wield the same Boros weapon my grandparent did, for the honor of our family.\n\n5 | I ran with the Rakdos in my youth, and I'm striving to atone for my past misdeeds.\n\n6 | I do what I can to help out the spouse of a comrade who died in battle.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I act bravely when I'm in a group, but I'm a coward when I'm alone.\n\n2 | I see everything in clear-cut black and white.\n\n3 | I'm just a little fascinated by the ways of the Gruul.\n\n4 | I trust the chain of command more than anything—more even than my closest friends.\n\n5 | I'm slow to trust members of other guilds.\n\n6 | I've been known to turn a blind eye to injustice, with the help of a modest bribe.\n\nContacts\n\nThe ordered structure of the Boros Legion offers abundant opportunities to make friends—and rivals—in higher places. You might have close friends in other guilds that share the Boros emphasis on order and community, or bitter enemies among the guilds that represent chaos and destruction.\n\nRoll twice on the Boros Contacts table (for an ally and a rival) and once on the Non-Boros Contacts table.\n\nd8 | Contact\n\n1 | A former comrade in arms was promoted into the prestigious Sunhome Guard.\n\n2 | One of my parents is a ranking Boros officer.\n\n3 | A close friend serves aboard the Parhelion II, a flying fortress.\n\n4 | I had a tangled affair with a Boros garrison captain.\n\n5 | I have maintained a relationship with one of my instructors at Horizon Military Academy.\n\n6 | I competed with a fellow student for the attention of a mentor at Horizon Military Academy.\n\n7 | The person who recruited me into the legion changed the course of my life.\n\n8 | A Boros angel knows my name.\n\nd10 | Contact\n\n1 | One of my siblings is an Azorius arrester.\n\n2 | Roll an additional Boros contact; you can decide if the contact is an ally or a rival.\n\n3 | I showed mercy to an injured, now-grateful Dimir spy.\n\n4 | I suspect someone I know is a Golgari assassin, but I can't prove it.\n\n5 | An adolescent relative ran off to join the Gruul in an act of rebellion and has not yet returned.\n\n6 | I once befriended an Izzet scientist, and we're still cordial though the relationship ended messily.\n\n7 | I owe a monetary debt to an Orzhov syndic.\n\n8 | A Rakdos blood witch seems to enjoy harassing me.\n\n9 | I tried to recruit a friend who ended up joining the Selesnya.\n\n10 | I keep running into a particular Simic biomancer, and I enjoy the arguments that inevitably result.\n\nHow Do I Fit In?\n\nAs a member of the Boros Legion, you are subject to the orders of your superior officers. You go where the angels tell you to go, and you do what they command you to do, to the best of your ability. If you enjoy some measure of independence, it's either because you have proven yourself capable of working without close supervision or because you're a rebellious sort who is willing to disobey orders now and face the consequences later.\n\nAs a soldier on the street, you are tasked with bringing dangerous threats like the Rakdos and the Gruul in line. You might contend with Rakdos performances gone horribly out of control, Gruul raids on outlying neighborhoods, shipments of rot-infested vegetation from the Golgari undercity, and violent uprisings among the guildless. At the same time, you might have to worry about Dimir spies infiltrating your leadership, overzealous or corrupt Azorius senators abusing the law at the expense of justice, Izzet experiments leveling city blocks, and Simic creations that break out of laboratories and wreak havoc through the Tenth District.\n\nTajic, Blade of the Legion\n\nTajic is a firefist who carries the exalted title of Blade of the Legion, putting him just below the angels in rank. He maintains close communication with Aurelia, though recent events in the city have set them at odds. Tajic believes that the Boros can trust only the Boros. He is convinced that any effort at peace among the guilds is doomed to failure without the Guildpact. The Boros, he argues, would be better off spending their energy to make themselves stronger so they can uphold the fragile balance that exists now—and protect the innocent when the balance tilts. Aurelia feels that his negative attitude runs the risk of poisoning the hearts of the other Boros and undermining any peace efforts. For the most part, in deference to the angel, Tajic keeps his views to himself."},
  ["spell.borrowed-knowledge.scc2014"]={title="Borrowed Knowledge",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nYou draw on knowledge from spirits of the past. Choose one skill in which you lack proficiency. For the spell's duration, you have proficiency in the chosen skill. The spell ends early if you cast it again."},
  ["creature.borthak.veor2014"]={title="Borthak",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 200 (16d12 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 16 | CON 22 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGlacial Aura\n\nAt the end of the borthak's turn, slippery ice covers surfaces within 10 feet of the borthak. This ice is difficult terrain. When a creature other than the borthak enters the ice's area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or have the prone condition. The ice disappears at the start of the borthak's next turn.\n\nWebbed Feet\n\nThe borthak can move across icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, difficult terrain composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe borthak makes one Bite attack or uses Noxious Regurgitation if available, and it makes two Stomp attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (1d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nNoxious Regurgitation {@recharge 5}\n\nThe borthak spews acid at a creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The target must make a 21 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 24 (7d6) acid damage and has the poisoned condition until the start of the borthak's next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReactive Tail\n\nWhen a creature within 10 feet of the borthak hits the borthak with an attack roll, the borthak swings its tail in retaliation. The triggering creature and any creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or take 16 (2d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nMove\n\nThe borthak moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nBite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe borthak makes one Bite attack."},
  ["creature.bosco-daggerhand.toa2014"]={title="Bosco Daggerhand",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.boss-augustus.bmt2014"]={title="Boss Augustus",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Thieves' cant (can't speak in wolf form)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration\n\nAugustus regains 10 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes damage from a silver weapon, this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Augustus dies only if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nAugustus wields a +2 Longsword.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAugustus makes any combination of two Bite, Claw, or Magic Longsword attacks.\n\nBite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h26 (5d8 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with MM. While cursed in this way, the target retains its alignment, languages, and equipment but otherwise uses the werewolf stat block, excluding actions that require equipment the target doesn't have. During any night when there's a full moon in the sky, the target becomes an NPC under the DM's control and remains so until the night ends. A Remove Curse spell or similar magic ends this curse.\n\nClaw (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h21 (5d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nMagic Longsword (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h28 (4d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nAugustus polymorphs into a wolf-humanoid hybrid, a wolf, or his humanoid form. His statistics, other than his speed, are the same in each form. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. He reverts to his humanoid form if he dies.\n\nCunning Action\n\nAugustus takes the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action."},
  ["creature.boss-delour.bmt2014"]={title="Boss Delour",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 83\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / S\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 110 (20d6 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Thieves' cant (can't speak in rat form)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasion\n\nIf Delour is subjected to an effect that allows him to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, he instead takes no damage if he succeeds on the saving throw and only half damage if he fails, provided he doesn't have the incapacitated condition.\n\nNimbleness\n\nDelour can move through the space of a Medium or larger creature.\n\nRegeneration\n\nDelour regains 10 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes damage from a silver weapon, this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Delour dies only if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nDelour makes any combination of three Bite, Shortsword, or Hand Crossbow attacks.\n\nBite (Rat or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h26 (5d8 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with MM. While cursed in this way, the target retains its alignment, languages, and equipment but otherwise uses the wererat stat block, excluding actions that require equipment the target doesn't have. During any night when there's a full moon in the sky, the target becomes an NPC under the DM's control and remains so until the night ends. A Remove Curse spell or similar magic ends this curse.\n\nShortsword (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage.\n\nHand Crossbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nDelour polymorphs into a rat-humanoid hybrid, a Medium giant rat, or his humanoid form. His statistics, other than his size and speed, are the same in each form. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. He reverts to his humanoid form if he dies.\n\nCunning Action\n\nDelour takes the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action."},
  ["language.bothii.frhof2014"]={title="Bothii",subtitle="Idioma - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 49"},
  ["language.bothii.skt2014"]={title="Bothii",subtitle="Idioma - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 86"},
  ["magicitem.bottle-of-boundless-coffee.scc2014"]={title="Bottle of Boundless Coffee",subtitle="Item Magico - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis metal bottle carries delicious, warm coffee. The bottle comes with a stopper, which is attached to the bottle by a little chain. Even when open, the bottle won't accept any liquid other than the coffee it produces. The coffee inside is always comfortably warm, and none of the heat can be felt through the bottle.\n\nEach time you drink the coffee, roll a d20. On a 1, the bottle refuses to dispense coffee for the next hour. If you pour coffee from the bottle, rather than drinking from it, the coffee vanishes the moment it leaves the bottle."},
  ["item.bottle-stopper-cork-embossed-with-gold-leaf-and-set-with-amethysts.dmg2014"]={title="Bottle stopper cork embossed with gold leaf and set with amethysts",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bottle-stopper-cork-embossed-with-gold-leaf-and-set-with-amethysts.xdmg2024"]={title="Bottle stopper cork embossed with gold leaf and set with amethysts",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.bottled-breath.pota2014"]={title="Bottled Breath",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis bottle contains a breath of elemental air. When you inhale it, you either exhale it or hold it.\n\nIf you exhale the breath, you gain the effect of the gust of wind spell. If you hold the breath, you don't need to breathe for 1 hour, though you can end this benefit early (for example, to speak). Ending it early doesn't give you the benefit of exhaling the breath."},
  ["feature.bottled-respite.tce2014.warlock.genie.1"]={title="Bottled Respite",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 73\n\nAs an action, you can magically vanish and enter your vessel, which remains in the space you left. The interior of the vessel is an extradimensional space in the shape of a 20-foot-radius cylinder, 20 feet high, and resembles your vessel. The interior is appointed with cushions and low tables and is a comfortable temperature. While inside, you can hear the area around your vessel as if you were in its space. You can remain inside the vessel up to a number of hours equal to twice your proficiency bonus. You exit the vessel early if you use a bonus action to leave, if you die, or if the vessel is destroyed. When you exit the vessel, you appear in the unoccupied space closest to it. Any objects left in the vessel remain there until carried out, and if the vessel is destroyed, every object stored there harmlessly appears in the unoccupied spaces closest to the vessel's former space. Once you enter the vessel, you can't enter again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["creature.boulderfoot-giant.psz2014"]={title="Boulderfoot Giant",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feat.bountiful-luck.xge2024"]={title="Bountiful Luck",subtitle="Feat - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nYour people have extraordinary luck, which you have learned to mystically lend to your companions when you see them falter. You're not sure how you do it; you just wish it, and it happens. Surely a sign of fortune's favor!\n\nWhen an ally you can see within 30 feet of you rolls a 1 on the d20 for an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw, you can use your reaction to let the ally reroll the die. The ally must use the new roll.\n\nWhen you use this ability, you can't use your Lucky racial trait before the end of your next turn."},
  ["magicitem.bowl-of-commanding-water-elementals.dmg2014"]={title="Bowl of Commanding Water Elementals",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile this bowl is filled with water, you can use an action to speak the bowl's command word and summon a water elemental, as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell. The bowl can't be used this way again until the next dawn.\n\nThe bowl is about 1 foot in diameter and half as deep. It weighs 3 pounds and holds about 3 gallons."},
  ["magicitem.bowl-of-commanding-water-elementals.xdmg2024"]={title="Bowl of Commanding Water Elementals",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile this bowl is filled with water and you are within 5 feet of it, you can take a XPHB action to summon a XMM. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the bowl as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB. The bowl can't be used this way again until the next dawn.\n\nThe bowl is about 1 foot in diameter and half as deep. It holds about 3 gallons."},
  ["item.box-of-turquoise-animal-figurines.dmg2014"]={title="Box of turquoise animal figurines",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.box-of-turquoise-animal-figurines.xdmg2024"]={title="Box of turquoise animal figurines",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.bozak-draconian.dsotdq2014"]={title="Bozak Draconian",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, its scales and flesh immediately shrivel away, and then its bones explode. Each creature within 10 feet of it must succeed on a 10 Dexterity saving throw or take 9 (2d8) force damage.\n\nGlide\n\nWhen the draconian falls and isn't incapacitated, it subtracts up to 100 feet from the fall when calculating the fall's damage, and it can move up to 2 feet horizontally for every 1 foot it descends.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Trident melee attacks or two Lightning Discharge attacks.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nLightning Discharge\n\nrs 4 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) lightning damage."},
  ["optionalfeature.brace.tce2014"]={title="Brace",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nWhen a creature you can see moves into the reach you have with the melee weapon you're wielding, you can use your reaction to expend one superiority die and make one attack against the creature, using that weapon. If the attack hits, add the superiority die to the weapon's damage roll."},
  ["magicitem.bracelet-of-rock-magic.tftyp2014"]={title="Bracelet of Rock Magic",subtitle="Item Magico - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile you wear this gold bracelet, it grants you immunity to being petrified, and it allows you to cast flesh to stone (save 15) as an action. Once the spell has been cast three times, the bracelet can no longer cast it. Thereafter, you can cast stone shape as an action. After you have done this thirteen times, the bracelet loses its magic and turns from gold to lead.\n\nCurse\n\nThe bracelet's affinity with earth manifests as an unusual curse. Creatures of flesh that are strongly related to earth and stone, such as stone giants and dwarves, have advantage on the saving throw against flesh to stone cast from the bracelet. If such a creature's save is successful, the bracelet breaks your attunement to it and casts the spell on you. You make your saving throw with disadvantage, and on a failed save you are petrified instantly."},
  ["magicitem.bracer-of-flying-daggers.wdh2014"]={title="Bracer of Flying Daggers",subtitle="Item Magico - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis armband appears to have thin phb strapped to it. As an action, you can pull up to two magic daggers from the bracer and immediately hurl them, making a ranged attack with each dagger. A dagger vanishes if you don't hurl it right away, and the daggers disappear right after they hit or miss. The bracer never runs out of daggers."},
  ["magicitem.bracers-of-archery.dmg2014"]={title="Bracers of Archery",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these bracers, you have proficiency with the PHB and PHB, and you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls on ranged attacks made with such weapons."},
  ["magicitem.bracers-of-archery.xdmg2024"]={title="Bracers of Archery",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing these bracers, you have proficiency with the XPHB and XPHB, and you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls made with such weapons."},
  ["magicitem.bracers-of-asmodeus.coa2014"]={title="Bracers of Asmodeus",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have a +2 bonus to AC while wearing these bracers, if you do not wear armor or use a shield at the same time.\n\nCurse\n\nWhile attuned to the bracers, you become obsessed with plotting, scheming, and manipulation. You always barter for better deals, often using secrets or leveraging other offers in the process. If you ever decline an opportunity to better yourself financially at another's expense, you immediately take 3d10 necrotic damage. Only the Remove Curse spell allows you to end attunement to this item.\n\nCorrupting\n\nThis item corrupts. See the \"CoA\" section."},
  ["magicitem.bracers-of-celerity.pabtso2014"]={title="Bracers of Celerity",subtitle="Item Magico - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis pair of lightweight bronze bracers is lined with soft, purple velvet and engraved with swirling designs.\n\nWhile you're wearing these bracers, all your speeds increase by 10 feet, and you have advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the paralyzed or restrained condition on yourself."},
  ["magicitem.bracers-of-defense.dmg2014"]={title="Bracers of Defense",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing these bracers, you gain a +2 bonus to AC if you are wearing no armor and using no PHB."},
  ["magicitem.bracers-of-defense.xdmg2024"]={title="Bracers of Defense",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing these bracers, you gain a +2 bonus to XPHB if you are wearing no armor and using no XPHB."},
  ["creature.brackish-trudge.scc2014"]={title="Brackish Trudge",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFungal Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the trudge to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 + the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the trudge drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTusk\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) poison damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.braelen-hatherhand.pota2014"]={title="Braelen Hatherhand",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nPV: 2 (1d8)"},
  ["creature.brahma-lutier.ai2014"]={title="Brahma Lutier",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nBrahma has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put her to sleep.\n\nTaunt (2/Day)\n\nBrahma can use a bonus action to target one creature she can see within 30 feet of her. If the target can hear Brahma, it must succeed on a 13 Charisma saving throw or have disadvantage on ability checks, attack rolls, and saving throws until the start of Brahma's next turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nWar Lute\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSong of Domination (3/Day)\n\nBrahma targets one creature that can see or hear her, which must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by her for 1 minute. The target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. It has disadvantage on these saves if being charmed by Brahma is something the target openly or secretly desires. For 1 hour after the charm effect ends, the target has disadvantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma checks made as part of a contest with Brahma."},
  ["creature.brain-breaker.pabtso2014"]={title="Brain Breaker",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 14\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30"},
  ["creature.brain-in-a-jar.llk2014"]={title="Brain in a Jar",subtitle="Criatura - LLK - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 1 | CON 15 | INT 19 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDetect Sentience\n\nThe brain in a jar can sense the presence and location of any creature within 300 feet of it that has an Intelligence of 3 or higher, regardless of interposing barriers, unless the creature is protected by a mind blank spell.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe brain in a jar has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMind Blast {@recharge 5}\n\nThe brain in a jar magically emits psychic energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 15 Intelligence saving throw or take 13 (2d8 + 4) psychic damage and be stunned for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.brain-in-a-jar.rhw2014"]={title="Brain in a Jar",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 239\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 55 (10d6 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 20\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 3 | CON 15 | INT 19 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft. understands Common plus three other languages but can't speak; telepathy 60 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDetect Intelligence\n\nThe brain magically senses the location of any creature within 300 feet of itself that has an Intelligence score of 3 or higher, regardless of interposing barriers.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe brain has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe brain makes two Disrupting Burst attacks.\n\nDisrupting Burst\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Psychic damage. The target can't take Reactions until the end of its next turn, and it has XPHB on saving throws to maintain XPHB until the end of its next turn.\n\nMind Blast {@recharge 5}\n\nint 14, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the brain's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.brain-in-a-jar.vrgr2014"]={title="Brain in a Jar",subtitle="Criatura - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 229\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 55 (10d6 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 10\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 3 | CON 15 | INT 19 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius); see also \"detect sentience\" below\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDetect Sentience\n\nThe brain can sense the presence and location of any creature within 300 feet of it that has an Intelligence of 3 or higher, regardless of interposing barriers, unless the creature is protected by a mind blank spell.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe brain has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magic effects.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe brain doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nChill Touch (Cantrip)\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h13 (3d8) necrotic damage, and the target can't regain hit points until the start of the brain's next turn. If the target is undead, it also has disadvantage on attack rolls against the brain until the end of the brain's next turn.\n\nMind Blast {@recharge 5}\n\nThe brain magically emits psychic energy in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 14 Intelligence saving throw or take 17 (3d8 + 4) psychic damage and be stunned for 1 minute. A stunned creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.brain-in-iron.imr2014"]={title="Brain in Iron",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCA: 15\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20"},
  ["deity.branchala.dsotdq2014"]={title="Branchala",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nCalled the Bard King, Branchala is the god of music, poetry, and the inner beauty of all living things. Many elves and kender worship him above all other gods. Both groups revere him as a champion of life and laughter, bringing solace and joy to those who listen."},
  ["deity.branchala.phb2014"]={title="Branchala",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["feature.branches-of-the-tree.xphb2024.barbarian.world-tree.6"]={title="Branches of the Tree",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.branding-smite.phb2014"]={title="Branding Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nThe next time you hit a creature with a weapon attack before this spell ends, the weapon gleams with astral radiance as you strike. The attack deals an extra 2d6 radiant damage to the target, which becomes visible if it's invisible, and the target sheds dim light in a 5-foot radius and can't become invisible until the spell ends."},
  ["deity.brandobaris.mtf2014"]={title="Brandobaris",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 104\n\nDashing trickster, patron of thieves, and star of fantastical fables and wild stories of adventure-that's the legacy of Brandobaris, the Master of Stealth. Stories of Brandobaris, full of artful trickery and narrow escapes, inspire many young halflings to play at roguish pursuits. In their imagination, a grain silo becomes a lofty wizard's tower to scale in search of treasures, or a rowboat becomes the setting for a swashbuckling adventure. And for some—the youngsters who are said to \"have a bit of Brandobaris in them\"—that play-acting is the prelude to a life of living as Brandobaris does: always on the lookout for the next challenge.\n\nBrandobaris continues to wander in search of excitement, and now, as an ascended being, his travels span the planes of existence. His curiosity takes him to all corners of the multiverse in search of magical curios, rare treasures, and mystical puzzles. When Brandobaris moves stealthily, no mortal or god can hear his footfalls-an ability he uses not only for defense, but also to bestow unlooked-for treats upon those he favors.\n\nAlthough he never seems to rest in his travels, Brandobaris always has time to reward halflings who dare to take risks and explore the world to make their own mark on it. He has been known to give a bit of aid to halflings in dire straits, turning them invisible for a time or intervening so that they can't be heard or tracked."},
  ["deity.brandobaris.scag2014"]={title="Brandobaris",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["magicitem.brass-dragon-scale-mail.dmg2014"]={title="Brass Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nDragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them to humanoids. Other times, hunters carefully skin and preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, dragon scale mail is highly valued. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to fire damage.\n\nAdditionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest brass dragon within 30 miles of you. This special action can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.brass-dragon-scale-mail.xdmg2024"]={title="Brass Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Dragon Scale Mail|XDMG"},
  ["creature.brass-dragon-wyrmling.mm2014"]={title="Brass Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 106\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, fly: 60\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Fire Breath\n\n• Sleep Breath"},
  ["creature.brass-dragon-wyrmling.xmm2024"]={title="Brass Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 54\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, fly: 60\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRend\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d10 + 2) Slashing damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 11, each creature in a 20-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nSleep Breath\n\ncon 11, each creature in a 15-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, at which point it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. This effect ends for the target if it takes damage or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to wake it."},
  ["creature.brass-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Brass Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 28\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 565 (29d20 + 261)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 16 | CON 29 | INT 21 | WIS 22 | CHA 30\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMetallic Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 450 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use the options in the \"Mythic Actions\" section for 1 hour. Award a party an additional 120,000 XP (240,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Metallic Awakening activates.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 20) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nTail\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Elemental Breath The greatwyrm exhales elemental energy in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw, taking 84 (13d12) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• Sapping Breath The greatwyrm exhales gas in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature falls unconscious for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature has disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws until the end of the greatwyrm's next turn. An unconscious creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses its action to end it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw or Tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm beats its wings. Each creature within 30 feet of it must succeed on a 26 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The greatwyrm can then fly up to half its flying speed.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nBite\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack.\n\nShattering Roar (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm unleashes a magical roar. Each creature in a 120-foot-radius sphere centered on the greatwyrm must succeed on a 26 Constitution saving throw or take 19 (3d12) thunder damage and be incapacitated until the end of its next turn."},
  ["item.brass-mug-with-jade-inlay.dmg2014"]={title="Brass mug with jade inlay",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.brass-mug-with-jade-inlay.xdmg2024"]={title="Brass mug with jade inlay",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.braxat.bam2014"]={title="Braxat",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 162 (13d12 + 78)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 8 | CON 22 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nImunidades: acid, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIntellect Fortress\n\nThe braxat's AC includes its Intelligence modifier.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe braxat makes two Greatclub attacks.\n\nGreatclub\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (3d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nAcid Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe braxat exhales a 15-foot cone of acid. Each creature in the cone must make a 18 Constitution saving throw, taking 26 (4d12) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nPsionic Shield (3/Day)\n\nWhen the braxat would be hit by an attack roll or a magic missile spell that originates from a source the braxat can see, the braxat can create an invisible barrier of magical force around itself that lasts until the start of its next turn. This barrier gives the braxat a +5 bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and prevents magic missile spells from damaging it."},
  ["creature.braxow.skt2014"]={title="Braxow",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.bray-martikov.cos2014"]={title="Bray Martikov",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.brazen-gorgon.xmm2024"]={title="Brazen Gorgon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 149\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 161 (17d10 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 19 | INT 2 | WIS 14 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlame Aura\n\nAt the end of each of the gorgon's turns, each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the gorgon takes 13 (3d8) Fire damage.\n\nIllumination\n\nThe gorgon sheds XPHB in a 10-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 10 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe gorgon makes two Gore attacks.\n\nGore\n\nm 8, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) Fire damage.\n\nSmelting Charge {@recharge 5}\n\nThe gorgon moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB and can move through the spaces of Medium or smaller creatures. Each time the gorgon enters a creature's space for the first time during this move, that target is subjected to the following effect. dex 16. actSaveFail 13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Fire damage, and the target is pulled into the gorgon's space and has the XPHB condition (escape 14); if the gorgon already has a creature XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition instead. Until the grapple ends, the target has the XPHB condition. When the gorgon moves, the XPHB target moves with it, costing no extra movement."},
  ["magicitem.brazier-of-commanding-fire-elementals.dmg2014"]={title="Brazier of Commanding Fire Elementals",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile a fire burns in this brass brazier, you can use an action to speak the brazier's command word and summon a fire elemental, as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell. The brazier can't be used this way again until the next dawn.\n\nThe brazier weighs 5 pounds."},
  ["magicitem.brazier-of-commanding-fire-elementals.xdmg2024"]={title="Brazier of Commanding Fire Elementals",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile you are within 5 feet of this brazier, you can take a XPHB action to summon a XMM. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the brazier as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB. The brazier can't be used this way again until the next dawn."},
  ["item.bread-loaf.xphb2024"]={title="Bread (loaf)",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 231\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["feature.breadth-of-knowledge.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.nomad.1"]={title="Breadth of Knowledge",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\nAt 1st level, you gain the ability to extend your knowledge. When you finish a long rest, you gain two proficiencies of your choice: two tools, two skills, or one of each. You can replace one or both of these selections with languages. This benefit lasts until you finish a long rest."},
  ["item.breastplate.phb2014"]={title="Breastplate",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis armor consists of a fitted metal chest piece worn with supple leather. Although it leaves the legs and arms relatively unprotected, this armor provides good protection for the wearer's vital organs while leaving the wearer relatively unencumbered."},
  ["item.breastplate.xphb2024"]={title="Breastplate",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 219\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.breastplate-of-balance.bmt2014"]={title="Breastplate of Balance",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis burnished copper breastplate looks as if it were made of interlocking gears. Merchant's scales are emblazoned across the chest.\n\nThe armor has 4 charges. You can use the charges in the following ways while wearing the armor:\n\n• Equalize When you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself is about to roll a d20 with advantage or disadvantage, you can expend 1 charge and take a reaction to prevent the roll from being affected by advantage or disadvantage.\n\n• Expunge Imbalance As a bonus action, you can expend 2 charges to cast the Lesser Restoration spell from the armor.\n\nThe armor regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn.\n\nThis armor consists of a fitted metal chest piece worn with supple leather. Although it leaves the legs and arms relatively unprotected, this armor provides good protection for the wearer's vital organs while leaving the wearer relatively unencumbered."},
  ["creature.breath-drinker.bmt2014"]={title="Breath Drinker",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 157 (21d8 + 63)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 60\n\nSTR 5 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 15 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: poison, radiant\n\nVulnerabilidades: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nThe breath drinker can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) force damage if it ends its turn inside an object.\n\nRadiant Absorption\n\nWhen the breath drinker is subjected to radiant damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the radiant damage dealt.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe breath drinker makes two Enervating Claw attacks. It can also use Drink Breath.\n\nEnervating Claw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h12 (2d6 + 5) necrotic damage, and if the target is Large or smaller, it has the grappled condition (escape 18). The target must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if this effect reduces its hit point maximum to 0.\n\nDrink Breath\n\nThe breath drinker targets a creature that has the incapacitated condition or that the breath drinker is grappling and that isn't a Construct or an Undead. The target must make a 18 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 36 (8d8) necrotic damage, and its Charisma score is reduced by 1d6. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a short or long rest. If this reduces the target's Charisma to 0, the target dies. Until the breath drinker dies, the dead target can't be returned to life by any means short of divine intervention. On a successful save, the target takes half as much necrotic damage only. On a successful or failed save, the breath drinker regains a number of hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt.\n\nInvisibility\n\nThe breath drinker has the invisible condition. This invisibility ends immediately after the breath drinker hits or misses with an attack roll or uses Drink Breath."},
  ["feature.breath-of-the-dragon.ftd2014.monk.ascendant-dragon.3"]={title="Breath of the Dragon",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\n3rd-level Way of the Ascendant Dragon feature\n\nYou can channel destructive waves of energy, like those created by the dragons you emulate. When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of the attacks with an exhalation of draconic energy in either a 20-foot cone or a 30-foot line that is 5 feet wide (your choice). Choose a damage type: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw against your ki save DC, taking damage of the chosen type equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nAt 11th level, the damage of this feature increases to three rolls of your Martial Arts die.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest. While you have no uses available, you can spend 2 ki points to use this feature again."},
  ["optionalfeature.breath-of-winter.phb2014"]={title="Breath of Winter",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\nYou can spend 6 ki points to cast cone of cold."},
  ["magicitem.breathing-bubble.egw2014"]={title="Breathing Bubble",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis translucent, bubble-like sphere has a slightly tacky outer surface, and you gain the item's benefits only while wearing it over your head like a helmet.\n\nThe bubble contains 1 hour of breathable air. The bubble regains all its expended air daily at dawn."},
  ["item.brewer-s-supplies.phb2014"]={title="Brewer's Supplies",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nBrewing is the art of producing beer. Not only does beer serve as an alcoholic beverage, but the process of brewing purifies water. Crafting beer takes weeks of fermentation, but only a few hours of work.\n\nComponents\n\nBrewer's supplies include a large glass jug, a quantity of hops, a siphon, and several feet of tubing.\n\nHistory\n\nProficiency with brewer's supplies gives you additional insight on Intelligence (History) checks concerning events that involve alcohol as a significant element.\n\nMedicine\n\nThis tool proficiency grants additional insight when you treat anyone suffering from alcohol poisoning or when you can use alcohol to dull pain.\n\nPersuasion\n\nA stiff drink can help soften the hardest heart. Your proficiency with brewer's supplies can help you ply someone with drink, giving them just enough alcohol to mellow their mood.\n\nPotable Water\n\nYour knowledge of brewing enables you to purify water that would otherwise be undrinkable. As part of a long rest, you can purify up to 6 gallons of water, or 1 gallon as part of a short rest.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nDetect poison or impurities in a drink | 10\n\nIdentify alcohol | 15\n\nIgnore effects of alcohol | 20"},
  ["item.brewer-s-supplies.xphb2024"]={title="Brewer's Supplies",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 220\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Intelligence\n\n• Utilize: Detect poisoned drink (15), or identify alcohol (10)\n\n• Craft: XPHB"},
  ["creature.bridesmaid-of-zuggtmoy.oota2014"]={title="Bridesmaid of Zuggtmoy",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 11 | INT 14 | WIS 8 | CHA 18\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFungus Stride\n\nOnce on its turn, the bridesmaid can use 10 feet of its movement to step magically into one living mushroom or fungus patch within 5 feet and emerge from another within 60 feet of the first one, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second mushroom or fungus patch. The mushrooms and patches must be large or bigger.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHallucination Spores\n\nThe bridesmaid ejects spores at one creature it can see within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. While poisoned in this way, the target is incapacitated. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nInfestation Spores (1/Day)\n\nThe bridesmaid releases spores that burst out in a cloud that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on it, and the cloud lingers for 1 minute. Any flesh-and-blood creature in the cloud when it appears, or that enters it later, must make a 10 Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the creature can't be infected by these spores for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature is infected with a disease called the spores of Zuggtmoy and also gains a random form of indefinite madness (determined by rolling on the Madness of Zuggtmoy table in appendix D) that lasts until the creature is cured of the disease or dies. While infected in this way, the creature can't be reinfected, and it must be repeat the saving throw at the end of every 24 hours, ending the infection on a success. On a failure, the infected creature's body is slowly taken over by fungal growth, and after three such failed saves, the creature dies and is reanimated as a spore servant if it's a type of creature that can be (see the \"Myconids\" entry in the Monster Manual)."},
  ["magicitem.bridle-of-capturing.imr2014"]={title="Bridle of Capturing",subtitle="Item Magico - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis fine leather bridle tugs at the hand when first held, as though it longs to reach out for a beast nearby. When you hold one end of the bridle, you can use an action to speak its command word, causing the other end to lash out at a beast you can see within 20 feet of you. The target must succeed on a 17 Charisma saving throw or have the bridle tie itself around its neck, then fall under your command as if subjected to the dominate beast spell. Once the targeted is affected, you do not need to hold the other end of the bridle to command it. With a successful saving throw, the target becomes immune to the bridle's power until the next dawn.\n\nA creature controlled by the bridle can be released by the creature that bound it as a bonus action. A creature controlled by the bridle can make a 17 Charisma check each day at dawn. On a success, the creature is no longer affected by the bridle."},
  ["deity.brigantia.phb2014"]={title="Brigantia",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["creature.brigganock.wbtw2014"]={title="Brigganock",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 9 (2d4 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nThe brigganock has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put it to sleep.\n\nSoul Light\n\nThe brigganock is accompanied by an insubstantial, invulnerable ball of light that contains its soul. The brigganock can't turn off the light or control its brightness. The soul light sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for an additional 10 feet. If the brigganock dies, its soul light fades away.\n\nTunneler\n\nUsing a pickaxe or similar tool, a brigganock can burrow through solid rock at a speed of 5 feet, leaving a 6-inch-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPickaxe\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nTime Lapse (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe brigganock accelerates the passage of time around itself, enabling it to accomplish up to 1 hour of work in a matter of seconds. This work can't affect any creature other than the brigganock, or any object being worn or carried by another creature, and the activity must take place within a 10-foot cube. For example, the brigganock could use this action to rapidly carve a pumpkin, cook and eat dinner, move a pile of stones, or tie a dozen knots in a length of rope.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nMove Soul Light\n\nThe brigganock moves its soul light up to 30 feet in any direction to an unoccupied space it can see. At the end of the current turn, the light returns to the brigganock."},
  ["item.bright-fungal-cloak.frhof2014"]={title="Bright Fungal Cloak",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nRaridade: none\n\nWhile wearing a Bright Fungal Cloak, you can take a XPHB to furl or unfurl it. When the cloak is unfurled, it sheds XPHB in a 5-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 5 feet.\n\nOne pound of fungus is sewn into a Bright Fungal Cloak. This fungus can be eaten as food. Once all the fungus is consumed, the cloak becomes a mundane set of XPHB."},
  ["item.bringers-of-cosmic-dawn-trinket.au2014"]={title="Bringers of Cosmic Dawn Trinket",subtitle="Item - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 87\n\nRaridade: none\n\n1d6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A razor-sharp, violet-tinted talon\n\n2 | An uneven spyglass lens that casts flickering pale-green light\n\n3 | A stone carved with stars in an unfamiliar constellation\n\n4 | Fragments of a prophecy about flumphs\n\n5 | A fern frond that twitches like a tentacle\n\n6 | A small box containing a worm that won't die"},
  ["creature.bristled-moorbounder.egw2014"]={title="Bristled Moorbounder",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 295\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 70\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBladed Hide\n\nAt the start of each of its turns, the moorbounder deals 5 (2d4) piercing damage to any creature grappling it.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe moorbounder's long jump is up to 40 feet and its high jump is up to 20 feet, with or without a running start.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe moorbounder makes two attacks: one with its blades and one with its claws.\n\nBlades\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d4 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.broken-king-antigonos.mot2014"]={title="Broken King Antigonos",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 38 (9d10 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 6 | WIS 16 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf Antigonos moves at least 10 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away and knocked prone.\n\nLabyrinthine Recall\n\nAntigonos can perfectly recall any path he has traveled.\n\nReckless\n\nAt the start of his turn, Antigonos can gain advantage on all melee weapon attack rolls he makes during that turn, but attack rolls against him have advantage until the start of his next turn.\n\nDecrepit State\n\nAntigonos has disadvantage on his attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGreataxe\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d12 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nGore\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nAmphora\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If there is not already a creature inside the amphora, the target is restrained inside. As an action, the restrained creature can make a 14 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check, escaping from the amphora on a success. The effect also ends if the amphora is destroyed. The amphora has AC 8, 20 hit points, and immunity to poison and psychic damage."},
  ["reward.broken-vow.vrgr2014"]={title="Broken Vow",subtitle="Recompensa - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\nA character breaks a solemn vow. The consequences stem from the powers that observed the oath's swearing.\n\nPronouncement\n\nWhatever vow the character made, it came with an implied warning that guilt and restlessness would beset anyone who broke the oath.\n\nBurden\n\nThe character is plagued by restless sleep and recurring nightmares featuring those the character swore to protect. The character gains 3 levels of exhaustion that can't be removed until the curse ends.\n\nResolution\n\nThe curse lasts until the character upholds the broken oath. That might require the character to wait until the circumstances arise again or, more questionably, to engineer the circumstances."},
  ["creature.brom-martikov.cos2014"]={title="Brom Martikov",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 98\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.brontodon.psx2014"]={title="Brontodon",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.brontosaurus.mpmm2014"]={title="Brontosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / G\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 121 (9d20 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 9 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStomp\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h27 (5d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nTail\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h32 (6d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.brontosaurus.vgm2014"]={title="Brontosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / G\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 121 (9d20 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 9 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStomp\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h27 (5d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nTail\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h32 (6d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.bronze-crown.dmg2014"]={title="Bronze crown",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.bronze-crown.xdmg2024"]={title="Bronze crown",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.bronze-dragon-scale-mail.dmg2014"]={title="Bronze Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nDragon scale mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off scales and gift them to humanoids. Other times, hunters carefully skin and preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, dragon scale mail is highly valued. While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to AC, you have advantage on saving throws against the Frightful Presence and breath weapons of dragons, and you have resistance to lightning damage.\n\nAdditionally, you can focus your senses as an action to magically discern the distance and direction to the closest bronze dragon within 30 miles of you. This special action can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.bronze-dragon-scale-mail.xdmg2024"]={title="Bronze Dragon Scale Mail",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 254\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Dragon Scale Mail|XDMG"},
  ["creature.bronze-dragon-wyrmling.mm2014"]={title="Bronze Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 109\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Lightning Breath\n\n• Repulsion Breath"},
  ["creature.bronze-dragon-wyrmling.xmm2024"]={title="Bronze Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 58\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d10 + 3) Slashing damage.\n\nLightning Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 12, each creature in a 40-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 16 (3d10) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nRepulsion Breath\n\nstr 12, each creature in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target is pushed up to 30 feet straight away from the dragon and has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.bronze-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Bronze Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 28\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 565 (29d20 + 261)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 16 | CON 29 | INT 21 | WIS 22 | CHA 30\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMetallic Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 450 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use the options in the \"Mythic Actions\" section for 1 hour. Award a party an additional 120,000 XP (240,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Metallic Awakening activates.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 20) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nTail\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Elemental Breath The greatwyrm exhales elemental energy in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw, taking 84 (13d12) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• Sapping Breath The greatwyrm exhales gas in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature falls unconscious for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature has disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws until the end of the greatwyrm's next turn. An unconscious creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses its action to end it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw or Tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm beats its wings. Each creature within 30 feet of it must succeed on a 26 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The greatwyrm can then fly up to half its flying speed.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nBite\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack.\n\nShattering Roar (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm unleashes a magical roar. Each creature in a 120-foot-radius sphere centered on the greatwyrm must succeed on a 26 Constitution saving throw or take 19 (3d12) thunder damage and be incapacitated until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.bronze-sable.mot2014"]={title="Bronze Sable",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands one language of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the sable remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal statue.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe sable has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the sable's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf the sable surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) damage from the attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sable makes two bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.bronze-scout.mtf2014"]={title="Bronze Scout",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 18 (4d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands one language of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEarth Armor\n\nThe bronze scout doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it burrows.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe bronze scout has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) lightning damage.\n\nLightning Flare (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nEach creature in contact with the ground within 15 feet of the bronze scout must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["item.bronze-spyglass-brazen-coalition.psx2014"]={title="Bronze spyglass (Brazen Coalition)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.bronzefume.pota2014"]={title="Bronzefume",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 92\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 13\n\nPV: 220 (22d20 + 110)"},
  ["magicitem.brooch-of-living-essence.egw2014"]={title="Brooch of Living Essence",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this nondescript brooch, spells and anything else that would detect or reveal your creature type treat you as humanoid, and those that would reveal your alignment treat it as neutral."},
  ["magicitem.brooch-of-shielding.dmg2014"]={title="Brooch of Shielding",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this brooch, you have resistance to force damage, and you have immunity to damage from the magic missile spell."},
  ["magicitem.brooch-of-shielding.xdmg2024"]={title="Brooch of Shielding",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this brooch, you have XPHB to Force damage, and you have XPHB to damage from the XPHB spell."},
  ["magicitem.brooch-of-the-elements.nf2014"]={title="Brooch of the Elements",subtitle="Item Magico - NF - 2014",body="Raridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThe central jewel of this butterfly-shaped brooch swirls with multicolored iridescence.\n\nThe brooch has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. As a XPHB when a creature you can see within 60 feet of you hits a target with an attack roll and deals damage, you can expend 1 charge and change one damage type the attack deals to one of the following damage types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, or Thunder."},
  ["creature.broom-of-animated-attack.cos2014"]={title="Broom of Animated Attack",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 17 (5d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nConstructed Nature\n\nAn animated object doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\nThe magic that animates an object is dispelled when the construct drops to 0 hit points. An animated object reduced to 0 hit points becomes inanimate and is too damaged to be of much use or value to anyone.\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe broom is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the broom must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the broom remains motionless and isn't flying, it is indistinguishable from a normal broom.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe broom makes two melee attacks.\n\nBroomstick\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nAnimated Attack\n\nIf the broom is motionless and a creature grabs hold of it, the broom makes a Dexterity check contested by the creature's Strength check. If the broom wins the contest, it flies out of the creature's grasp and makes a melee attack against it with advantage on the attack roll."},
  ["magicitem.broom-of-flying.dmg2014"]={title="Broom of Flying",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 156\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis wooden broom, which weighs 3 pounds, functions like a mundane broom until you stand astride it and speak its command word. It then hovers beneath you and can be ridden in the air. It has a flying speed of 50 feet. It can carry up to 400 pounds, but its flying speed becomes 30 feet while carrying over 200 pounds. The broom stops hovering when you land.\n\nYou can send the broom to travel alone to a destination within 1 mile of you if you speak the command word, name the location, and are familiar with that place. The broom comes back to you when you speak another command word, provided that the broom is still within 1 mile of you."},
  ["magicitem.broom-of-flying.xdmg2024"]={title="Broom of Flying",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis wooden broom functions like a mundane broom until you stand astride it and take a XPHB action to make it hover beneath you, at which time it can be ridden in the air. It has a XPHB of 50 feet. It can carry up to 400 pounds, but its XPHB becomes 30 feet while carrying over 200 pounds. The broom stops hovering when you land or when you're no longer riding it.\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can send the broom to travel alone to a destination within 1 mile of you if you name the location and are familiar with it. The broom comes back to you when you take a XPHB action and use a command word if the broom is still within 1 mile of you."},
  ["creature.brother-adramalech.coa2014"]={title="Brother Adramalech",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 212 (25d8 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 25 | WIS 25 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Adramalech's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAdramalech has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nUnbreakable Bond\n\nIf Adramalech is reduced to 0 hit points while Brother Morax still lives, Adramalech regenerates 50 hit points at the start of his next turn. This regeneration is interrupted if Brother Morax is reduced to 0 hit points before the start of Adramalech's turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAdramalech makes four attacks using Mental\n\nBarrage\n\nHe can replace one of the attacks with Brain Freeze or Cone of Madness (if available).\n\nMental Barrage\n\nmw,rw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60/120 ft., one target. h25 (4d8 + 7) psychic damage.\n\nBrain Freeze\n\nAdramalech attempts to overload the brain of a creature he can see within 60 feet of him. The target must make a 22 Intelligence saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. Creatures that fail the saving throw have the stunned condition for up to 1 minute. A stunned creature may repeat the saving throw at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success.\n\nCone of Madness {@recharge 4}\n\nAdramalech unleashes visions in a 30-foot cone in front of him. All creatures in the cone must make a 22 Wisdom saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. For up to 1 minute, creatures that failed the save can't take reactions and each turn must use their action to make a melee attack against the nearest creature. Creatures may repeat the saving throw at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nConjure Effigy {@recharge}\n\nAdramalech targets a creature, reading its thoughts and creating an effigy of a loved one in an unoccupied space that he can see within 60 feet of Adramalech. The effigy has 55 (10d10) hit points, an AC of 10, and ability scores of 10. It occasionally shouts for help, but otherwise takes no actions. While the effigy is alive, the target creature has disadvantage on attacks targeting Adramalech and any time the effigy takes damage, the target creature also takes an equal amount as psychic damage. If the effigy is killed, the target creature gains a level of exhaustion. If Adramalech is killed while effigies exist, they harmlessly melt into a warm sludge.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBarrage\n\nAdramalech makes a Mental Barrage attack.\n\nMental Blocker\n\nAdramalech fortifies the mind of a creature he can see within 60 feet of him, or himself. The target benefits as if the Greater Restoration spell has been cast on them and is granted resistance to psychic damage until the end of Adramalech's next turn."},
  ["creature.brother-broumane.jttrc2014"]={title="Brother Broumane",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 178\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.brother-morax.coa2014"]={title="Brother Morax",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 186\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 337 (25d10 + 200)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 22 | CON 27 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrittle Spine\n\nFor each Brittle Spine a creature has, the creature takes 3 (1d6) poison damage at the start of each of their turns, and when Morax activates Burrow or Deep Burrow. Spines can only be removed by a Regeneration spell or similar, or by killing Morax.\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Morax's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nMorax has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpined Hide\n\nWhenever Morax is hit with a melee attack, the attacker takes 7 (2d6) piercing damage and gains 1 Brittle Spine.\n\nUnbreakable Bond\n\nIf Morax is reduced to 0 hit points while Brother Adramalech still lives, Morax regenerates 50 hit points at the start of his next turn. This regeneration is interrupted if Brother Adramalech is reduced to 0 hit points before the start of Morax's turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nMorax makes four attacks using his Claw, Spine Fling, or a combination of the two.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (3d6 + 7) slashing damage, and the target gains 1 Brittle Spine.\n\nSpine Fling\n\nrw 13 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one target. h12 (1d12 + 6) piercing damage, and the target gains 1 Brittle Spine.\n\nDeep Burrow\n\nMorax immediately deals Brittle Spine ongoing damage to all creatures that have at least one Brittle Spine that he can see.\n\nBone Spikes {@recharge}\n\nMorax shoves an arm into the ground, rapidly growing bones that erupt at a point he can see within 100 feet of him. Each creature in a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 28 (8d6) piercing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Creatures that fail the save gain 2 Brittle Spines, while creatures that succeed only gain 1 Brittle Spine.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nMorax makes a Claw attack.\n\nBone Splinters (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMorax gestures at a creature he can see that has at least 1 Brittle Spine. That creature must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw or the number of Brittle Spines it has doubles.\n\nBurrow (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nMorax bristles the spines within a creature that he can see. The target immediately takes Brittle Spine ongoing damage."},
  ["creature.brown-bear.mm2014"]={title="Brown Bear",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 319\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 34 (4d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe bear has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bear makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.brown-bear.xmm2024"]={title="Brown Bear",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 350\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 22 (3d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bear makes one Bite attack and one Claw attack.\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["traphazard.brown-mold.dmg2014"]={title="Brown Mold",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 105\n\nBrown mold feeds on warmth, drawing heat from anything around it. A patch of brown mold typically covers a 10-foot square, and the temperature within 30 feet of it is always frigid.\n\nWhen a creature moves to within 5 feet of the mold for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must make a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nBrown mold is immune to fire, and any source of fire brought within 5 feet of a patch causes it to instantly expand outward in the direction of the fire, covering a 10-foot-square area (with the source of the fire at the center of that area). A patch of brown mold exposed to an effect that deals cold damage is instantly destroyed."},
  ["traphazard.brown-mold.xdmg2024"]={title="Brown Mold",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 76\n\nBrown mold resembles a furry, light-brown carpet. This fungus feeds on warmth, drawing heat from anything around itself. One patch of brown mold covers a 10-foot square, and the temperature within 30 feet of it is always frigid.\n\nWhen a creature enters a space within 5 feet of the mold for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, the creature makes a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) Cold damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nBrown mold has XPHB to Fire damage, and any source of fire brought within 5 feet of it causes the mold to instantly expand across a surface and toward the fire, creating a new patch that covers a 10-foot square. A patch of brown mold exposed to an effect that deals any amount of Cold damage is destroyed instantly."},
  ["creature.brown-scavver.bam2014"]={title="Brown Scavver",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 49\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 51 (6d10 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe scavver doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSwallowing Bite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or be swallowed by the scavver. The scavver can have one creature swallowed at a time.\n\nA swallowed creature is blinded and restrained, has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the scavver, and takes 13 (3d8) poison damage at the start of each of the scavver's turns from the poisonous gas in the scavver's gullet.\n\nIf the scavver takes 15 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the scavver must succeed on a 20 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate the swallowed creature, which falls prone in a space within 10 feet of the scavver. If the scavver dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse by using 10 feet of movement, exiting prone."},
  ["creature.bruna.psi2014"]={title="Bruna",subtitle="Criatura - PSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.brusipha.bmt2014"]={title="Brusipha",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 11 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDemonic Ritual\n\nBrusipha can spend 3 hours performing a ritual that summons 1d3 + 1 barlguras or 1 hezrou. She must sacrifice a Medium or larger living creature to Baphomet during this ritual, and the ritual can be performed only at night. The demons vanish at dawn.\n\nLabyrinthine Recall\n\nBrusipha can perfectly recall any path she has traveled.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBrusipha makes two Eldritch Blast attacks.\n\nEldritch Blast\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) force damage.\n\nGore\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) necrotic damage. If Brusipha moved at least 10 feet straight toward the target immediately before she hit, the target takes an extra 4 (1d8) piercing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet from Brusipha and have the prone condition.\n\nIncite the Hunters (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nBrusipha allows each ally within 30 feet of herself that has the Unerring Tracker trait to make one weapon attack as a reaction against the target of that ally's Unerring Tracker.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nUnerring Tracker\n\nBrusipha magically creates a psychic link with one creature she can see. For the next hour, Brusipha knows the current distance and direction to the target if it is on the same plane of existence. The link ends if Brusipha has the incapacitated condition or uses this ability on a different target.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nBaphomet's Blessing\n\nWhen Brusipha reduces a hostile creature to 0 hit points, she gains 8 temporary hit points."},
  ["feature.brutal-critical-1-die.phb2014.barbarian.base.9"]={title="Brutal Critical (1 die)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.brutal-critical-2-dice.phb2014.barbarian.base.13"]={title="Brutal Critical (2 dice)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.brutal-critical-3-dice.phb2014.barbarian.base.17"]={title="Brutal Critical (3 dice)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.brutal-strike.xphb2024.barbarian.base.9"]={title="Brutal Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["psionic.brute-force.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Brute Force",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 11\n\nYou augment your natural strength with psionic energy, granting you the ability to achieve incredible feats of might."},
  ["creature.bubba-wugga.drde-bd2014"]={title="Bubba Wugga",subtitle="Criatura - DrDe-BD - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish"},
  ["item.bucket.phb2014"]={title="Bucket",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA bucket holds 3 gallons of liquid or ½ cubic foot of solids."},
  ["item.bucket.xphb2024"]={title="Bucket",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Bucket holds up to half a cubic foot of contents."},
  ["magicitem.budding-blossom-rod.au2014"]={title="Budding Blossom Rod",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nBudding\n\nMulticolored leaves decorate the rod's stems, and a few buds cluster near each end.\n\nWhile you hold the rod, you can cast XPHB or XPHB (Overgrowth only) from it. Once the rod has been used to cast XPHB, it can't be used to cast this spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile you hold the rod, as a XPHB action, you can rejuvenate nonmagical plants in a 5-foot XPHB you can see within 15 feet of yourself. The rejuvenated plants remain verdant for 1d4 days, after which they grow or wither as normal plants would."},
  ["creature.buer.coa2014"]={title="Buer",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 315 (30d10 + 150)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 22 | CON 21 | INT 16 | WIS 18 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nContractually Obligated\n\nBuer has advantage to hit creatures under an infernal contract and when she hits such creatures she delivers an additional 9 (2d8) damage of a type the target is most vulnerable to. A creature bound under an infernal contract also makes all saving throws against effects originating from Buer with disadvantage.\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Buer's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nBuer has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nBuer makes three attacks using her Claw. She can replace two of the attacks with a Cleansing Bite attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nCleansing Bite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (2d12 + 6) bludgeoning damage, healing Buer for an amount equal to the damage dealt.\n\nSpectral Reaping {@recharge}\n\nBuer focuses her ethereal form, dashing up to 50 feet in a straight line through the ethereal plane. Any creatures in the line must make a 21 Constitution saving throw, taking 42 (12d6) force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Buer may reappear at any unoccupied space along the line. For 1 minute after using Spectral Reaping, Buer is empowered by ethereal essence. Her Cleansing Bite attack now deals force damage instead of bludgeoning.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDefensive Trip {@recharge 5}\n\nBuer attempts to slow the actions of a creature she can see within 60 feet of her. The target must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw or be slowed until the end of its next turn. A slowed creature's speed is halved, it takes a-2 penalty to AC and Dexterity saving throws, and it can't use its reactions. Regardless of the slowed creature's abilities or magic items, it can't make more than one melee or ranged attack during its turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSoul Exchange\n\nWhen Buer is subjected to a spell targeting only her, she can attempt to swap places with a creature she damaged on her last turn. The creature must make a 19 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature and Buer swap positions, and the spell now targets the creature instead of Buer.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTeamwork\n\nBuer or one other devil within 60 feet of Buer makes a melee weapon attack against a target of Buer's choosing.\n\nBackdoor Clause\n\nBuer wreathes energy around a creature she can see within 60 feet of her. Until the end of Buer's next turn, the target is covered in fire or cold energy, Buer's choice. Each time the target is struck with a melee attack, the attacker takes 9 (2d8) fire or cold damage.\n\nRefresh Souls (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nBuer devours a Soul Coin, instantly refreshing one Recharge ability of any devil within 60 feet, including herself."},
  ["species.bugbear.erlw2014"]={title="Bugbear",subtitle="Especie - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nAge\n\nBugbears reach adulthood at age 16 and live up to 80 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nBugbears live on the fringes of society even in Darguun, where they value self-sufficiency and violence. They are generally chaotic, organizing in loose tribes under charismatic and powerful leaders.\n\nSize\n\nYour size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nLong-Limbed\n\nWhen you make a melee attack on your turn, your reach for it is 5 feet greater than normal.\n\nPowerful Build\n\nYou count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, or lift.\n\nSneaky\n\nYou are proficient in the Stealth skill.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf you surprise a creature and hit it with an attack on your first turn in combat, the attack deals an extra 2d6 damage to it. You can use this trait only once per combat.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Goblin."},
  ["creature.bugbear.mm2014"]={title="Bugbear",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrute\n\nA melee weapon deals one extra die of its damage when the bugbear hits with it (included in the attack).\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf the bugbear surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage from the attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMorningstar\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) piercing damage in melee or 5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage at range."},
  ["species.bugbear.mpmm2014"]={title="Bugbear",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Humanoid. You are also considered a goblinoid for any prerequisite or effect that requires you to be a goblinoid.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light and in darkness as if it were dim light. You discern colors in that darkness only as shades of gray.\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the charmed condition on yourself.\n\nLong-Limbed\n\nWhen you make a melee attack on your turn, your reach for it is 5 feet greater than normal.\n\nPowerful Build\n\nYou count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, or lift.\n\nSneaky\n\nYou are proficient in the Stealth skill. In addition, without squeezing, you can move through and stop in a space large enough for a Small creature.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf you hit a creature with an attack roll, the creature takes an extra 2d6 damage if it hasn't taken a turn yet in the current combat."},
  ["species.bugbear.vgm2014"]={title="Bugbear",subtitle="Especie - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nAge\n\nBugbears reach adulthood at age 16 and live up to 80 years.\n\nSize\n\nBugbears are between 6 and 8 feet tall and weigh between 250 and 350 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nLong-Limbed\n\nWhen you make a melee attack on your turn, your reach for it is 5 feet greater than normal.\n\nPowerful Build\n\nYou count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push, drag, or lift.\n\nSneaky\n\nYou are proficient in the Stealth skill.\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf you surprise a creature and hit it with an attack on your first turn in combat, the attack deals an extra 2d6 damage to it. You can use this trait only once per combat.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Goblin."},
  ["creature.bugbear-chief.mm2014"]={title="Bugbear Chief",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrute\n\nA melee weapon deals one extra die of its damage when the bugbear hits with it (included in the attack).\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf the bugbear surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage from the attack.\n\nHeart of Hruggek\n\nThe bugbear has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, stunned, or put to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bugbear makes two melee attacks.\n\nMorningstar\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage in melee or 5 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage at range."},
  ["creature.bugbear-gardener.tftyp2014"]={title="Bugbear Gardener",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.bugbear-lieutenant.tftyp2014"]={title="Bugbear Lieutenant",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.bugbear-stalker.xmm2024"]={title="Bugbear Stalker",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAbduct\n\nThe bugbear needn't spend extra movement to move a creature it is grappling.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bugbear makes two Javelin or Morningstar attacks.\n\nJavelin\n\nm,r 5, reach 10 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h13 (3d6 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nMorningstar\n\nm 5 (with XPHB if the target is XPHB by the bugbear), reach 10 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nQuick Grapple\n\ndex 13, one Medium or smaller creature the bugbear can see within 10 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition (escape 13)."},
  ["creature.bugbear-warrior.xmm2024"]={title="Bugbear Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAbduct\n\nThe bugbear needn't spend extra movement to move a creature it is grappling.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGrab\n\nm 4, reach 10 ft. h9 (2d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 12).\n\nLight Hammer\n\nm,r 4 (with XPHB if the target is XPHB by the bugbear), reach 10 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h9 (3d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.bulette.mm2014"]={title="Bulette",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 94 (9d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 21 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe bulette's long jump is up to 30 feet and its high jump is up to 15 feet, with or without a running start.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h30 (4d12 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nDeadly Leap\n\nIf the bulette jumps at least 15 feet as part of its movement, it can then use this action to land on its feet in a space that contains one or more other creatures. Each of those creatures must succeed on a 16 Strength or Dexterity saving throw (target's choice) or be knocked prone and take 14 (3d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (3d6 + 4) slashing damage. On a successful save, the creature takes only half the damage, isn't knocked prone, and is pushed 5 feet out of the bulette's space into an unoccupied space of the creature's choice. If no unoccupied space is within range, the creature instead falls prone in the bulette's space."},
  ["creature.bulette.xmm2024"]={title="Bulette",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 63\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 94 (9d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 21 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft., Tremorsense 120 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bulette makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h17 (2d12 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nDeadly Leap\n\nThe bulette spends 5 feet of movement to jump to a space within 15 feet that contains one or more Large or smaller creatures. dex 15, each creature in the bulette's destination space. actSaveFail 19 (3d12) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage, and the target is pushed 5 feet straight away from the bulette.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeap\n\nThe bulette jumps up to 30 feet by spending 10 feet of movement."},
  ["creature.bulette-pup.xmm2024"]={title="Bulette Pup",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 63\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 8 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 30 ft., Tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h14 (2d10 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeap\n\nThe bulette jumps up to 30 feet by spending 10 feet of movement."},
  ["creature.bulezau.mpmm2014"]={title="Bulezau",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 67\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (7d8 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 8 | WIS 9 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRotting Presence\n\nWhen any creature that isn't a demon starts its turn within 30 feet of the bulezau, that creature must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) necrotic damage.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe bulezau's long jump is up to 20 feet and its high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nSure-Footed\n\nThe bulezau has advantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws made against effects that would knock it prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBarbed Tail\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d12 + 2) piercing damage plus 4 (1d8) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against disease or become poisoned until the disease ends. While poisoned in this way, the target sports festering boils, coughs up flies, and sheds rotting skin, and the target must repeat the saving throw after every 24 hours that elapse. On a successful save, the disease ends. On a failed save, the target's hit point maximum is reduced by 4 (1d8). The target dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0."},
  ["creature.bulezau.mtf2014"]={title="Bulezau",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 131\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (7d8 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 8 | WIS 9 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRotting Presence\n\nWhen any creature that isn't a demon starts its turn within 30 feet one or more bulezaus, that creature must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 necrotic damage plus 1 necrotic damage for each bulezau within 30 feet of it.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe bulezau's long jump is up to 20 feet and its high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nSure-Footed\n\nThe bulezau has advantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws made against effects that would knock it prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBarbed Tail\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d12 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against disease or become poisoned until the disease ends. While poisoned in this way, the target sports festering boils, coughs up flies, and sheds rotting skin, and the target must repeat the saving throw after every 24 hours that elapse. On a successful save, the disease ends. On a failed save, the target's hit point maximum is reduced by 4 (1d8). The target dies if its hit point maximum is reduced to 0."},
  ["item.bullseye-lantern.phb2014"]={title="Bullseye Lantern",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA bullseye lantern casts bright light in a 60-foot cone and dim light for an additional 60 feet. Once lit, it burns for 6 hours on a flask (1 pint) of oil."},
  ["item.bullseye-lantern.xphb2024"]={title="Bullseye Lantern",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 226\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Bullseye Lantern burns Oil as fuel to cast XPHB in a 60-foot Cone and XPHB for an additional 60 feet."},
  ["species.bullywug.dmg2014"]={title="Bullywug",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nAmphibious\n\nYou can breathe air and water.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nYou can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when you speak in Bullywug.\n\nSwamp Camouflage\n\nYou have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in swampy terrain.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nYour long jump is up to 20 feet and your high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Bullywug."},
  ["creature.bullywug.mm2014"]={title="Bullywug",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Bullywug\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe bullywug can breathe air and water.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nThe bullywug can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when it speaks in Bullywug.\n\nSwamp Camouflage\n\nThe bullywug has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in swampy terrain.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe bullywug's long jump is up to 20 feet and its high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bullywug makes two melee attacks: one with its bite and one with its spear.\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage, or 5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["language.bullywug.mm2014"]={title="Bullywug",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 35"},
  ["language.bullywug.xmm2024"]={title="Bullywug",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 64"},
  ["creature.bullywug-bog-sage.xmm2024"]={title="Bullywug Bog Sage",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 64\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Bullywug, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe bullywug can breathe air and water.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nThe bullywug can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when it speaks in Bullywug.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bullywug makes two Bog Staff attacks. It can replace any attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nBog Staff\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) Poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeap\n\nThe bullywug can jump up to 30 feet by spending 10 feet of movement."},
  ["creature.bullywug-croaker.gos2014"]={title="Bullywug Croaker",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 7 | WIS 15 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Bullywug\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe croaker can breathe air and water.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nThe croaker can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when it speaks in Bullywug.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe croaker's long jump is up to 20 feet and its high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nSwamp Camouflage\n\nThe croaker has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in swampy terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nGlaaar-pat (3/Day)\n\nThe croaker sings a song of marshy doom. Each chosen creature within 30 feet of the croaker that can hear the song must make a 12 Wisdom saving throw, taking 9 (2d8) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that fails this saving throw also has disadvantage on Constitution saving throws until the end of its next turn.\n\nRooooo-glog (1/Day)\n\nThe croaker sings an ode to an elder froghemoth. Each bullywug within 30 feet of the croaker that can hear the song gains 10 temporary hit points."},
  ["creature.bullywug-knight.wbtw2014"]={title="Bullywug Knight",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 231\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 9 | WIS 11 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Bullywug, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe knight can breathe air and water.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nThe knight can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when it speaks in Bullywug.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe knight's long jump is up to 20 feet and its high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe knight makes two Glaive attacks.\n\nGlaive\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nCroak of Charming (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe knight makes a loud croak while targeting one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 12 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.bullywug-royal.gos2014"]={title="Bullywug Royal",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Bullywug\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe royal can breathe air and water.\n\nBrute\n\nA melee weapon deals one extra die of its damage when the royal hits with it (included in the attack).\n\nFrog Rider\n\nThe royal has advantage on melee attacks made while riding a frog mount.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nThe royal can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when it speaks in Bullywug.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe royal's long jump is up to 20 feet and its high jump is up to 10 feet, with or without a running start.\n\nSwamp Camouflage\n\nThe royal has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in swampy terrain.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe royal makes two attacks: one with its royal spear and one with its bite.\n\nRoyal Spear\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage, or 12 (2d8 + 3) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nCroaked Decree (1/Day)\n\nThe royal makes a loud pronouncement. Each bullywug within 60 feet of the royal that can hear the pronouncement has advantage on its next attack roll."},
  ["creature.bullywug-warrior.xmm2024"]={title="Bullywug Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 64\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Bullywug, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe bullywug can breathe air and water.\n\nSpeak with Frogs and Toads\n\nThe bullywug can communicate simple concepts to frogs and toads when it speaks in Bullywug.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nInsectile Rapier\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeap\n\nThe bullywug can jump up to 30 feet by spending 10 feet of movement."},
  ["feature.bulwark.scag2014.fighter.purple-dragon-knight-banneret.15"]={title="Bulwark",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\nBeginning at 15th level, you can extend the benefit of your Indomitable feature to an ally. When you decide to use Indomitable to reroll an Intelligence, a Wisdom, or a Charisma saving throw and you aren't incapacitated, you can choose one ally within 60 feet of you that also failed its saving throw against the same effect. If that creature can see or hear you, it can reroll its saving throw and must use the new roll."},
  ["feature.bulwark-of-force.tce2014.fighter.psi-warrior.15"]={title="Bulwark of Force",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.bulwark-of-force.xphb2024.fighter.psi-warrior.15"]={title="Bulwark of Force",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["item.bundle-of-sheet-music-representing-the-lost-dirges-of-a-famous-composer.xdmg2024"]={title="Bundle of sheet music representing the lost dirges of a famous composer",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.buppido.oota2014"]={title="Buppido",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.burglar-s-pack.phb2014"]={title="Burglar's Pack",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nIncludes:\n\n• a phb\n\n• a phb\n\n• 10 feet of string\n\n• a phb\n\n• 5 phb\n\n• a phb\n\n• a phb\n\n• 10 phb\n\n• a phb\n\n• 2 phb\n\n• 5 days phb\n\n• a phb\n\n• a phb\n\n• phb"},
  ["item.burglar-s-pack.xphb2024"]={title="Burglar's Pack",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Burglar's Pack contains the following items: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, 10 XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, 7 flasks of XPHB, 5 days of XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB."},
  ["creature.burney-the-barber.bgdia2014"]={title="Burney the Barber",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["traphazard.burning.xphb2024"]={title="Burning",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 362\n\nA burning creature or object takes 1d4 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns. As an action, you can extinguish fire on yourself by giving yourself the XPHB condition and rolling on the ground. The fire also goes out if it is doused, submerged, or suffocated."},
  ["spell.burning-hands.phb2014"]={title="Burning Hands",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\nAs you hold your hands with thumbs touching and fingers spread, a thin sheet of flames shoots forth from your outstretched fingertips. Each creature in a 15-foot cone must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 3d6 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nThe fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried."},
  ["spell.burning-hands.xphb2024"]={title="Burning Hands",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 248\n\nA thin sheet of flames shoots forth from you. Each creature in a 15-foot XPHB makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nFlammable objects in the XPHB that aren't being worn or carried start XPHB."},
  ["creature.burnished-hart.mot2014"]={title="Burnished Hart",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 3 | WIS 15 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands one language of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the hart moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with an antlers attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) fire damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nHeated Body\n\nA creature that touches the hart or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 5 (1d10) fire damage.\n\nSure-Footed\n\nThe hart has advantage on Strength and Dexterity saving throws made against effects that would knock it prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe hart makes two attacks: one with its antlers and one with its hooves.\n\nAntlers\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 2 (1d4) fire damage."},
  ["item.burnt-othur-fumes.dmg2014"]={title="Burnt Othur Fumes",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) poison damage, and must repeat the saving throw at the start of each of its turns. On each successive failed save, the character takes 3 (1d6) poison damage. After three successful saves, the poison ends."},
  ["item.burnt-othur-fumes.xdmg2024"]={title="Burnt Othur Fumes",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 90\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to Burnt Othur Fumes must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) Poison damage, and it must repeat the save at the start of each of its turns. On each successive failed save, the creature takes 3 (1d6) Poison damage. After three successful saves, the poison ends."},
  ["creature.burrowshark.pota2014"]={title="Burrowshark",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBond of the Black Earth\n\nThe burrowshark is magically bound to a bulette trained to serve as its mount. While mounted on its bulette, the burrowshark shares the bulette's senses and can ride the bulette while it burrows. The bonded bulette obeys the burrowshark's commands. If its mount dies, the burrowshark can train a new bulette to serve as its bonded mount, a process requiring a month.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe burrowshark makes three melee attacks.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUnyielding\n\nWhen the burrowshark is subjected to an effect that would move it, knock it prone, or both, it can use its reaction to be neither moved nor knocked prone."},
  ["optionalfeature.bursting-arrow.xge2024"]={title="Bursting Arrow",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 29\n\nYou imbue your arrow with force energy drawn from the school of evocation. The energy detonates after your attack. Immediately after the arrow hits the creature, the target and all other creatures within 10 feet of it take 2d6 force damage each.\n\nThe force damage increases to 4d6 when you reach 18th level in this class."},
  ["optionalfeature.bursting-shot.au2014"]={title="Bursting Shot",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou imbue your ammunition with explosive magical energy. Immediately after you deal damage to the creature, your target and each creature within a 10-foot XPHB originating from the target take Force damage equal to two rolls of your Arcane Shot Die."},
  ["creature.buster-the-bear.rmbre2014"]={title="Buster the Bear",subtitle="Criatura - RMBRE - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSurprise Attack\n\nIf Buster the Bear surprises a creature and hits it with an attack during the first round of combat, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) damage from the attack.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBashin' Banjo\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["magicitem.butcher-s-bib.egw2014"]={title="Butcher's Bib",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis black leather apron is perpetually covered by blood, even after being washed off. You gain the following benefits while wearing the apron:\n\n• Once per turn when you roll damage for a melee attack with a weapon, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice. If you do so, you must use the second total.\n\n• Your weapon attacks that deal slashing damage score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20."},
  ["creature.cackler.ggr2014"]={title="Cackler",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 195\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 10 (3d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 11 | WIS 7 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLast Laugh\n\nWhen the cackler dies, it releases a dying laugh that scars the minds of other nearby creatures. Each creature within 10 feet of the cackler must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or take 2 (1d4) psychic damage.\n\nMimicry\n\nThe cackler can mimic any sounds it has heard, including voices. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful 11 Wisdom (Insight) check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nSpiked Chain\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["spell.cacophonic-shield.frhof2014"]={title="Cacophonic Shield",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 143\n\nThunderous reverberations fill a 10-foot XPHB originating from you for the duration. Whenever the XPHB enters a creature's space and whenever a creature enters the XPHB or ends its turn there, the creature makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d6 Thunder damage and has the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. A creature makes this save only once per turn. When you cast this spell, you can designate creatures to be unaffected by it.\n\nIn addition, you have XPHB to Thunder damage, and ranged attack rolls against you are made with XPHB."},
  ["creature.cadaver-collector.mpmm2014"]={title="Cadaver Collector",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 189 (18d10 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 14 | CON 20 | INT 5 | WIS 11 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands all languages but can't speak\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe collector has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe collector doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe collector makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (3d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage.\n\nParalyzing Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe collector releases paralyzing gas in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a successful 18 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. A paralyzed creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself with a success.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSummon Specters (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe collector calls up the enslaved spirits of those it has slain; 1d4 specter (without Sunlight Sensitivity) arise in unoccupied spaces within 15 feet of it. The specters act right after the collector on the same initiative count and fight until they're destroyed. They disappear when the collector is destroyed."},
  ["creature.cadaver-collector.mtf2014"]={title="Cadaver Collector",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 189 (18d10 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 14 | CON 20 | INT 5 | WIS 11 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands all languages but can't speak\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe cadaver collector has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSummon Specters (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAs a bonus action, the cadaver collector calls up the enslaved spirits of those it has slain; 1d6 specter (without Sunlight Sensitivity) arise in unoccupied spaces within 15 feet of the cadaver collector. The specters act right after the cadaver collector on the same initiative count and fight until they're destroyed. They disappear when the cadaver collector is destroyed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cadaver collector makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (3d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage.\n\nParalyzing Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe cadaver collector releases paralyzing gas in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a successful 18 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. A paralyzed creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself with a success."},
  ["creature.cairnwight.bgg2014"]={title="Cairnwight",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, petrified\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cairnwight makes two Slam attacks or two Rock attacks, and it uses its Petrifying Touch if available.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 10 to hit, range 60/240 ft., one target. h19 (3d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nPetrifying Touch {@recharge 5}\n\nThe cairnwight touches one creature it can see within 10 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or take 26 (4d12) force damage and have the restrained condition as it begins to turn to stone. The affected target must repeat the saving throw at the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the effect ends on the target. On a failed save, the target has the petrified condition instead of the restrained condition."},
  ["creature.calcryx.tftyp2014"]={title="Calcryx",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 5 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales an icy blast of hail in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (5d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.caldron-magen.nf2014"]={title="Caldron Magen",subtitle="Criatura - NF - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Common plus two other languages but can't speak\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDisintegration\n\nIf the magen dies, it disintegrates into dust, leaving behind anything it was wearing or carrying.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe magen has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe magen makes two attacks, using Extended Fist or Acid Spittle in any combination.\n\nExtended Fist\n\nm 6, reach 15 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 5 (1d10) Acid damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from one of two fists.\n\nAcid Spittle\n\nr 6, range 60 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Acid damage."},
  ["traphazard.calim-sandstorm.fraif2014"]={title="Calim Sandstorm",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nSandstorms arise quickly in the Calim desert, scouring the flesh of those caught inside. A Calim sandstorm is typically at least 300 feet in diameter and lasts {@b 1d6 hours.\n\nThe area of a Calim sandstorm is XPHB, and open flames in the area are extinguished. A creature makes a 10 Constitution saving throw after each hour spent in a sandstorm's area. On a failed save, the creature gains 1 XPHB level."},
  ["magicitem.calimemnon-crystal.fraif2014"]={title="Calimemnon Crystal",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThis immaculately cut sixty-sided diamond fits in one hand, yet it contains an entire genie empire. The Calimemnon Crystal was made by high elf magic to imprison the notorious genie lords Calim and Memnon, who once ruled and warred over what is now Calimshan.\n\nWhen viewed by a creature with XPHB, the normally beautiful diamond is a grotesque sight: trapped within the gemstone are more than a hundred genies, including the physical forms of Calim and Memnon. The genies scream and strain in agonized fury, pressing their belligerent faces against the walls of their crystal line prison.\n\nProperties of the Crystal\n\nWhile attuned to the crystal, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Arcane Focus You can use the Calimemnon Crystal as an Arcane Focus.\n\n• Flight You have a XPHB of 30 feet and can hover.\n\n• Spells You can cast these spells with the crystal (spell save DC 18): XPHB, XPHB, XPHB (targeting yourself only), and XPHB.\n\nAura of Cold\n\nThe temperature drops precipitously in a 20-foot XPHB originating from the crystal. Whenever the XPHB enters a creature's space and whenever a creature enters the XPHB or ends its turn there, the creature takes (2d6) Cold damage. A creature takes this damage only once per turn. While attuned to the crystal, you are unaffected by the aura, and you can take a XPHB action to disable or enable the aura.\n\nHealing/Damage Rays\n\nWhile holding the crystal, you can take a XPHB action to fire six rays of volatile energy from the crystal at one or more creatures within 60 feet. You can aim the rays at one target or at several. For each ray, choose one of the following effects:\n\n• Damage Ray The target makes a DC 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking (6d6 + 6) Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• Healing Ray The target regains 2d6 + 2 XPHB. This property can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Artifact has the following random properties (see chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide):\n\n• 1 XDMG property\n\n• 1 XDMG property\n\n• 1 XDMG property\n\n• 1 XDMG property\n\nDestroying the Crystal\n\nThe Calimemnon Crystal is destroyed if the creature attuned to it casts the XPHB spell and wishes the crystal destroyed. Nothing else can harm it. When the crystal is destroyed, all the genies in the crystal are released."},
  ["spell.call-lightning.phb2014"]={title="Call Lightning",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\nA storm cloud appears in the shape of a cylinder that is 10 feet tall with a 60-foot radius, centered on a point you can see within range directly above you. The spell fails if you can't see a point in the air where the storm cloud could appear (for example, if you are in a room that can't accommodate the cloud).\n\nWhen you cast the spell, choose a point you can see under the cloud. A bolt of lightning flashes down from the cloud to that point. Each creature within 5 feet of that point must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 3d10 lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. On each of your turns until the spell ends, you can use your action to call down lightning in this way again, targeting the same point or a different one.\n\nIf you are outdoors in stormy conditions when you cast this spell, the spell gives you control over the existing storm instead of creating a new one. Under such conditions, the spell's damage increases by 1d10."},
  ["spell.call-lightning.xphb2024"]={title="Call Lightning",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 248\n\nA storm cloud appears at a point within range that you can see above yourself. It takes the shape of a XPHB that is 10 feet tall with a 60-foot radius.\n\nWhen you cast the spell, choose a point you can see under the cloud. A lightning bolt shoots from the cloud to that point. Each creature within 5 feet of that point makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d10 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nUntil the spell ends, you can take a XPHB action to call down lightning in that way again, targeting the same point or a different one.\n\nIf you're outdoors in a storm when you cast this spell, the spell gives you control over that storm instead of creating a new one. Under such conditions, the spell's damage increases by 1d10."},
  ["feature.call-the-hunt.tce2014.barbarian.beast.14"]={title="Call the Hunt",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["deity.callarduran-smoothhands.mtf2014"]={title="Callarduran Smoothhands",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nCallarduran became the patron of the deep gnomes when he led them into the Underdark and taught them how to survive, but all gnomes see him as the embodiment of the drive to know more, to examine everything more minutely-and thereby make great discoveries.\n\nCallarduran earned his moniker when, after stealing the heart of Ogrémoch, he rubbed his hands smooth as he polished the heart and turned it into a magical stone. The theft caused Ogrémoch to turn to evil, but it gave Callarduran the power to control earth elementals-which, it is said, he can confer to deep gnomes by rubbing the stone and saying their names."},
  ["deity.callarduran-smoothhands.scag2014"]={title="Callarduran Smoothhands",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 24"},
  ["item.calligrapher-s-supplies.phb2014"]={title="Calligrapher's Supplies",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nCalligraphy treats writing as a delicate, beautiful art. Calligraphers produce text that is pleasing to the eye, using a style that is difficult to forge. Their supplies also give them some ability to examine scripts and determine if they are legitimate, since a calligrapher's training involves long hours of studying writing and attempting to replicate its style and design.\n\nComponents\n\nCalligrapher's supplies include ink, a dozen sheets of parchment, and three quills.\n\nArcana\n\nAlthough calligraphy is of little help in deciphering the content of magical writings, proficiency with these supplies can aid in identifying who wrote a script of a magical nature.\n\nHistory\n\nThis tool proficiency can augment the benefit of successful checks made to analyze or investigate ancient writings, scrolls, or other texts, including runes etched in stone or messages in frescoes or other displays.\n\nDecipher Treasure Map\n\nThis tool proficiency grants you expertise in examining maps. You can make an Intelligence check to determine a map's age, whether a map includes any hidden messages, or similar facts.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nIdentify writer of nonmagical script | 10\n\nDetermine writer's state of mind | 15\n\nSpot forged text | 15\n\nForge a signature | 20"},
  ["item.calligrapher-s-supplies.xphb2024"]={title="Calligrapher's Supplies",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 220\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Dexterity\n\n• Utilize: Write text with impressive flourishes that guard against forgery (15)\n\n• Craft: XPHB, XDMG"},
  ["spell.calm-emotions.phb2014"]={title="Calm Emotions",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nYou attempt to suppress strong emotions in a group of people. Each humanoid in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on a point you choose within range must make a Charisma saving throw; a creature can choose to fail this saving throw if it wishes. If a creature fails its saving throw, choose one of the following two effects.\n\nYou can suppress any effect causing a target to be charmed or frightened. When this spell ends, any suppressed effect resumes, provided that its duration has not expired in the meantime.\n\nAlternatively, you can make a target indifferent about creatures of your choice that it is hostile toward. This indifference ends if the target is attacked or harmed by a spell or if it witnesses any of its friends being harmed. When the spell ends, the creature becomes hostile again, unless the DM rules otherwise."},
  ["spell.calm-emotions.xphb2024"]={title="Calm Emotions",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 249\n\nEach Humanoid in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point you choose within range must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be affected by one of the following effects (choose for each creature):\n\n• The creature has XPHB to the XPHB and XPHB conditions until the spell ends. If the creature was already XPHB or XPHB, those conditions are suppressed for the duration.\n\n• The creature becomes XPHB about creatures of your choice that it's XPHB toward. This indifference ends if the target takes damage or witnesses its allies taking damage. When the spell ends, the creature's attitude returns to normal."},
  ["item.caltrop.phb2014"]={title="Caltrop",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs an action, you can spread a single bag of caltrops to cover a 5-foot-square area. Any creature that enters the area must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or stop moving and take 1 piercing damage. Until the creature regains at least 1 hit point, its walking speed is reduced by 10 feet. A creature moving through the area at half speed doesn't need to make the saving throw."},
  ["item.caltrops.xphb2024"]={title="Caltrops",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can spread Caltrops from their bag to cover a 5-foot-square area within 5 feet of yourself. A creature that enters this area for the first time on a turn must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 1 Piercing damage and have its XPHB reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. It takes 10 minutes to recover the Caltrops."},
  ["item.caltrops-bag-of-20.phb2014"]={title="Caltrops (bag of 20)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs an action, you can spread a single bag of caltrops to cover a 5-foot-square area. Any creature that enters the area must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or stop moving and take 1 piercing damage. Until the creature regains at least 1 hit point, its walking speed is reduced by 10 feet. A creature moving through the area at half speed doesn't need to make the saving throw."},
  ["creature.cambion.mm2014"]={title="Cambion",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning, poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFiendish Blessing\n\nThe AC of the cambion includes its Charisma bonus.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cambion makes two melee attacks or uses its Fire Ray twice.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 3 (1d6) fire damage.\n\nFire Ray\n\nrs 7 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) fire damage.\n\nFiendish Charm\n\nOne humanoid the cambion can see within 30 feet of it must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be magically charmed for 1 day. The charmed target obeys the cambion's spoken commands. If the target suffers any harm from the cambion or another creature or receives a suicidal command from the cambion, the target can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a target's saving throw is successful, or if the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the cambion's Fiendish Charm for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.cambion.xmm2024"]={title="Cambion",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 65\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 105 (14d8 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cambion makes two attacks, using Claw or Fire Ray in any combination.\n\nClaw\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage.\n\nFire Ray\n\nr 7, range 120 ft. h13 (3d6 + 3) Fire damage."},
  ["creature.camel.mm2014"]={title="Camel",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 320\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 15 (2d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.camel.phb2014"]={title="Camel",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.camel.xmm2024"]={title="Camel",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 351\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 17 (2d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 8 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 11 | CHA 5\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.camel.xphb2024"]={title="Camel",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.camlash.veor2014"]={title="Camlash",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 19\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 325 (26d12 + 156)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 15 | CON 22 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nCamlash explodes when reduced to 0 hit points, and each creature within 30 feet of Camlash must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 70 (20d6) fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. The explosion ignites flammable objects in that area that aren't being worn or carried.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nCamlash has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpider Aura\n\nCamlash is surrounded by tiny biting spiders that magically appear and disappear from moment to moment. At the start of each of Camlash's turns, each creature within 10 feet of Camlash takes 10 (3d6) poison damage and must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw or have the paralyzed condition until the start of Camlash's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nCamlash makes one Flaming Whip attack and one Lightning Blade attack. Camlash can replace one of these attacks with Teleport.\n\nFlaming Whip\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h25 (5d6 + 8) fire damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 21 Strength saving throw or be pulled up to 25 feet toward Camlash.\n\nLightning Blade\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (3d8 + 8) slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) lightning damage.\n\nTeleport\n\nCamlash magically teleports, along with any equipment she is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space she can see."},
  ["creature.campestri.wbtw2014"]={title="Campestri",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 232\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 2 (1d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 7 | CON 10 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: tremorsense 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but speaks only through the use of its Mimicry trait\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMimicry\n\nThe campestri can mimic any voice or song it has heard, albeit in a nasal falsetto.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHead Butt\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 bludgeoning damage.\n\nSpores (1/Day)\n\nA 5-foot radius of spores extends from the campestri. These spores can go around corners, and they have no effect on Constructs, Elementals, Plants, or Undead. Each other creature in the area must make a 10 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is incapacitated and its speed is halved, both for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["item.candle.phb2014"]={title="Candle",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nFor 1 hour, a candle sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet."},
  ["item.candle.xphb2024"]={title="Candle",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nFor 1 hour, a lit Candle sheds XPHB in a 5-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 5 feet."},
  ["magicitem.candle-mace.bgdia2014"]={title="Candle Mace",subtitle="Item Magico - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The head of this mace sheds bright light in a 5-foot-radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet. When you wield this mace, you can extinguish or ignite its light as an action."},
  ["magicitem.candle-of-invocation.dmg2014"]={title="Candle of Invocation",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis slender taper is dedicated to a deity and shares that deity's alignment. The candle's alignment can be detected with the detect evil and good spell. The DM chooses the god and associated alignment or determines the alignment randomly.\n\nd20 | Alignment\n\n1-2 | Chaotic evil\n\n3-4 | Chaotic neutral\n\n5-7 | Chaotic good\n\n8-9 | Neutral evil\n\n10-11 | Neutral\n\n12-13 | Neutral good\n\n14-15 | Lawful evil\n\n16-17 | Lawful neutral\n\n18-20 | Lawful good\n\nThe candle's magic is activated when the candle is lit, which requires an action. After burning for 4 hours, the candle is destroyed. You can snuff it out early for use at a later time. Deduct the time it burned in increments of 1 minute from the candle's total burn time.\n\nWhile lit, the candle sheds dim light in a 30-foot radius. Any creature within that light whose alignment matches that of the candle makes attack rolls, saving throws, and ability checks with advantage. In addition, a cleric or druid in the light whose alignment matches the candle's can cast 1st-level spells he or she has prepared without expending spell slots, though the spell's effect is as if cast with a 1st-level slot.\n\nAlternatively, when you light the candle for the first time, you can cast the gate spell with it. Doing so destroys the candle."},
  ["magicitem.candle-of-invocation.xdmg2024"]={title="Candle of Invocation",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis candle's magic is activated when the candle is lit, which requires a XPHB action. After burning for 4 hours, the candle is destroyed. You can snuff it out early for use at a later time. Deduct the time it burned in increments of 1 minute from its total burn time.\n\nWhile lit, the candle sheds XPHB in a 30-foot radius. While you are within that light, you have XPHB on XPHB. In addition, a Cleric or Druid in the light can cast level 1 spells they have prepared without expending spell slots.\n\nAlternatively, when you light the candle for the first time, you can cast XPHB with it. Doing so destroys the candle. The portal created by the spell links to a particular Outer Plane chosen by the DM or determined by rolling on the following table.\n\n1d100 | Outer Plane\n\n01-05 | XDMG\n\n06-10 | XDMG\n\n11-17 | XDMG\n\n18-25 | XDMG\n\n26-33 | XDMG\n\n34-41 | XDMG\n\n42-46 | XDMG\n\n47-54 | XDMG\n\n55-59 | XDMG\n\n60-64 | XDMG\n\n65-69 | XDMG\n\n70-77 | XDMG\n\n78-85 | XDMG\n\n86-90 | XDMG\n\n91-95 | XDMG\n\n96-00 | XDMG"},
  ["magicitem.candle-of-the-deep.xdmg2024"]={title="Candle of the Deep",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThe flame of this candle isn't extinguished when immersed in water. It gives off light and heat like a normal candle."},
  ["magicitem.candle-of-the-deep.xge2024"]={title="Candle of the Deep",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 136\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThe flame of this candle is not extinguished when immersed in water. It gives off light and heat like a normal candle."},
  ["magicitem.canian-fork.coa2014"]={title="Canian Fork",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou have a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one additional attack with it as a bonus action on each of your turns.\n\nCurse\n\nYou're unwilling to part with this weapon while attuned to it. You're also vulnerable to radiant damage and each time you receive magical healing, you must make a 15 Constitution saving throw.\n\nOn a failed save, the healing has no effect. Only the Remove Curse spell allows you to end attunement to this item.\n\nCorrupting\n\nThis item corrupts. See the \"CoA\" section."},
  ["creature.cannith-artificer.efa2014"]={title="Cannith Artificer",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 71 (11d8 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 18 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe artificer makes two attacks, using Battering Mace or Artillery Strike in any combination.\n\nBattering Mace\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h14 (3d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nArtillery Strike\n\nr 6, range 120 ft. h22 (4d8 + 4) Force damage."},
  ["object.cannon.dmg2014"]={title="Cannon",subtitle="Objeto - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 255\n\nA cannon uses gunpowder to propel heavy balls of cast iron through the air at destructive speeds. In a campaign without gunpowder, a cannon might be an arcane device built by clever gnomes or wizardly engineers.\n\nA cannon is usually supported in a wooden frame with wheels. Before it can be fired, the cannon must be loaded and aimed. It takes one action to load the weapon, one action to aim it, and one action to fire it."},
  ["object.cannon.xdmg2024"]={title="Cannon",subtitle="Objeto - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 96\n\nA Cannon uses gunpowder or arcane power to propel heavy iron balls at destructive speeds. A Cannon is usually attached to a wooden frame with wheels. Loading a Cannon requires the XPHB action, and aiming it requires another XPHB action. Then a crew member can take the Cannonball action."},
  ["item.canoe.toa2014"]={title="Canoe",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA canoe can be purchased in Port Nyanzaru for 50 gp. It holds up to six Medium creatures and has a maximum speed of 2 mph. It is otherwise identical to a rowboat."},
  ["creature.canoloth.mpmm2014"]={title="Canoloth",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 120 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 17 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDimensional Lock\n\nOther creatures can't teleport to or from a space within 60 feet of the canoloth. Any attempt to do so is wasted.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe canoloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nUncanny Senses\n\nThe canoloth can't be surprised unless it's incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe canoloth makes one Bite or Tongue attack and one Claw attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) force damage.\n\nTongue\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) acid damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 15), pulled up to 30 feet toward the canoloth, and restrained until the grapple ends. The canoloth can grapple one target at a time with its tongue."},
  ["creature.canoloth.mtf2014"]={title="Canoloth",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 120 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 17 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Infernal, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDimensional Lock\n\nOther creatures can't teleport to or from a space within 60 feet of the canoloth. Any attempt to do so is wasted.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe canoloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe canoloth's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nUncanny Senses\n\nThe canoloth can't be surprised while it isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe canoloth makes two attacks: one with its tongue or its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h25 (6d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nTongue\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 30 ft., one target. h17 (2d12 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 15), pulled up to 30 feet toward the canoloth, and is restrained until the grapple ends. The canoloth can grapple one target at a time with its tongue."},
  ["creature.canopic-golem.cm2014"]={title="Canopic Golem",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 252 (24d10 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 7 | WIS 11 | CHA 1\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLimited Spell Immunity\n\nThe golem automatically succeeds on saving throws against spells of 7th level or lower, and the attack rolls of such spells always miss it.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe golem doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes two attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h27 (4d10 + 5) force damage.\n\nCrystal Dart\n\nrw 10 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) force damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSpell Deflection\n\nIn response to a spell attack missing the golem, it causes that spell to hit another creature within 120 feet of it that it can see."},
  ["feature.cantrip-formulas.tce2014.wizard.base.3"]={title="Cantrip Formulas",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 75\n\n{@i 3rd-level wizard tce\n\nYou have scribed a set of arcane formulas in your spellbook that you can use to formulate a cantrip in your mind. Whenever you finish a long rest and consult those formulas in your spellbook, you can replace one wizard cantrip you know with another cantrip from the wizard spell list."},
  ["feature.cantrip-versatility.tce2014.cleric.base.4"]={title="Cantrip Versatility",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n{@i 4th-level cleric tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can replace one cantrip you learned from this class's Spellcasting feature with another cantrip from the spells."},
  ["feature.cantrip-versatility.tce2014.druid.base.4"]={title="Cantrip Versatility",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n{@i 4th-level druid tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can replace one cantrip you learned from this class's Spellcasting feature with another cantrip from the spells."},
  ["item.canvas-1-sq-yd.phb2014"]={title="Canvas (1 sq. yd.)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.canvas-1-sq-yd.xdmg2024"]={title="Canvas (1 sq. yd.)",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.cap-of-vanishing.wtthc2014"]={title="Cap of Vanishing",subtitle="Item Magico - WttHC - 2014",body="Raridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis cap has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the cap, you can take a XPHB action and expend 1 charge to give yourself the XPHB condition for 10 minutes. The effect ends early if the hat is removed, or immediately after you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell."},
  ["magicitem.cap-of-water-breathing.dmg2014"]={title="Cap of Water Breathing",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this cap underwater, you can speak its command word as an action to create a bubble of air around your head. It allows you to breathe normally underwater. This bubble stays with you until you speak the command word again, the cap is removed, or you are no longer underwater."},
  ["magicitem.cap-of-water-breathing.xdmg2024"]={title="Cap of Water Breathing",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this cap underwater, you can take a XPHB action to create a bubble of air around your head. This bubble allows you to breathe normally underwater. This bubble stays with you until the cap is removed or you are no longer underwater.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.cape-of-enlargement.pabtso2014"]={title="Cape of Enlargement",subtitle="Item Magico - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nAncient runes are stitched in silver thread along the hem of this grayish-purple cape.\n\nThe cape has 3 charges. As a bonus action while wearing the cape, you can expend 1 of its charges to enlarge yourself, granting yourself the following benefits:\n\n• Your size increases by one category—from Medium to Large, for example. If there isn't enough room for your size to increase by one category, you instead become the maximum possible size in the space available.\n\n• You have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\n\n• When you hit with an attack roll using a weapon or an unarmed strike, you can add your proficiency bonus to the attack's damage.\n\nThese benefits last for 10 minutes or until you use another bonus action to dismiss them. The cape regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["magicitem.cape-of-the-mountebank.dmg2014"]={title="Cape of the Mountebank",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis cape smells faintly of brimstone. While wearing it, you can use it to cast the dimension door spell as an action. This property of the cape can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nWhen you disappear, you leave behind a cloud of smoke, and you appear in a similar cloud of smoke at your destination. The smoke lightly obscures the space you left and the space you appear in, and it dissipates at the end of your next turn. A light or stronger wind disperses the smoke."},
  ["magicitem.cape-of-the-mountebank.xdmg2024"]={title="Cape of the Mountebank",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis cape smells faintly of brimstone. While wearing it, you can use it to cast XPHB as a XPHB action. This property can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nWhen you teleport with that spell, you leave behind a cloud of smoke. The space you left is XPHB by that smoke until the end of your next turn."},
  ["object.captain-a-hole.rmbre2014"]={title="Captain A-Hole",subtitle="Objeto - RMBRE - 2014",body="Pagina: 21"},
  ["creature.captain-hask.dsotdq2014"]={title="Captain Hask",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 148\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.captain-n-ghathrod.wdmm2014"]={title="Captain N'ghathrod",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 111 (13d8 + 13)"},
  ["creature.captain-othelstan.hotdq2014"]={title="Captain Othelstan",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAction Surge (Recharges on a Short or Long Rest)\n\nOn his turn, Othelstan can take one additional action.\n\nTiamat's Blessing of Retribution\n\nWhen Othelstan takes damage that reduces him to 0 hit points, he immediately regains 20 hit points. If he has 20 hit points or fewer at the end of his next turn, he dies.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nOthelstan attacks twice with his flail or spear, or makes two ranged attacks with his spears.\n\nFlail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or ranged 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.captain-xendros.gos2014"]={title="Captain Xendros",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.caradoc.dsotdq2014"]={title="Caradoc",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 110 (20d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 1 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 15 | WIS 13 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Solamnic\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBound Haunting\n\nCaradoc's spirit is bound to Dargaard Keep. At the start of his turn, if he's outside the keep's walls and not possessing a creature using his Possession action, he must succeed on a 15 Charisma saving throw or vanish and reappear in an unoccupied space within the keep.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nCaradoc can move through other creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain. He takes 5 (1d10) force damage if he ends his turn inside an object.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf Caradoc dies, he reforms within Dargaard Keep in 2d6 days.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nCaradoc doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nCaradoc makes two Withering Touch attacks.\n\nWithering Touch\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) necrotic damage.\n\nPossession {@recharge 5}\n\nOne Humanoid that Caradoc can see within 5 feet of himself must succeed on a 15 Charisma saving throw or be possessed by him; he then disappears, and the target is incapacitated and loses control of its body. Caradoc now controls the body but doesn't deprive the target of awareness. Caradoc can't be targeted by any attack, spell, or other effect, except ones that turn Undead, and he retains his alignment, Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma, immunity to being charmed and frightened, and his Divisive Whispers bonus action. He otherwise uses the possessed target's statistics but doesn't gain access to the target's knowledge, class features, or proficiencies.\n\nThe possession lasts until the body drops to 0 hit points, Caradoc ends it as a bonus action, or he is turned or forced out by an effect like the dispel evil and good spell. When the possession ends, Caradoc reappears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the body. The target is immune to Caradoc's Possession for 24 hours after succeeding on the saving throw or after the possession ends.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDivisive Whispers\n\nCaradoc magically whispers to one creature within 60 feet of himself. The target must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw, or the target must immediately use its reaction to make a melee attack against another creature of Caradoc's choice (wasting its reaction if there are no other creatures within reach)."},
  ["magicitem.card-sharp-s-deck.bmt2014"]={title="Card Sharp's Deck",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThe cards of this deck shimmer around the edges. While holding this deck, you can use the following properties:\n\n• Deadly Deal As an action, you can use this deck to make a ranged spell attack by throwing a spectral card and using Dexterity for the attack roll. The card has a range of 120 feet and deals 1d8 force damage on a hit.\n\n• Spray of Cards As an action, you can shuffle the deck and cast the BMT spell at 3rd level from the deck (spell save 15). Once the deck has cast the spell, it can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["optionalfeature.careful-spell.phb2014"]={title="Careful Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\nWhen you cast a spell that forces other creatures to make a saving throw, you can protect some of those creatures from the spell's full force. To do so, you spend 1 sorcery point and choose a number of those creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). A chosen creature automatically succeeds on its saving throw against the spell."},
  ["optionalfeature.careful-spell.xphb2024"]={title="Careful Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 141\n\nWhen you cast a spell that forces other creatures to make a saving throw, you can protect some of those creatures from the spell's full force. To do so, spend 1 Sorcery Point and choose a number of those creatures up to your Charisma modifier (minimum of one creature). A chosen creature automatically succeeds on its saving throw against the spell, and it takes no damage if it would normally take half damage on a successful save."},
  ["item.carnelian.dmg2014"]={title="Carnelian",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque orange to red-brown gemstone."},
  ["item.carnelian.xdmg2024"]={title="Carnelian",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA orange to red brown gemstone."},
  ["creature.carnivorous-flower.rot2014"]={title="Carnivorous Flower",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 67\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0"},
  ["background.carouser.abh2014"]={title="Carouser",subtitle="Background - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 6\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["item.carpenter-s-tools.phb2014"]={title="Carpenter's Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSkill at carpentry enables a character to construct wooden structures. A carpenter can build a house, a shack, a wooden cabinet, or similar items.\n\nComponents\n\nCarpenter's tools include a saw, a hammer, nails, a hatchet, a square, a ruler, an adze, a plane, and a chisel.\n\nHistory\n\nThis tool proficiency aids you in identifying the use and the origin of wooden buildings and other large wooden objects.\n\nInvestigation\n\nYou gain additional insight when inspecting areas within wooden structures, because you know tricks of construction that can conceal areas from discovery.\n\nPerception\n\nYou can spot irregularities in wooden walls or floors, making it easier to find trap doors and secret passages.\n\nStealth\n\nYou can quickly assess the weak spots in a wooden floor, making it easier to avoid the places that creak and groan when they're stepped on.\n\nFortify\n\nWith 1 minute of work and raw materials, you can make a door or window harder to force open. Increase the DC needed to open it by 5.\n\nTemporary Shelter\n\nAs part of a long rest, you can construct a lean-to or a similar shelter to keep your group dry and in the shade for the duration of the rest. Because it was fashioned quickly from whatever wood was available, the shelter collapses 1d3 days after being assembled.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nBuild a simple wooden structure | 10\n\nDesign a complex wooden structure | 15\n\nFind a weak point in a wooden wall | 15\n\nPry apart a door | 20"},
  ["item.carpenter-s-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Carpenter's Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 220\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Strength\n\n• Utilize: Seal or pry open a door or container (20)\n\n• Craft: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-3-ft-5-ft.dmg2014"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 3 ft. × 5 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can speak the carpet's command word as an action to make the carpet hover and fly. It moves according to your spoken directions, provided that you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 3 ft. × 5 ft. carpet can carry up to 200 lb. at a fly speed of 80 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice this weight, but it flies at half speed if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-3-ft-5-ft.xdmg2024"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 3 ft. × 5 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can make this carpet hover and fly by taking a XPHB action and using the carpet's command word. It moves according to your directions if you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 3 ft. × 5 ft. carpet can carry up to 200 lb. at a fly speed of 80 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice the weight shown on the table, but its XPHB is halved if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-4-ft-6-ft.dmg2014"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 4 ft. × 6 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can speak the carpet's command word as an action to make the carpet hover and fly. It moves according to your spoken directions, provided that you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 4 ft. × 6 ft. carpet can carry up to 400 lb. at a fly speed of 60 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice this weight, but it flies at half speed if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-4-ft-6-ft.xdmg2024"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 4 ft. × 6 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can make this carpet hover and fly by taking a XPHB action and using the carpet's command word. It moves according to your directions if you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 4 ft. × 6 ft. carpet can carry up to 400 lb. at a fly speed of 60 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice the weight shown on the table, but its XPHB is halved if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-5-ft-7-ft.dmg2014"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 5 ft. × 7 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can speak the carpet's command word as an action to make the carpet hover and fly. It moves according to your spoken directions, provided that you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 5 ft. × 7 ft. carpet can carry up to 600 lb. at a fly speed of 40 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice this weight, but it flies at half speed if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-5-ft-7-ft.xdmg2024"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 5 ft. × 7 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can make this carpet hover and fly by taking a XPHB action and using the carpet's command word. It moves according to your directions if you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 5 ft. × 7 ft. carpet can carry up to 600 lb. at a fly speed of 40 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice the weight shown on the table, but its XPHB is halved if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-6-ft-9-ft.dmg2014"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 6 ft. × 9 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can speak the carpet's command word as an action to make the carpet hover and fly. It moves according to your spoken directions, provided that you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 6 ft. × 9 ft. carpet can carry up to 800 lb. at a fly speed of 30 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice this weight, but it flies at half speed if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
  ["magicitem.carpet-of-flying-6-ft-9-ft.xdmg2024"]={title="Carpet of Flying, 6 ft. × 9 ft.",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou can make this carpet hover and fly by taking a XPHB action and using the carpet's command word. It moves according to your directions if you are within 30 feet of it.\n\nA 6 ft. × 9 ft. carpet can carry up to 800 lb. at a fly speed of 30 feet. A carpet can carry up to twice the weight shown on the table, but its XPHB is halved if it carries more than its normal capacity."},
