  ["item.carved-wooden-harp-with-ivory-inlay-and-zircon-gems.xdmg2024"]={title="Carved wooden harp with ivory inlay and zircon gems",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.cassiok-shadowdusk.wdmm2014"]={title="Cassiok Shadowdusk",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 287\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration\n\nCA: 14/17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech, Infernal, Undercommon\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["actionref.cast-a-spell.phb2014"]={title="Cast a Spell",subtitle="Acao - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nSpellcasters such as wizards and clerics, as well as many monsters, have access to spells and can use them to great effect in combat. Each spell has a casting time, which specifies whether the caster must use an action, a reaction, minutes, or even hours to cast the spell. Casting a spell is, therefore, not necessarily an action. Most spells do have a casting time of 1 action, so a spellcaster often uses his or her action in combat to cast such a spell. See phb for the rules on spellcasting."},
  ["creature.cat.mm2014"]={title="Cat",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 320\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 2 (1d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe cat has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 slashing damage."},
  ["creature.cat.xmm2024"]={title="Cat",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 351\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 2 (1d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nJumper\n\nThe cat's jump distance is determined using its Dexterity rather than its Strength.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScratch\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h1 Slashing damage."},
  ["creature.cat-skeleton.cos2014"]={title="Cat Skeleton",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 109\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.catapult.xge2024"]={title="Catapult",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 150\n\nChoose one object weighing 1 to 5 pounds within range that isn't being worn or carried. The object flies in a straight line up to 90 feet in a direction you choose before falling to the ground, stopping early if it impacts against a solid surface. If the object would strike a creature, that creature must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the object strikes the target and stops moving. When the object strikes something, the object and what it strikes each take 3d8 bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.catapult-munition.scc2014"]={title="Catapult Munition",subtitle="Item - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nA catapult munition roughly the size and weight of a cannonball.\n\nThe munition can be thrown up to 30 feet and explodes on impact. Any creature within a 15-foot-radius sphere centered on the point of impact must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 35 (10d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. In addition, each object in that area that isn't being worn or carried takes 35 (10d6) fire damage."},
  ["creature.category-1-krasis.ggr2014"]={title="Category 1 Krasis",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe krasis can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe krasis makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.category-2-krasis.ggr2014"]={title="Category 2 Krasis",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 136 (16d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe krasis can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe krasis makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h17 (2d12 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d12 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.category-3-krasis.ggr2014"]={title="Category 3 Krasis",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 287 (25d12 + 125)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe krasis can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe krasis makes three attacks: one with its bite, one with its claws, and one with its tail.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h27 (6d6 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h33 (6d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 19 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["spell.catnap.au2014"]={title="Catnap",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nYou make a calming gesture, and up to three willing creatures of your choice that you can see within range have the XPHB condition for the spell's duration. The spell ends on a target if it takes damage or another creature takes an action to shake it awake. If a target has the XPHB condition from this spell for the full duration, that target gains the benefits of finishing a XPHB, and it can't be affected by this spell again until it finishes a XPHB."},
  ["spell.catnap.xge2024"]={title="Catnap",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 151\n\nYou make a calming gesture, and up to three willing creatures of your choice that you can see within range fall unconscious for the spell's duration. The spell ends on a target early if it takes damage or someone uses an action to shake or slap it awake. If a target remains unconscious for the full duration, that target gains the benefit of a short rest, and it can't be affected by this spell again until it finishes a long rest."},
  ["creature.catoblepas.mpmm2014"]={title="Catoblepas",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 70\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 84 (8d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nStench\n\nAny creature other than a catoblepas that starts its turn within 10 feet of the catoblepas must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of the creature's next turn. On a successful saving throw, the creature is immune to the Stench of any catoblepas for 1 hour.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (5d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the start of the catoblepas's next turn.\n\nDeath Ray {@recharge 5}\n\nThe catoblepas targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the target instead takes 64 necrotic damage. The target dies if reduced to 0 hit points by this ray."},
  ["creature.catoblepas.vgm2014"]={title="Catoblepas",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 84 (8d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 12 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe catoblepas has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nStench\n\nAny creature other than a catoblepas that starts its turn within 10 feet of the catoblepas must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of the creature's next turn. On a successful saving throw, the creature is immune to the stench of any catoblepas for 1 hour.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h21 (5d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the start of the catoblepas's next turn.\n\nDeath Ray {@recharge 5}\n\nThe catoblepas targets a creature that it can see within 30 feet of it. The target must make a 16 Constitution saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the target instead takes 64 necrotic damage. The target dies if reduced to 0 hit points by this ray."},
  ["magicitem.cauldron-of-plenty.idrotf2014"]={title="Cauldron of Plenty",subtitle="Item Magico - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 314\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis cauldron is made of thick copper that has turned green with age. It is 4 feet wide, has a mouth 3½ feet in diameter, weighs 50 pounds, and can hold up to 30 gallons of liquid. Embossed on its bulging sides are images of satyrs and nymphs in repose, holding ladles. The cauldron comes with a lid and has side handles. It sits on five little clawed feet that keep it from tipping.\n\nIf water is poured into the cauldron and stirred for 1 minute, it transforms into a hearty, hot stew, which can provide one nourishing meal for up to four people per gallon. The stew remains hot while in the cauldron, then cools naturally after it is removed. The outside of the cauldron remains safe to touch despite the heat of the stew.\n\nThe cauldron can create stew three times. It then ceases to function until the next dawn, when it regains all its uses."},
  ["magicitem.cauldron-of-rebirth.tce2014"]={title="Cauldron of Rebirth",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis Tiny pot bears relief scenes of heroes on its cast iron sides. You can use the cauldron as a spellcasting focus for your spells, and it functions as a suitable component for the scrying spell. When you finish a long rest, you can use the cauldron to create a potion of greater healing. The potion lasts for 24 hours, then loses its magic if not consumed.\n\nAs an action, you can cause the cauldron to grow large enough for a Medium creature to crouch within. You can revert the cauldron to its normal size as an action, harmlessly shunting anything that can't fit inside to the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nIf you place the corpse of a humanoid into the cauldron and cover the corpse with 200 pounds of salt (which costs 10 gp) for at least 8 hours, the salt is consumed and the creature returns to life as if by raise dead at the next dawn. Once used, this property can't be used again for 7 days."},
  ["magicitem.cauldron-of-rebirth.xdmg2024"]={title="Cauldron of Rebirth",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 243\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis Tiny pot bears relief scenes of heroes on its cast-iron sides.\n\nYou can use the cauldron as a XPHB for your spells, and it functions as a suitable component for the XPHB spell.\n\nBrew Potion\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you can use the cauldron to create a XDMG, which takes 1 minute. The potion lasts for 24 hours, then loses its magic if not consumed.\n\nRaise Dead\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can cause the cauldron to grow large enough for a Medium creature to crouch within. You can revert the cauldron to its normal size as a XPHB action, harmlessly shunting anything that can't fit inside to the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nIf you place the corpse of a Humanoid into the cauldron and cover the corpse with 200 pounds of salt (which costs 10 GP) for at least 8 hours, the salt is consumed and the creature returns to life as if by XPHB at the next dawn. Once used, this property can't be used again for 7 days."},
  ["spell.cause-fear.xge2024"]={title="Cause Fear",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 151\n\nYou awaken the sense of mortality in one creature you can see within range. A construct or an undead is immune to this effect. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of you until the spell ends. The frightened target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.caustic-crawler.psz2014"]={title="Caustic Crawler",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.cauterizing-flames.tce2014.druid.wildfire.10"]={title="Cauterizing Flames",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n10th-level Circle of Wildfire feature\n\nYou gain the ability to turn death into magical flames that can heal or incinerate. When a Small or larger creature dies within 30 feet of you or your wildfire spirit, a harmless spectral flame springs forth in the dead creature's space and flickers there for 1 minute. When a creature you can see enters that space, you can use your reaction to extinguish the spectral flame there and either heal the creature or deal fire damage to it. The healing or damage equals 2d10 + your Wisdom modifier.\n\nYou can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["subclass.cavalier.xge2024.fighter.cavalier.0"]={title="Cavalier",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nPagina: 30\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, History, Insight, Performance, or Persuasion. Alternatively, you learn one language of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Born to the Saddle\n\nPagina: 30\n\nStarting at 3rd level, your mastery as a rider becomes apparent. You have advantage on saving throws made to avoid falling off your mount. If you fall off your mount and descend no more than 10 feet, you can land on your feet if you're not incapacitated.\n\nFinally, mounting or dismounting a creature costs you only 5 feet of movement, rather than half your speed.\n\nNivel 3 - Cavalier\n\nPagina: 30\n\nThe archetypal Cavalier excels at mounted combat. Usually born among the nobility and raised at court, a Cavalier is equally at home leading a cavalry charge or exchanging repartee at a state dinner. Cavaliers also learn how to guard those in their charge from harm, often serving as the protectors of their superiors and of the weak. Compelled to right wrongs or earn prestige, many of these fighters leave their lives of comfort to embark on glorious adventure.\n\nNivel 3 - Unwavering Mark\n\nPagina: 30\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can menace your foes, foiling their attacks and punishing them for harming others. When you hit a creature with a melee weapon attack, you can mark the creature until the end of your next turn. This effect ends early if you are incapacitated or you die, or if someone else marks the creature.\n\nWhile it is within 5 feet of you, a creature marked by you has disadvantage on any attack roll that doesn't target you.\n\nIn addition, if a creature marked by you deals damage to anyone other than you, you can make a special melee weapon attack against the marked creature as a bonus action on your next turn. You have advantage on the attack roll, and if it hits, the attack's weapon deals extra damage to the target equal to half your fighter level.\n\nRegardless of the number of creatures you mark, you can make this special attack a number of times equal to your Strength modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 7 - Warding Maneuver\n\nPagina: 30\n\nAt 7th level, you learn to fend off strikes directed at you, your mount, or other creatures nearby. If you or a creature you can see within 5 feet of you is hit by an attack, you can roll 1d8 as a reaction if you're wielding a melee weapon or a shield. Roll the die, and add the number rolled to the target's AC against that attack. If the attack still hits, the target has resistance against the attack's damage.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 10 - Hold the Line\n\nPagina: 30\n\nAt 10th level, you become a master of locking down your enemies. Creatures provoke an opportunity attack from you when they move 5 feet or more while within your reach, and if you hit a creature with an opportunity attack, the target's speed is reduced to 0 until the end of the current turn.\n\nNivel 15 - Ferocious Charger\n\nPagina: 30\n\nStarting at 15th level, you can run down your foes, whether you're mounted or not. If you move at least 10 feet in a straight line right before attacking a creature and you hit it with the attack, that target must succeed on a Strength saving throw (8 + your proficiency bonus + your Strength modifier) or be knocked prone. You can use this feature only once on each of your turns.\n\nNivel 18 - Vigilant Defender\n\nPagina: 30\n\nStarting at 18th level, you respond to danger with extraordinary vigilance. In combat, you get a special reaction that you can take once on every creature's turn, except your turn. You can use this special reaction only to make an opportunity attack, and you can't use it on the same turn that you take your normal reaction."},
  ["feature.cavalier.xge2024.fighter.cavalier.3"]={title="Cavalier",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 30\n\nThe archetypal Cavalier excels at mounted combat. Usually born among the nobility and raised at court, a Cavalier is equally at home leading a cavalry charge or exchanging repartee at a state dinner. Cavaliers also learn how to guard those in their charge from harm, often serving as the protectors of their superiors and of the weak. Compelled to right wrongs or earn prestige, many of these fighters leave their lives of comfort to embark on glorious adventure."},
  ["creature.cave-badger.oota2014"]={title="Cave Badger",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 96\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 12\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft., tremorsense 60 ft."},
  ["creature.cave-bear.mm2014"]={title="Cave Bear",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 334\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 42 (5d10 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe bear has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bear makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.cave-fisher.mpmm2014"]={title="Cave Fisher",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 73\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlammable Blood\n\nIf the cave fisher drops to half its hit points or fewer, it gains vulnerability to fire damage.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe cave fisher can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cave fisher makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nRetract Filament\n\nOne Large or smaller creature grappled by the cave fisher's Adhesive Filament must make a 13 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the target is pulled into an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the cave fisher, and the cave fisher makes one Claw attack against it. Anyone else who was attached to the filament is released. Until the grapple ends on the target, the cave fisher can't use Adhesive Filament.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAdhesive Filament\n\nThe cave fisher extends a sticky filament up to 60 feet, and the filament adheres to anything that touches it. A creature the filament adheres to is grappled by the cave fisher (escape 13), and ability checks made to escape this grapple have disadvantage. The filament can be attacked (AC 15; 5 hit points; immunity to poison and psychic damage). A weapon that fails to sever it becomes stuck to it, requiring an action and a successful 13 Strength check to pull free. Destroying the filament deals no damage to the cave fisher. The filament crumbles away if the cave fisher takes this bonus action again."},
  ["creature.cave-fisher.vgm2014"]={title="Cave Fisher",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAdhesive Filament\n\nThe cave fisher can use its action to extend a sticky filament up to 60 feet, and the filament adheres to anything that touches it. A creature adhered to the filament is grappled by the cave fisher (escape 13), and ability checks made to escape this grapple have disadvantage. The filament can be attacked (AC 15; 5 hit points; immunity to poison and psychic damage), but a weapon that fails to sever it becomes stuck to it, requiring an action and a successful 13 Strength check to pull free. Destroying the filament causes no damage to the cave fisher, which can extrude a replacement filament on its next turn\n\nFlammable Blood\n\nIf the cave fisher drops to half its hit points or fewer, it gains vulnerability to fire damage.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe cave fisher can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cave fisher makes two attacks with its claws.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nFilament\n\nOne creature grappled by the cave fisher's adhesive filament must make a 13 Strength saving throw, provided that the target weighs 200 pounds or less. On a failure, the target is pulled into an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the cave fisher, and the cave fisher makes a claw attack against it as a bonus action. Reeling up the target releases anyone else who was attached to the filament. Until the grapple ends on the target, the cave fisher can't extrude another filament."},
  ["creature.cavil-zaltobar.pota2014"]={title="Cavil Zaltobar",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 182\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["optionalfeature.celebrated-in-house.efa2014"]={title="Celebrated in House",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\nWhen you request a favor from your house (as described under \"EFA\"), it can take one of the following additional forms:\n\n• A dragonmarked member of the house casts for you a level 3 or 4 spell associated with the house's mark at no cost.\n\n• A member of the house casts for you a different spell of level 6 or lower at half the usual cost.\n\n• You gain a bodyguard for the duration of your next mission for the house (maximum of 1 week). The bodyguard—a creature with a XPHB no higher than half your level (round up)—is appropriate to your house.\n\nIn addition, your house stipend increases to support your Wealthy lifestyle (4 GP per day)."},
  ["background.celebrity-adventurer-s-scion.ai2014"]={title="Celebrity Adventurer's Scion",subtitle="Background - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Name Dropping\n\nYou know and have met any number of powerful people across the land—and some of them might even remember you. You might be able to wrangle minor assistance from a major figure in the campaign, at the DM's discretion. Additionally, the common folk treat you with deference, and your heritage and the stories you tell might be good for a free meal or a place to sleep.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nScions of celebrity adventurers must deal with fame that's not theirs, wealth they didn't earn, and expectations they can never hope to meet. These hardships can have adverse effects, but those who cope with them can arrive at a decent attitude and a grounded worldview. Those who fail become bitter—or worse.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I will never get out of my famous parent's shadow, and no one else will ever understand this burden.\n\n2 | I've seen enough of the adventuring life to have realistic expectations and empathy for my peers.\n\n3 | Living up to my legacy will be difficult, but I'm going to do it.\n\n4 | I'm used to the very best in life, and that's a hard habit to break.\n\n5 | My parent taught me a sense of duty. I strive to uphold it, even when the odds are against me.\n\n6 | No one can fake a smile, a handshake, or an interested nod like I can.\n\n7 | I've been part of the adventuring life since I was old enough to walk. Let me explain a few things to you.\n\n8 | No risk is too great for the rewards of defeating my enemies... and taking their stuff.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Power. The only way to get ahead in this world is to attain power and hold onto it with all your might. (Evil)\n\n2 | Peace. Those who can find or make peace in the chaotic world around them have everything. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Fame. I've seen what fame can bring. And I'll do anything to get all that for myself. (Neutral)\n\n4 | Training. Hard work, sacrifice, and training lead to success—and eventually to perfection. (Any)\n\n5 | Anonymity. I want to be successful. And alone. With lots of guards and wards between me and everyone else in the world. (Any)\n\n6 | Wisdom. Material wealth is an illusion. Wisdom is the real treasure. (Good)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | While my parent was out adventuring, a servant raised me, and I care about that person more than anyone.\n\n2 | I consider every member of my parent's former adventuring party to be family.\n\n3 | Despite their absences, my famous parent was kind and generous. I love them and want to make them proud.\n\n4 | My parent once brought a cursed magic item home. It is my obsession.\n\n5 | My childhood home holds all my best memories, and its upkeep is my primary concern.\n\n6 | Growing up, I had an imaginary friend I could always count on. That friend is still with me.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | You don't know what I'm going through. You never can.\n\n2 | You. Fetch my cloak. And maybe rub my feet for a while.\n\n3 | My comrades are brave, but I must defeat this threat alone to prove my worth.\n\n4 | Oh, yeah, that spell? Named after my parent's best friend. Let me tell you about them.\n\n5 | My best days are behind me. Ahead lies only toil, pain, and death.\n\n6 | You have to look out for yourself. No one else will."},
  ["psionic.celerity.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Celerity",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nYou channel psionic power into your body, honing your reflexes and agility to an incredible degree. The world seems to slow down while you continue to move as normal."},
  ["creature.celeste.crcotn2014"]={title="Celeste",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["language.celestial.erlw2014"]={title="Celestial",subtitle="Idioma - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 6"},
  ["language.celestial.ggr2014"]={title="Celestial",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.celestial.mot2014"]={title="Celestial",subtitle="Idioma - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["language.celestial.phb2014"]={title="Celestial",subtitle="Idioma - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 123"},
  ["language.celestial.xphb2024"]={title="Celestial",subtitle="Idioma - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 37"},
  ["subclass.celestial-patron.xphb2024.warlock.celestial.0"]={title="Celestial Patron",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Cantrips\n\nPagina: 54\n\nAt 1st level, you learn the sacred flame and light cantrips. They count as warlock cantrips for you, but they don't count against your number of cantrips known.\n\nNivel 1 - Healing Light\n\nPagina: 54\n\nAt 1st level, you gain the ability to channel celestial energy to heal wounds. You have a pool of d6s that you spend to fuel this healing. The number of dice in the pool equals 1 + your warlock level.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can heal one creature you can see within 60 feet of you, spending dice from the pool. The maximum number of dice you can spend at once equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of one die). Roll the dice you spend, add them together, and restore a number of hit points equal to the total.\n\nYour pool regains all expended dice when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 1 - The Celestial\n\nPagina: 54\n\nYour patron is a powerful being of the Upper Planes. You have bound yourself to an ancient empyrean, solar, ki-rin, unicorn, or other entity that resides in the planes of everlasting bliss. Your pact with that being allows you to experience the barest touch of the holy light that illuminates the multiverse.\n\nBeing connected to such power can cause changes in your behavior and beliefs. You might find yourself driven to annihilate the undead, to defeat fiends, and to protect the innocent. At times, your heart might also be filled with a longing for the celestial realm of your patron, and a desire to wander that paradise for the rest of your days. But you know that your mission is among mortals for now, and that your pact binds you to bring light to the dark places of the world.\n\nExpanded Spell List\n\nThe Celestial lets you choose from an expanded list of spells when you learn a warlock spell. The following spells are added to the warlock spell list for you.\n\nSpell Level | Spells\n\n1st | cure wounds, guiding bolt\n\n2nd | flaming sphere, lesser restoration\n\n3rd | daylight, revivify\n\n4th | guardian of faith, wall of fire\n\n5th | flame strike, greater restoration\n\nNivel 3 - Celestial Patron\n\nPagina: 160\n\nCall on the Power of the Heavens\n\nYour pact draws on the Upper Planes, the realms of everlasting bliss. You might enter an agreement with an empyrean, a couatl, a sphinx, a unicorn, or another heavenly entity. Or you might call on numerous such beings as you pursue goals aligned with theirs. Your pact allows you to experience a hint of the holy light that illuminates the multiverse.\n\nNivel 3 - Celestial Spells\n\nPagina: 160\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Celestial Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Healing Light\n\nPagina: 160\n\nYou gain the ability to channel celestial energy to heal wounds. You have a pool of d6s to fuel this healing. The number of dice in the pool equals 1 plus your Warlock level.\n\nAs a XPHB, you can heal yourself or one creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself, expending dice from the pool. The maximum number of dice you can expend at once equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of one die). Roll the dice you expend, and restore a number of XPHB equal to the roll's total. Your pool regains all expended dice when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Healing Light\n\nNivel 3 - The Celestial\n\nNivel 6 - Radiant Soul\n\nPagina: 54\n\nStarting at 6th level, your link to the Celestial allows you to serve as a conduit for radiant energy. You have resistance to radiant damage, and when you cast a spell that deals radiant or fire damage, you can add your Charisma modifier to one radiant or fire damage roll of that spell against one of its targets.\n\nNivel 6 - Radiant Soul\n\nPagina: 160\n\nYour link to your patron allows you to serve as a conduit for radiant energy. You have XPHB to Radiant damage. Once per turn, when a spell you cast deals Radiant or Fire damage, you can add your Charisma modifier to that spell's damage against one of the spell's targets.\n\nNivel 6 - Radiant Soul\n\nNivel 6 - Radiant Soul\n\nNivel 10 - Celestial Resilience\n\nPagina: 54\n\nStarting at 10th level, you gain temporary hit points whenever you finish a short or long rest. These temporary hit points equal your warlock level + your Charisma modifier. Additionally, choose up to five creatures you can see at the end of the rest. Those creatures each gain temporary hit points equal to half your warlock level + your Charisma modifier.\n\nNivel 10 - Celestial Resilience\n\nPagina: 161\n\nYou gain XPHB whenever you use your Magical Cunning feature or finish a XPHB or XPHB. These XPHB equal your Warlock level plus your Charisma modifier. Additionally, choose up to five creatures you can see when you gain the points. Those creatures each gain XPHB equal to half your Warlock level plus your Charisma modifier.\n\nNivel 10 - Celestial Resilience\n\nNivel 14 - Searing Vengeance\n\nPagina: 54\n\nStarting at 14th level, the radiant energy you channel allows you to resist death. When you have to make a death saving throw at the start of your turn, you can instead spring back to your feet with a burst of radiant energy. You regain hit points equal to half your hit point maximum, and then you stand up if you so choose. Each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of you takes radiant damage equal to 2d8 + your Charisma modifier, and it is blinded until the end of the current turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 14 - Searing Vengeance\n\nPagina: 161\n\nWhen you or an ally within 60 feet of you is about to make a XPHB, you can unleash radiant energy to save the creature. The creature regains XPHB equal to half its XPHB maximum and can end the XPHB condition on itself. Each creature of your choice that is within 30 feet of the creature takes Radiant damage equal to 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier, and each has the XPHB condition until the end of the current turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 14 - Searing Vengeance\n\nNivel 14 - Searing Vengeance"},
  ["feature.celestial-patron.xphb2024.warlock.celestial.3"]={title="Celestial Patron",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nCall on the Power of the Heavens\n\nYour pact draws on the Upper Planes, the realms of everlasting bliss. You might enter an agreement with an empyrean, a couatl, a sphinx, a unicorn, or another heavenly entity. Or you might call on numerous such beings as you pursue goals aligned with theirs. Your pact allows you to experience a hint of the holy light that illuminates the multiverse."},
  ["feature.celestial-resilience.xge2024.warlock.celestial.10"]={title="Celestial Resilience",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 54\n\nStarting at 10th level, you gain temporary hit points whenever you finish a short or long rest. These temporary hit points equal your warlock level + your Charisma modifier. Additionally, choose up to five creatures you can see at the end of the rest. Those creatures each gain temporary hit points equal to half your warlock level + your Charisma modifier."},
  ["feature.celestial-resilience.xphb2024.warlock.celestial.10"]={title="Celestial Resilience",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.celestial-spells.xphb2024.warlock.celestial.3"]={title="Celestial Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 160\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Celestial Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.celestial-spirit.tce2014"]={title="Celestial Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, understands the languages you speak\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe celestial makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (rounded down).\n\nRadiant Bow (Avenger Only)\n\nrw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h2d6 + 2 + summonSpellLevel radiant damage.\n\nRadiant Mace (Defender Only)\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d10 + 3 + summonSpellLevel radiant damage, and the celestial can choose itself or another creature it can see within 10 feet of the target. The chosen creature gains 1d10 temporary hit points.\n\nHealing Touch (1/Day)\n\nThe celestial touches another creature. The target magically regains hit points equal to 2d8 + summonSpellLevel."},
  ["creature.celestial-spirit.xphb2024"]={title="Celestial Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 323\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, understands the languages you know\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spirit makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (round down).\n\nRadiant Bow (Avenger Only)\n\nr Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, range 600 ft. h2d6 + 2 + summonSpellLevel Radiant damage.\n\nRadiant Mace (Defender Only)\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d10 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Radiant damage, and the spirit can choose itself or another creature it can see within 10 feet of the target. The chosen creature gains 1d10 XPHB.\n\nHealing Touch (1/Day)\n\nThe spirit touches another creature. The target regains XPHB equal to 2d8 + summonSpellLevel."},
  ["deity.celestian.phb2014"]={title="Celestian",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["deity.celestian.xdmg2024"]={title="Celestian",subtitle="Divindade - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 148"},
  ["magicitem.censer-of-controlling-air-elementals.dmg2014"]={title="Censer of Controlling Air Elementals",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile incense is burning in this censer, you can use an action to speak the censer's command word and summon an air elemental, as if you had cast the conjure elemental spell. The censer can't be used this way again until the next dawn.\n\nThis 6-inch-wide, 1-foot-high vessel resembles a chalice with a decorated lid. It weighs 1 pound."},
  ["magicitem.censer-of-controlling-air-elementals.xdmg2024"]={title="Censer of Controlling Air Elementals",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 243\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile gently swinging this censer, you can take a XPHB action to summon an XMM. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the censer as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your XPHB count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a XPHB. The censer can't be used this way again until the next dawn."},
  ["species.centaur.ggr2014"]={title="Centaur",subtitle="Especie - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nAge\n\nCentaurs mature and age at about the same rate as humans.\n\nAlignment\n\nCentaurs are inclined toward neutrality. Those who join the Selesnya are more often neutral good, while those who join the Gruul are typically chaotic neutral.\n\nSize\n\nCentaurs stand between 6 and 7 feet tall, with their equine bodies reaching about 4 feet at the withers. Your size is Medium.\n\nFey\n\nYour creature type is fey, rather than humanoid.\n\nCharge\n\nIf you move at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack on the same turn, you can immediately follow that attack with a bonus action, making one attack against the target with your hooves.\n\nHooves\n\nYour hooves are natural melee weapons, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nEquine Build\n\nYou count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push or drag.\n\nIn addition, any climb that requires hands and feet is especially difficult for you because of your equine legs. When you make such a climb, each foot of movement costs you 4 extra feet, instead of the normal 1 extra foot.\n\nSurvivor\n\nYou have proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Medicine, Nature, or Survival.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Sylvan. Sylvan is widely spoken in the Selesnya Conclave, for it is rich in vocabulary to describe natural phenomena and spiritual forces."},
  ["creature.centaur.mm2014"]={title="Centaur",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the centaur moves at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a pike attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe centaur makes two attacks: one with its pike and one with its hooves or two with its longbow.\n\nPike\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["species.centaur.mot2014"]={title="Centaur",subtitle="Especie - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 18"},
  ["species.centaur.mpmm2014"]={title="Centaur",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Fey.\n\nCharge\n\nIf you move at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack on the same turn, you can immediately follow that attack with a bonus action, making one attack against the target with your hooves.\n\nEquine Build\n\nYou count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity and the weight you can push or drag.\n\nIn addition, any climb that requires hands and feet is especially difficult for you because of your equine legs. When you make such a climb, each foot of movement costs you 4 extra feet instead of the normal 1 extra foot.\n\nHooves\n\nYou have hooves that you can use to make unarmed strikes. When you hit with them, the strike deals 1d6 + your Strength modifier bludgeoning damage, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nNatural Affinity\n\nYour fey connection to nature gives you an intuitive connection to the natural world and the animals within it. You therefore have proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Medicine, Nature, or Survival."},
  ["creature.centaur-mummy.tftyp2014"]={title="Centaur Mummy",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 231\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the centaur mummy moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a pike attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 10 (3d6) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe centaur mummy makes two melee attacks, one with its pike and one with its hooves, or it attacks with its pike and uses Dreadful Glare.\n\nPike\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with mummy rot. The cursed target can't regain hit points, and its hit point maximum decreases by 10 (3d6) for every 24 hours that elapse. If the curse reduces the target's hit point maximum to 0, the target dies, and its body turns to dust. The curse lasts until removed by the remove curse spell or similar magic.\n\nDreadful Glare\n\nThe centaur mummy targets one creature it can see within 60 feet of it. If the target can see the mummy, the target must succeed on a 12 Wisdom saving throw against this magic or become frightened until the end of the mummy's next turn. If the target fails the saving throw by 5 or more, it is also paralyzed for the same duration. A target that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to the Dreadful Glare of all mummies (but not mummy lords) for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.centaur-trooper.xmm2024"]={title="Centaur Trooper",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 67\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe centaur makes two attacks, using Pike or Longbow in any combination.\n\nPike\n\nm 6, reach 10 ft. h9 (1d10 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nr 4, range 150/600 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTrampling Charge {@recharge 5}\n\nThe centaur moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB and can move through the spaces of Medium or smaller creatures. Each creature whose space the centaur enters is targeted once by the following effect. str 14. actSaveFail 7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.centaur-warden.xmm2024"]={title="Centaur Warden",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 67\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 105 (14d10 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 9 | WIS 18 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Druidic, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe centaur makes two attacks, using Forest Staff or Sun Ray in any combination.\n\nForest Staff\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) Poison damage.\n\nSun Ray\n\nr 7, range 90 ft. h14 (3d6 + 4) Radiant damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the centaur's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEntangling Trail {@recharge 5}\n\nThe centaur moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB. Each creature within 5 feet of the centaur as it moves is targeted once by the following effect. str 15. actSaveFail 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ceo-viktra-mordenheim.pl2014"]={title="CEO Viktra Mordenheim",subtitle="Criatura - PL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 123 (19d8 + 38)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 21 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Elvish, Goblin, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBolster Inventions\n\nAt the end of each of Viktra's turns, each of her Construct allies in a 5-foot XPHB originating from Viktra gains 5 XPHB. This trait doesn't function if Viktra has the XPHB condition.\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Viktra dies, she revives with all her XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Mordenheim Kinetics.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Viktra fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nActivate Constructs (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nViktra makes two Lightning Rod attacks. She can replace one attack with a use of Syringe.\n\nLightning Rod\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 90 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Lightning damage, and the target can't take Reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\nSyringe\n\ncon 16, one creature Viktra can see within 5 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While XPHB in this way, the target suffers one of the following effects (Viktra's choice). The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The target succeeds automatically after 1 minute:\n\n• Corrosive Serum The target takes 10 (4d4) Acid damage at the start of each of its turns, and its XPHB decreases by 10 feet.\n\n• Deadly Serum The target takes 11 (2d10) Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns, and it can't regain XPHB.\n\n• Mind-Altering Serum The target takes 10 (3d6) Psychic damage at the start of each of its turns, and it has XPHB on saving throws to maintain XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nShocking Prod\n\nViktra moves up to half her XPHB and makes one Lightning Rod attack. Viktra can't take this action again until the start of her next turn.\n\nStatic Explosion\n\ndex 16, each creature in a 10-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point Viktra can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 5 (2d4) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.ceratops.bgg2014"]={title="Ceratops",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 129\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 139 (9d20 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 8 | CON 21 | INT 4 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe ceratops has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ceratops makes one Gore attack and one Stomp attack.\n\nGore\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h29 (4d10 + 7) piercing damage. If the ceratops moved at least 20 feet in a straight line toward the target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 11 (2d10) piercing damage; if the target is a creature, it also must succeed on a 19 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 20 feet from the ceratops and have the prone condition.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ceratops.psx2014"]={title="Ceratops",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.ceratos.egw2014"]={title="Ceratos",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nA being that slipped from the Far Realm into Exandria before the Founding, Ceratos is one of the oldest creatures in the world. A single creature of many minds, Ceratos reveled in chaos. When the Elemental Chaos was divided into four planes, Ceratos retreated underground, their minds unraveling as they entered a nightmarish slumber.\n\nThe digging of the Crawling King woke Ceratos a long time after. Though their minds were scattered, each desired the return of chaos to unite themselves. So Ceratos sent thoughts to the surface, offering magic to those who could create chaos in the land above, so that they might one day regain their full power. Ceratos tells their followers that chaos brings clarity and destruction begets rebirth.\n\nAppearance\n\nCeratos is thought to be a massive skinless sphere of flesh covered in mismatched eyes, mouths, and tentacles. They can project their minds' thoughts into other creatures, especially those who desire to bring chaos to the world."},
  ["item.ceremonial-electrum-dagger-with-a-black-pearl-in-the-pommel.dmg2014"]={title="Ceremonial electrum dagger with a black pearl in the pommel",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.ceremonial-gold-armor-with-black-pearls.xdmg2024"]={title="Ceremonial gold armor with black pearls",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.ceremonial-silver-dagger-with-gold-pommel-and-black-pearl-legion-of-dusk.psx2014"]={title="Ceremonial silver dagger with gold pommel and black pearl (Legion of Dusk)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.ceremony.xge2024"]={title="Ceremony",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 151\n\nYou perform a special religious ceremony that is infused with magic. When you cast the spell, choose one of the following rites, the target of which must be within 10 feet of you throughout the casting.\n\nAtonement\n\nYou touch one willing creature whose alignment has changed, and you make a 20 Wisdom (Insight) check. On a successful check, you restore the target to its original alignment.\n\nBless Water\n\nYou touch one phb of water and cause it to become phb.\n\nComing of Age\n\nYou touch one humanoid who is a young adult. For the next 24 hours, whenever the target makes an ability check, it can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check. A creature can benefit from this rite only once.\n\nDedication\n\nYou touch one humanoid who wishes to be dedicated to your god's service. For the next 24 hours, whenever the target makes a saving throw, it can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to the save. A creature can benefit from this rite only once.\n\nFuneral Rite\n\nYou touch one corpse, and for the next 7 days, the target can't become undead by any means short of a wish spell.\n\nWedding\n\nYou touch adult humanoids willing to be bonded together in marriage. For the next 7 days, each target gains a +2 bonus to AC while they are within 30 feet of each other. A creature can benefit from this rite again only if widowed."},
  ["creature.cerodon.psa2014"]={title="Cerodon",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.chain.xphb2024"]={title="Chain",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can wrap a Chain around an unwilling creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition if you succeed on a 13 Strength (XPHB) check. If the creature's legs are bound, the creature has the XPHB condition until it escapes. Escaping the Chain requires the creature to make a successful 18 Dexterity (XPHB) check as an action. Bursting the Chain requires a successful 20 Strength (XPHB) check as an action."},
  ["item.chain-10-feet.phb2014"]={title="Chain (10 feet)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA chain has 10 hit points. It can be burst with a successful 20 Strength check."},
  ["creature.chain-devil.mm2014"]={title="Chain Devil",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 85 (10d8 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the devil's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe devil has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe devil makes two attacks with its chains.\n\nChain\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage. The target is grappled (escape 14) if the devil isn't already grappling a creature. Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained and takes 7 (2d6) piercing damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\nAnimate Chains (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nUp to four chains the devil can see within 60 feet of it magically sprout razor-edged barbs and animate under the devil's control, provided that the chains aren't being worn or carried.\n\nEach animated chain is an object with AC 20, 20 hit points, resistance to piercing damage, and immunity to psychic and thunder damage. When the devil uses Multiattack on its turn, it can use each animated chain to make one additional chain attack. An animated chain can grapple one creature of its own but can't make attacks while grappling. An animated chain reverts to its inanimate state if reduced to 0 hit points or if the devil is incapacitated or dies.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUnnerving Mask\n\nWhen a creature the devil can see starts its turn within 30 feet of the devil, the devil can create the illusion that it looks like one of the creature's departed loved ones or bitter enemies. If the creature can see the devil, it must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of its turn."},
  ["creature.chain-devil.xmm2024"]={title="Chain Devil",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 68\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 85 (10d8 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft. (unimpeded by magical {@variantrule Darkness|XPHB})\n\nIdiomas: Infernal; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, cold, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDiabolical Restoration\n\nIf the devil dies outside the Nine Hells, its body disappears in sulfurous smoke, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere in the Nine Hells.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe devil has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe devil makes two Chain attacks and uses Conjure Infernal Chain.\n\nChain\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from one of two chains, and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends.\n\nConjure Infernal Chain\n\nThe devil conjures a fiery chain to bind a creature. dex 15, one creature the devil can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 9 (2d4 + 4) Fire damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the devil's next turn, at which point the chain disappears. If the target is Large or smaller, the devil moves the target up to 30 feet straight toward itself. actSaveSuccess The chain disappears.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUnnerving Gaze\n\nactTrigger A creature the devil can see starts its turn within 30 feet of the devil and can see the devil. dwis 15, the triggering creature. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its turn. actSaveSuccess The target is immune to this devil's Unnerving Gaze for 24 hours."},
  ["spell.chain-lightning.phb2014"]={title="Chain Lightning",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nYou create a bolt of lightning that arcs toward a target of your choice that you can see within range. Three bolts then leap from that target to as many as three other targets, each of which must be within 30 feet of the first target. A target can be a creature or an object and can be targeted by only one of the bolts.\n\nA target must make a Dexterity saving throw. The target takes 10d8 lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["spell.chain-lightning.xphb2024"]={title="Chain Lightning",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 249\n\nYou launch a lightning bolt toward a target you can see within range. Three bolts then leap from that target to as many as three other targets of your choice, each of which must be within 30 feet of the first target. A target can be a creature or an object and can be targeted by only one of the bolts.\n\nEach target makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d8 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["item.chain-mail.phb2014"]={title="Chain Mail",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\nRaridade: none\n\nMade of interlocking metal rings, chain mail includes a layer of quilted fabric worn underneath the mail to prevent chafing and to cushion the impact of blows. The suit includes gauntlets."},
  ["item.chain-mail.xphb2024"]={title="Chain Mail",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 219\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.chain-shirt.phb2014"]={title="Chain Shirt",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nRaridade: none\n\nMade of interlocking metal rings, a chain shirt is worn between layers of clothing or leather. This armor offers modest protection to the wearer's upper body and allows the sound of the rings rubbing against one another to be muffled by outer layers."},
  ["item.chain-shirt.xphb2024"]={title="Chain Shirt",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 219\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["optionalfeature.chains-of-carceri.phb2014"]={title="Chains of Carceri",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou can cast hold monster at will—targeting a celestial, fiend, or elemental—without expending a spell slot or material components. You must finish a long rest before you can use this invocation on the same creature again."},
  ["creature.chakuna.rhw2014"]={title="Chakuna",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 210 (28d8 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 150 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common (can't speak in panther form)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Chakuna dies and her heart remains intact, she revives with all her XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Valachan. Chakuna's heart is a Tiny object that has AC 17, HP 10, and XPHB to all damage except Fire.\n\nExperienced Hunter\n\nXPHB composed of undergrowth doesn't cost Chakuna extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Chakuna fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nChakuna makes three attacks, using Scratch or Barbed Spear in any combination. She can replace one attack with a Bite attack.\n\nBite (Panther or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nm 8, reach 5 ft. h20 (3d10 + 4) Piercing damage. If the target is a Humanoid, it is subjected to the following effect. con 15. actSaveFail The target is cursed. If the cursed target drops to 0 XPHB, it instead becomes a werepanther under the DM's control and has 10 XPHB (use the Weretiger stat block). actSaveSuccess The target is immune to Chakuna's curse for 24 hours.\n\nScratch\n\nm 8, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\nBarbed Spear (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nm,r 8, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage and the target receives a dire wound if it doesn't have one. While the target is wounded, its speed is reduced by 10 feet, and it loses 5 (1d10) XPHB at the start of each of its turns. The wound closes after 1 minute, after a spell restores XPHB to the target, or after the target or a creature within 5 feet of it takes an action to staunch the wound, doing so by succeeding on a 15 Wisdom (XPHB) check. homThe spear magically returns to Chakuna's hand immediately after a ranged attack.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nProwl (Panther or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nChakuna moves up to her XPHB without provoking XPHB. At the end of this movement, she can take the XPHB action.\n\nShape-Shift\n\nChakuna shape-shifts into a Large panther-humanoid hybrid or a Large panther, or she returns to her true humanoid form. Her game statistics, other than her size, are the same in each form. Any equipment she is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nChakuna moves up to half her XPHB and makes one Scratch attack.\n\nStrike from Shadows\n\nChakuna makes one Barbed Spear attack. If Chakuna has the XPHB action's XPHB condition, this attack doesn't end that condition. Chakuna can't take this action again until the start of her next turn.\n\nSudden Bite\n\nChakuna uses Shape-Shift to turn into her hybrid form or panther form and then makes one Bite attack. Chakuna can't take this action again until the start of her next turn."},
  ["item.chalcedony.dmg2014"]={title="Chalcedony",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque white gemstone."},
  ["item.chalcedony.xdmg2024"]={title="Chalcedony",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA white gemstone."},
  ["feature.chalice.tce2014.druid.stars.2"]={title="Chalice",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nA constellation of a life-giving goblet appears on you. Whenever you cast a spell using a spell slot that restores hit points to a creature, you or another creature within 30 feet of you can regain hit points equal to 1d8 + your Wisdom modifier."},
  ["feature.chalice.xphb2024.druid.stars.3"]={title="Chalice",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["item.chalk-1-piece.phb2014"]={title="Chalk (1 piece)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.chamberlain-of-zuggtmoy.oota2014"]={title="Chamberlain of Zuggtmoy",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 7 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 8 | CHA 12\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMushroom Portal\n\nThe chamberlain counts as a mushroom for the Fungus Stride feature of the bridesmaid of Zuggtmoy.\n\nPoison Spores\n\nWhenever the chamberlain takes damage, it releases a cloud of spores. Creatures within 5 feet of the chamberlain when this happens must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe chamberlain makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nInfestation Spores (1/Day)\n\nThe chamberlain releases spores that burst out in a cloud that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on it, and the cloud lingers for 1 minute. Any flesh-and-blood creature in the cloud when it appears, or that enters it later, must make a 12 Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the creature can't be infected by these spores for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature is infected with a disease called the spores of Zuggtmoy and also gains a random form of indefinite madness (determined by rolling on the Madness of Zuggtmoy table in appendix D) that lasts until the creature is cured of the disease or dies. While infected in this way, the creature can't be reinfected, and it must be repeat the saving throw at the end of every 24 hours, ending the infection on a success. On a failure, the infected creature's body is slowly taken over by fungal growth, and after three such failed saves, the creature dies and is reanimated as a spore servant if it's a type of creature that can be (see the \"Myconids\" entry in the Monster Manual)."},
  ["creature.champion.mpmm2014"]={title="Champion",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 74\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 143 (22d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIndomitable (2/Day)\n\nThe champion rerolls a failed saving throw.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes three Greatsword or Shortbow attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage, plus 7 (2d6) slashing damage if the champion has more than half of its total hit points remaining.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, plus 7 (2d6) piercing damage if the champion has more than half of its total hit points remaining.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSecond Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe champion regains 20 hit points."},
  ["subclass.champion.phb2014.fighter.champion.0"]={title="Champion",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Champion\n\nPagina: 72\n\nThe archetypal Champion focuses on the development of raw physical power honed to deadly perfection. Those who model themselves on this archetype combine rigorous training with physical excellence to deal devastating blows.\n\nNivel 3 - Champion\n\nPagina: 96\n\nPursue Physical Excellence in Combat\n\nA Champion focuses on the development of martial prowess in a relentless pursuit of victory. Champions combine rigorous training with physical excellence to deal devastating blows, withstand peril, and garner glory. Whether in athletic contests or bloody battle, Champions strive for the crown of the victor.\n\nNivel 3 - Improved Critical\n\nPagina: 72\n\nBeginning when you choose this archetype at 3rd level, your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20.\n\nNivel 3 - Improved Critical\n\nPagina: 96\n\nYour attack rolls with weapons and Unarmed Strikes can score a XPHB on a roll of 19 or 20 on the d20.\n\nNivel 3 - Improved Critical\n\nNivel 3 - Improved Critical\n\nNivel 3 - Remarkable Athlete\n\nPagina: 96\n\nThanks to your athleticism, you have XPHB on XPHB rolls and Strength (XPHB) checks.\n\nIn addition, immediately after you score a XPHB, you can move up to half your XPHB without provoking XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Remarkable Athlete\n\nNivel 7 - Additional Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 96\n\nYou gain another feats of your choice.\n\nNivel 7 - Remarkable Athlete\n\nPagina: 72\n\nStarting at 7th level, you can add half your proficiency bonus (round up) to any Strength, Dexterity, or Constitution check you make that doesn't already use your proficiency bonus.\n\nIn addition, when you make a running long jump, the distance you can cover increases by a number of feet equal to your Strength modifier.\n\nNivel 7 - Remarkable Athlete\n\nNivel 10 - Additional Fighting Style\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 10th level, you can choose a second option from the Fighting Style class feature.\n\nNivel 10 - Heroic Warrior\n\nPagina: 96\n\nThe thrill of battle drives you toward victory. During combat, you can give yourself XPHB whenever you start your turn without it.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Critical\n\nPagina: 72\n\nStarting at 15th level, your weapon attacks score a critical hit on a roll of 18-20.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Critical\n\nPagina: 96\n\nYour attack rolls with weapons and Unarmed Strikes can now score a XPHB on a roll of 18–20 on the d20.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Critical\n\nNivel 18 - Survivor\n\nPagina: 72\n\nAt 18th level, you attain the pinnacle of resilience in battle. At the start of each of your turns, you regain hit points equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier if you have no more than half of your hit points left. You don't gain this benefit if you have 0 hit points.\n\nNivel 18 - Survivor\n\nPagina: 96\n\nYou attain the pinnacle of resilience in battle, giving you these benefits.\n\nDefy Death\n\nYou have XPHB on XPHB. Moreover, when you roll 18–20 on a XPHB, you gain the benefit of rolling a 20 on it.\n\nHeroic Rally\n\nAt the start of each of your turns, you regain XPHB equal to 5 plus your Constitution modifier if you are XPHB and have at least 1 XPHB.\n\nNivel 18 - Survivor"},
  ["feature.champion.phb2014.fighter.champion.3"]={title="Champion",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nThe archetypal Champion focuses on the development of raw physical power honed to deadly perfection. Those who model themselves on this archetype combine rigorous training with physical excellence to deal devastating blows."},
