  ["reward.champion-of-destiny.mot2014"]={title="Champion of Destiny",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 58\n\nPiety 50+ Klothys trait\n\nYou can increase your Strength or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["creature.champion-of-gorm.qftis2014"]={title="Champion of Gorm",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nThe champion has advantage on saving throws against the frightened condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes two Lightning Mace attacks or three Handaxe attacks.\n\nLightning Mace\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 5 (2d4) lightning damage.\n\nHandaxe\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAura of Resilience (1/Day)\n\nThe champion exudes an aura of ghostly lightning that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. While this aura is active, the champion and each creature of its choice within the aura have advantage on saving throws. The aura moves with the champion and lasts for 1 minute, until the champion has the incapacitated condition, or until the champion uses another bonus action to end the aura."},
  ["reward.champion-of-harvests.mot2014"]={title="Champion of Harvests",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\nPiety 50+ Karametra trait\n\nYou can increase your Constitution or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-horizons.mot2014"]={title="Champion of Horizons",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\nPiety 50+ Kruphix trait\n\nYou can increase your Constitution or Intelligence score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["creature.champion-of-madarua.qftis2014"]={title="Champion of Madarua",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes three Longsword attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage if used with two hands.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAura of Fury (1/Day)\n\nThe champion summons an aura of ghostly animals that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. While this aura is active, the champion and all its allies in the aura have advantage on attack rolls. The aura moves with the champion and lasts for 1 minute, until the champion has the incapacitated condition, or until the champion uses another bonus action to end the aura.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe champion adds 2 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the champion must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["reward.champion-of-slaughter.mot2014"]={title="Champion of Slaughter",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nPiety 50+ Mogis trait\n\nYou can increase your Strength or Constitution score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-storms.mot2014"]={title="Champion of Storms",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 55\n\nPiety 50+ Keranos trait\n\nYou can increase your Intelligence or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-dead.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Dead",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\nPiety 50+ Erebos trait\n\nYou can increase your Constitution or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-forge.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Forge",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nPiety 50+ Purphoros trait\n\nYou can increase your Strength or Intelligence score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-hunt.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Hunt",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 67\n\nPiety 50+ Nylea trait\n\nYou can increase your Dexterity or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-passage.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Passage",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nPiety 50+ Athreos trait\n\nYou can increase your Intelligence or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-polis.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Polis",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\nPiety 50+ Ephara trait\n\nYou can increase your Intelligence or Charisma score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-sea.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Sea",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\nPiety 50+ Thassa trait\n\nYou can increase your Dexterity or Intelligence score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["reward.champion-of-the-sun.mot2014"]={title="Champion of the Sun",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\nPiety 50+ Heliod trait\n\nYou can increase your Strength or Wisdom score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["creature.champion-of-usamigaras.qftis2014"]={title="Champion of Usamigaras",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes two Arcane Burst attacks or makes one Arcane Burst attack and uses Spellcasting.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) force damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAura of Deception (1/Day)\n\nThe champion emits an aura of ghostly illusions that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. While this aura is active, creatures have disadvantage on attack rolls against the champion and any of the champion's allies that are in the aura. The aura moves with the champion and lasts for 1 minute, until the champion has the incapacitated condition, or until the champion uses another bonus action to end the aura."},
  ["reward.champion-of-victory.mot2014"]={title="Champion of Victory",subtitle="Recompensa - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 49\n\nPiety 50+ Iroas trait\n\nYou can increase your Strength or Charisma score by 2 and also increase your maximum for that score by 2."},
  ["species.changeling.efa2014"]={title="Changeling",subtitle="Especie - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\nChangeling Instincts\n\nThanks to your connection to the fey realm, you gain proficiency in two of the following skills of your choice: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB.\n\nShape-Shifter\n\nAs an action, you can shape-shift to change your appearance and your voice. You determine the specifics of the changes, including your coloration, hair length, and sex. You can also adjust your height and weight and can change your size between Medium and Small. You can make yourself appear as a member of another playable species, though none of your game statistics change. You can't duplicate the appearance of an individual you've never seen, and you must adopt a form that has the same basic arrangement of limbs that you have. This trait doesn't change your clothing and equipment.\n\nWhile shape-shifted with this trait, you have XPHB on Charisma checks.\n\nYou stay in the new form until you take an action to revert to your true form."},
  ["creature.changeling.erlw2014"]={title="Changeling",subtitle="Criatura - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 317\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish, Elvish, Halfling, Thieves' cant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChange Appearance\n\nThe changeling can use its action to polymorph into a Medium humanoid it has seen, or back into its true form. Its statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe changeling makes two attacks with its dagger.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nUnsettling Visage (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nEach creature within 30 feet of the changeling must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["species.changeling.erlw2014"]={title="Changeling",subtitle="Especie - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nAge\n\nChangelings mature slightly faster than humans but share a similar lifespan—typically a century or less. While a changeling can transform to conceal their age, the effects of aging affect them similarly to humans.\n\nAlignment\n\nChangelings tend toward pragmatic neutrality, and few changelings embrace evil.\n\nSize\n\nYour size is Medium.\n\nShapechanger\n\nAs an action, you can change your appearance and your voice. You determine the specifics of the changes, including your coloration, hair length, and sex. You can also adjust your height and weight, but not so much that your size changes. You can make yourself appear as a member of another race, though none of your game statistics change. You can't duplicate the appearance of a creature you've never seen, and you must adopt a form that has the same basic arrangement of limbs that you have. Your clothing and equipment aren't changed by this trait.\n\nYou stay in the new form until you use an action to revert to your true form or until you die.\n\nChangeling Instincts\n\nYou gain proficiency with two of the following skills of your choice: Deception, Insight, Intimidation, and Persuasion.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and two other languages of your choice."},
  ["species.changeling.mpmm2014"]={title="Changeling",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Fey.\n\nSize\n\nYou are Medium or Small. You choose the size when you select this race.\n\nChangeling Instincts\n\nThanks to your connection to the fey realm, you gain proficiency with two of the following skills of your choice: Deception, Insight, Intimidation, Performance, or Persuasion.\n\nShapechanger\n\nAs an action, you change your appearance and your voice. You determine the specifics of the changes, including your coloration, hair length, and sex. You can also adjust your height between Medium and Small. You can make yourself appear as a member of another race, though none of your game statistics change. You can't duplicate the appearance of an individual you've never seen, and you must adopt a form that has the same basic arrangement of limbs that you have. Your clothing and equipment aren't changed by this trait.\n\nYou stay in the new form until you use an action to revert to your true form or until you die."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.dmg2014.paladin.oathbreaker.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nAn Oathbreaker paladin of 3rd level or higher gains the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.cleric.base.2"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAt 2nd level, you gain the ability to channel divine energy directly from your deity, using that energy to fuel magical effects. You start with two such effects: Turn Undead and an effect determined by your domain. Some domains grant you additional effects as you advance in levels, as noted in the domain description.\n\nWhen you use your Channel Divinity, you choose which effect to create. You must then finish a short or long rest to use your Channel Divinity again.\n\nSome Channel Divinity effects require saving throws. When you use such an effect from this class, the DC equals your cleric spell save DC.\n\nBeginning at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity twice between rests, and beginning at 18th level, you can use it three times between rests. When you finish a short or long rest, you regain your expended uses."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.cleric.base.6"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.cleric.base.18"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.paladin.base.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nYour oath allows you to channel divine energy to fuel magical effects. Each Channel Divinity option provided by your oath explains how to use it.\n\nWhen you use your Channel Divinity, you choose which option to use. You must then finish a short or long rest to use your Channel Divinity again.\n\nSome Channel Divinity effects require saving throws. When you use such an effect from this class, the DC equals your paladin spell save DC."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.paladin.ancients.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 86\n\nWhen you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.paladin.devotion.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 85\n\nWhen you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.phb2014.paladin.vengeance.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 87\n\nWhen you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.scag2014.paladin.crown.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nWhen you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.tce2014.paladin.glory.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 53\n\n3rd-level Oath of Glory feature\n\nYou gain the following two Channel Divinity options. See the Sacred Oath class feature for how Channel Divinity works."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.tce2014.paladin.watchers.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\n3rd-level Oath of the Watchers feature\n\nYou gain the following Channel Divinity options. See the Sacred Oath class feature for how Channel Divinity works."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.xge2024.paladin.conquest.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 37\n\nWhen you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.xge2024.paladin.redemption.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 38\n\nWhen you take this oath at 3rd level, you gain the following two Channel Divinity options."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.xphb2024.cleric.base.2"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity.xphb2024.paladin.base.3"]={title="Channel Divinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-arcane-abjuration.scag2014.cleric.arcana.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-arcane-abjuration.scag2014.cleric.arcana.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Arcane Abjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-artisan-s-blessing.xge2024.cleric.forge.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Artisan's Blessing",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 18\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to create simple items.\n\nYou conduct an hour-long ritual that crafts a nonmagical item that must include some metal: a items, a suit of armor, ten pieces of ammunition, a set of tools, or another metal object (see chapter 5, \"Equipment,\" in the Player's Handbook for examples of these items). The creation is completed at the end of the hour, coalescing in an unoccupied space of your choice on a surface within 5 feet of you.\n\nThe thing you create can be something that is worth no more than 100 gp. As part of this ritual, you must lay out metal, which can include coins, with a value equal to the creation. The metal irretrievably coalesces and transforms into the creation at the ritual's end, magically forming even nonmetal parts of the creation. The ritual can create a duplicate of a nonmagical item that contains metal, such as a key, if you possess the original during the ritual."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-artisan-s-blessing.xge2024.cleric.forge.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Artisan's Blessing",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-balm-of-peace.tce2014.cleric.peace.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Balm of Peace",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n2nd-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to make your very presence a soothing balm. As an action, you can move up to your speed, without provoking opportunity attacks, and when you move within 5 feet of any other creature during this action, you can restore a number of hit points to that creature equal to 2d6 + your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1 hit point). A creature can receive this healing only once whenever you take this action."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-balm-of-peace.tce2014.cleric.peace.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Balm of Peace",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-charm-animals-and-plants.phb2014.cleric.nature.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Charm Animals and Plants",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-charm-animals-and-plants.phb2014.cleric.nature.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Charm Animals and Plants",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-cloak-of-shadows.phb2014.cleric.trickery.6"]={title="Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity to vanish.\n\nAs an action, you become invisible until the end of your next turn. You become visible if you attack or cast a spell."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-cloak-of-shadows.psa2014.cleric.ambition-psa.6"]={title="Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity to vanish. As an action, you become invisible until the end of your next turn. You become visible if you attack or cast a spell."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-consuming-fervor.psa2014.cleric.zeal-psa.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Consuming Fervor",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to channel your zeal into unchecked ferocity.\n\nWhen you roll fire or thunder damage, you can use your Channel Divinity to deal maximum damage instead of rolling."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-consuming-fervor.psa2014.cleric.zeal-psa.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Consuming Fervor",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-destructive-wrath.phb2014.cleric.tempest.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Destructive Wrath",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to wield the power of the storm with unchecked ferocity.\n\nWhen you roll lightning or thunder damage, you can use your Channel Divinity to deal maximum damage, instead of rolling."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-destructive-wrath.phb2014.cleric.tempest.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Destructive Wrath",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-feat-of-strength.psa2014.cleric.strength-psa.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Feat of Strength",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nAt 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to enhance your physical might. When you make an attack roll, ability check, or saving throw using Strength, you can use your Channel Divinity to gain a +10 bonus to the roll. You make this choice after you see the roll, but before the DM says whether the roll succeeds or fails."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-feat-of-strength.psa2014.cleric.strength-psa.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Feat of Strength",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-guided-strike.phb2014.cleric.war.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Guided Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 63\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to strike with supernatural accuracy. When you make an attack roll, you can use your Channel Divinity to gain a +10 bonus to the roll. You make this choice after you see the roll, but before the DM says whether the attack hits or misses."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-guided-strike.phb2014.cleric.war.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Guided Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-harness-divine-power.tce2014.cleric.base.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Harness Divine Power",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-harness-divine-power.tce2014.paladin.base.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Harness Divine Power",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\n{@i 3rd-level paladin tce\n\nYou can expend a use of your Channel Divinity to fuel your spells. As a bonus action, you touch your holy symbol, utter a prayer, and regain one expended spell slot, the level of which can be no higher than half your proficiency bonus (rounded up). The number of times you can use this feature is based on the level you've reached in this class: 3rd level, once; 7th level, twice; and 15th level, thrice. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-invoke-duplicity.phb2014.cleric.trickery.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-invoke-duplicity.phb2014.cleric.trickery.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-invoke-duplicity.psa2014.cleric.ambition-psa.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to create an illusory duplicate of yourself.\n\nAs an action, you create a perfect illusion of yourself that lasts for 1 minute, or until you lose your concentration (as if you were concentration on a spell). The illusion appears in an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet of you. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to a space you can see, but it must remain within 120 feet of you.\n\nFor the duration, you can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses. Additionally, when both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have advantage on attack rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-invoke-duplicity.psa2014.cleric.ambition-psa.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-knowledge-of-the-ages.phb2014.cleric.knowledge.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Knowledge of the Ages",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-knowledge-of-the-ages.phb2014.cleric.knowledge.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Knowledge of the Ages",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-order-s-demand.tce2014.cleric.order.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Order's Demand",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-order-s-demand.tce2014.cleric.order.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Order's Demand",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-path-to-the-grave.xge2024.cleric.grave.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Path to the Grave",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-path-to-the-grave.xge2024.cleric.grave.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Path to the Grave",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-preserve-life.phb2014.cleric.life.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Preserve Life",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to heal the badly injured.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol and evoke healing energy that can restore a number of hit points equal to five times your cleric level. Choose any creatures within 30 feet of you, and divide those hit points among them. This feature can restore a creature to no more than half of its hit point maximum. You can't use this feature on an undead or a construct."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-preserve-life.phb2014.cleric.life.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Preserve Life",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-preserve-life.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Preserve Life",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to heal the badly injured.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol and evoke healing energy that can restore a number of hit points equal to five times your cleric level. Choose any creatures within 30 feet of you, and divide those hit points among them. This feature can restore a creature to no more than half of its hit point maximum. You can't use this feature on an undead or a construct."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-preserve-life.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Preserve Life",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-radiance-of-the-dawn.phb2014.cleric.light.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-radiance-of-the-dawn.phb2014.cleric.light.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Radiance of the Dawn",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-read-thoughts.phb2014.cleric.knowledge.6"]={title="Channel Divinity: Read Thoughts",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-touch-of-death.dmg2014.cleric.death.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Touch of Death",subtitle="Caracteristica - DMG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-touch-of-death.dmg2014.cleric.death.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Touch of Death",subtitle="Caracteristica - DMG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-turn-undead.phb2014.cleric.base.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Turn Undead",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol and speak a prayer censuring the undead. Each undead that can see or hear you within 30 feet of you must make a Wisdom saving throw. If the creature fails its saving throw, it is turned for 1 minute or until it takes any damage.\n\nA turned creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can't willingly move to a space within 30 feet of you. It also can't take reactions. For its action, it can use only the Dash action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If there's nowhere to move, the creature can use the Dodge action."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-twilight-sanctuary.tce2014.cleric.twilight.2"]={title="Channel Divinity: Twilight Sanctuary",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n2nd-level Twilight Domain feature\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to refresh your allies with soothing twilight.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol, and a sphere of twilight emanates from you. The sphere is centered on you, has a 30-foot radius, and is filled with dim light. The sphere moves with you, and it lasts for 1 minute or until you are incapacitated or die. Whenever a creature (including you) ends its turn in the sphere, you can grant that creature one of these benefits:\n\n• You grant it temporary hit points equal to 1d6 plus your cleric level.\n\n• You end one effect on it causing it to be charmed or frightened."},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-twilight-sanctuary.tce2014.cleric.twilight.3"]={title="Channel Divinity: Twilight Sanctuary",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.channel-divinity-war-god-s-blessing.phb2014.cleric.war.6"]={title="Channel Divinity: War God's Blessing",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 63\n\nAt 6th level, when a creature within 30 feet of you makes an attack roll, you can use your reaction to grant that creature a +10 bonus to the roll, using your Channel Divinity. You make this choice after you see the roll, but before the DM says whether the attack hits or misses."},
  ["feature.channeler.rhw2014.bard.spirits.3"]={title="Channeler",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.chaos-bolt.xge2024"]={title="Chaos Bolt",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 151\n\nYou hurl an undulating, warbling mass of chaotic energy at one creature in range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 + 1d6 damage. Choose one of the d8s. The number rolled on that die determines the attack's damage type, as shown below.\n\nd8 | Damage Type\n\n | Acid\n\n | Cold\n\n | Fire\n\n | Force\n\n | Lightning\n\n | Poison\n\n | Psychic\n\n | Thunder\n\nIf you roll the same number on both d8s, the chaotic energy leaps from the target to a different creature of your choice within 30 feet of it. Make a new attack roll against the new target, and make a new damage roll, which could cause the chaotic energy to leap again.\n\nA creature can be targeted only once by each casting of this spell."},
  ["creature.chaos-quadrapod.ai2014"]={title="Chaos Quadrapod",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe chaos quadrapod has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe chaos quadrapod makes up to two tentacle attacks.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 14). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained. The chaos quadrapod can grapple no more than two targets at a time.\n\nChaos Cloud (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe chaos quadrapod shoots forth a knot of roiling ethereal light that explodes at a point it can see within 60 feet of it. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must succeed on a 14 Charisma saving throw or be stunned until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.chardalyn-berserker.idrotf2014"]={title="Chardalyn Berserker",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 280\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 9 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChardalyn Madness\n\nThe berserker must roll a d6 at the start of each of its turns. On a 1, the berserker does nothing on its turn except speak to a nonexistent, evil master whom it has pledged to serve.\n\nReckless\n\nAt the start of its turn, the berserker can gain advantage on all melee weapon attack rolls during that turn, but attack rolls against it have advantage until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe berserker attacks three times with a melee weapon.\n\nChardalyn Flail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the end of its next turn.\n\nChardalyn Javelin\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.chardalyn-dragon.idrotf2014"]={title="Chardalyn Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 281\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 147 (14d12 + 56)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 11 | CON 19 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages known by its creator\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades: cold, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe dragon is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe dragon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe dragon deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep, and it gains no benefit from finishing a short or long rest.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon uses its Malevolent Presence. It then makes three attacks: two with its claws and one with its tail. If the dragon isn't flying, it can also make one attack with its wings.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nWings\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d4 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nMalevolent Presence\n\nAny creature with an Intelligence of 4 or more that is within 30 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by it for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Malevolent Presence for the next 24 hours. A creature charmed in this way fixates on another creature or object that the dragon mentally chooses and must, on each of its turns, move as close as it can to that target and use its action to make a melee attack against it. If the dragon doesn't choose a target, the charmed creature can act normally on its turn.\n\nRadiant Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a ray of radiant energy in a 120-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 31 (7d8) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["feat.charger.phb2014"]={title="Charger",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\nWhen you use your action to Dash, you can use a bonus action to make one melee weapon attack or to shove a creature.\n\nIf you move at least 10 feet in a straight line immediately before taking this bonus action, you either gain a +5 bonus to the attack's damage roll (if you chose to make a melee attack and hit) or push the target up to 10 feet away from you (if you chose to shove and you succeed)."},
  ["feat.charger.xphb2024"]={title="Charger",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 202\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nImproved Dash\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action, your XPHB increases by 10 feet for that action.\n\nCharge Attack\n\nIf you move at least 10 feet in a straight line toward a target immediately before hitting it with a melee attack roll as part of the XPHB action, choose one of the following effects: gain a 1d8 bonus to the attack's damage roll, or push the target up to 10 feet away if it is no more than one size larger than you. You can use this benefit only once on each of your turns."},
  ["item.chariot.phb2014"]={title="Chariot",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none\n\nChariots\n\nChariots and the creatures pulling them work like controlled mounts, as described in the mounted combat rules in the PHB, but with the following differences:\n\n• Mounting or dismounting a chariot costs you 5 feet of movement, rather than a number of feet equal to half your speed.\n\n• Being mounted on a chariot grants you Cover.\n\n• A chariot's speed is equal to the speed of the slowest creature pulling it.\n\n• If multiple creatures are pulling the chariot, they all act on the same initiative, and they must take the same action on their turn."},
  ["item.chariot.xphb2024"]={title="Chariot",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["background.charlatan.phb2014"]={title="Charlatan",subtitle="Background - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: False Identity\n\nYou have created a second identity that includes documentation, established acquaintances, and disguises that allow you to assume that persona. Additionally, you can forge documents including official papers and personal letters, as long as you have seen an example of the kind of document or the handwriting you are trying to copy.\n\nFavorite Schemes\n\nEvery charlatan has an angle he or she uses in preference to other schemes. Choose a favorite scam or roll on the table below.\n\nd6 | Scam\n\n1 | I cheat at games of chance.\n\n2 | I shave coins or forge documents.\n\n3 | I insinuate myself into people's lives to prey on their weakness and secure their fortunes.\n\n4 | I put on new identities like clothes.\n\n5 | I run sleight-of-hand cons on street corners.\n\n6 | I convince people that worthless junk is worth their hard-earned money.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nCharlatans are colorful characters who conceal their true selves behind the masks they construct. They reflect what people want to see, what they want to believe, and how they see the world. But their true selves are sometimes plagued by an uneasy conscience, an old enemy, or deep-seated trust issues.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I fall in and out of love easily, and am always pursuing someone.\n\n2 | I have a joke for every occasion, especially occasions where humor is inappropriate.\n\n3 | Flattery is my preferred trick for getting what I want.\n\n4 | I'm a born gambler who can't resist taking a risk for a potential payoff.\n\n5 | I lie about almost everything, even when there's no reason to.\n\n6 | Sarcasm and insults are my weapons of choice.\n\n7 | I keep multiple holy symbols on me and invoke whatever deity might come in useful at any given moment.\n\n8 | I pocket anything I see that might have some value.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Independence. I am a free spirit—no one tells me what to do. (Chaotic)\n\n2 | Fairness. I never target people who can't afford to lose a few coins. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Charity. I distribute the money I acquire to the people who really need it. (Good)\n\n4 | Creativity. I never run the same con twice. (Chaotic)\n\n5 | Friendship. Material goods come and go. Bonds of friendship last forever. (Good)\n\n6 | Aspiration. I'm determined to make something of myself. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | I fleeced the wrong person and must work to ensure that this individual never crosses paths with me or those I care about.\n\n2 | I owe everything to my mentor—a horrible person who's probably rotting in jail somewhere.\n\n3 | Somewhere out there, I have a child who doesn't know me. I'm making the world better for him or her.\n\n4 | I come from a noble family, and one day I'll reclaim my lands and title from those who stole them from me.\n\n5 | A powerful person killed someone I love. Some day soon, I'll have my revenge.\n\n6 | I swindled and ruined a person who didn't deserve it. I seek to atone for my misdeeds but might never be able to forgive myself.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I can't resist a pretty face.\n\n2 | I'm always in debt. I spend my ill-gotten gains on decadent luxuries faster than I bring them in.\n\n3 | I'm convinced that no one could ever fool me the way I fool others.\n\n4 | I'm too greedy for my own good. I can't resist taking a risk if there's money involved.\n\n5 | I can't resist swindling people who are more powerful than me.\n\n6 | I hate to admit it and will hate myself for it, but I'll run and preserve my own hide if the going gets tough."},
  ["background.charlatan.xphb2024"]={title="Charlatan",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 180\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["magicitem.charlatan-s-die.xdmg2024"]={title="Charlatan's Die",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 243\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhenever you roll this six-sided die, you can control which number it rolls."},
  ["magicitem.charlatan-s-die.xge2024"]={title="Charlatan's Die",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 136\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nWhenever you roll this six-sided die, you can control which number it rolls."},
  ["spell.charm-monster.xge2024"]={title="Charm Monster",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 151\n\nYou attempt to charm a creature you can see within range. It must make a Wisdom saving throw, and it does so with advantage if you or your companions are fighting it. If it fails the saving throw, it is charmed by you until the spell ends or until you or your companions do anything harmful to it. The charmed creature is friendly to you. When the spell ends, the creature knows it was charmed by you."},
  ["spell.charm-monster.xphb2024"]={title="Charm Monster",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 249\n\nOne creature you can see within range makes a Wisdom saving throw. It does so with XPHB if you or your allies are fighting it. On a failed save, the target has the XPHB condition until the spell ends or until you or your allies damage it. The XPHB creature is XPHB to you. When the spell ends, the target knows it was XPHB by you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-agelessness.bgdia2014"]={title="Charm of Agelessness",subtitle="Recompensa - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nWhile you have this charm, you don't age naturally, and your skin gains the waxy complexion of a doll. Magical aging still affects you, however. This charm vanishes from you when you die."},
  ["reward.charm-of-air-bubbles.bam2014"]={title="Charm of Air Bubbles",subtitle="Recompensa - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\n{@note This charm can be bestowed by a BAM using their Magical Gift action.\n\nThis charm allows you to cast the AAG spell (see the Astral Adventurer's Guide) as an action. Once used three times, this charm goes away."},
  ["reward.charm-of-animal-conjuring.dmg2014"]={title="Charm of Animal Conjuring",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nThis charm allows you to cast the conjure animals spell (3rd-level version) as an action. Once used three times, the charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-animal-conjuring.xdmg2024"]={title="Charm of Animal Conjuring",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nThis Charm allows you to cast XPHB. Once used three times, the Charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-argonnessen.efa2014"]={title="Charm of Argonnessen",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nWhile you have this Charm, you know XPHB. You can expend the Charm to cast XPHB (level 4 version), targeting yourself only."},
  ["reward.charm-of-ashtakala.efa2014"]={title="Charm of Ashtakala",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nWhile you have this Charm, you know XPHB and XPHB. You can expend the Charm to cast XPHB (level 4 version)."},
  ["reward.charm-of-balance.bmt2014"]={title="Charm of Balance",subtitle="Recompensa - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 60 feet of you damages you, you can use your reaction to deal an amount of force damage to that creature equal to half the damage you took. Once used three times, the charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-biting-cold.idrotf2014"]={title="Charm of Biting Cold",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\n{@note This charm can be bestowed by a ToA living in Icewind Dale or other cold regions by using their Magical Gift action.\n\nThis charm has 3 charges. As a bonus action, you can expend 1 of the charm's charges to wreathe your weapon attacks with biting cold for 1 minute. Until this effect ends, you deal an extra 1d6 cold damage when you hit with a melee or ranged weapon attack. Once all its charges have been expended, this charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-bounty.idrotf2014"]={title="Charm of Bounty",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\n{@note This charm can be bestowed by a ToA living in Icewind Dale or other cold regions by using their Magical Gift action.\n\nThis charm has 3 charges. As an action, you can expend 1 of the charm's charges to cast the create food and water spell, requiring no components. Once all its charges have been expended, this charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-cold-resistance.idrotf2014"]={title="Charm of Cold Resistance",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\n{@note This charm can be bestowed by a ToA living in Icewind Dale or other cold regions by using their Magical Gift action.\n\nThis charm allows you to give yourself resistance to cold damage as an action. This benefit lasts for 24 hours, after which the charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-cozmioko-s-glory.drde2014"]={title="Charm of Cozmioko's Glory",subtitle="Recompensa - DrDe - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nThis charm infuses you with the righteous vengeance of the brass dragon Cozmioko. You can use it as a XPHB action and choose one of the following effects:\n\n• Cozmioko's Fire\n\n• Cozmioko's Light\n\n• Cozmioko's Revenge\n\nOnce you use the charm, it vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-cure-wounds.idrotf2014"]={title="Charm of Cure Wounds",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nThis charm allows you to cast the cure wounds spell (3rd-level version) as an action, no components required. Your spellcasting ability for this charm is Wisdom. Once used, this charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-darkvision.dmg2014"]={title="Charm of Darkvision",subtitle="Recompensa - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nThis charm allows you to cast the darkvision spell as an action, no components required. Once used three times, the charm goes away."},
  ["reward.charm-of-darkvision.xdmg2024"]={title="Charm of Darkvision",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 99\n\nThis Charm allows you to cast XPHB. Once used three times, the Charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-dhakaan.efa2014"]={title="Charm of Dhakaan",subtitle="Recompensa - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nWhile you have this Charm, you know the XPHB language. You can expend the Charm to cast XPHB."},
  ["reward.charm-of-diabolical-inspiration.bgdia2014"]={title="Charm of Diabolical Inspiration",subtitle="Recompensa - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nYou grow a short, vestigial tail when you receive this charm unless you have a tail already. When you make an ability check, an attack roll, or a saving throw, you can use this charm to gain advantage on the roll. Once used nine times, the charm vanishes from you, as does your vestigial tail."},
  ["reward.charm-of-druidcraft.idrotf2014"]={title="Charm of Druidcraft",subtitle="Recompensa - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 228\n\nThis charm allows you to cast the druidcraft cantrip as an action, no components required. Once used three times, this charm vanishes from you."},
  ["reward.charm-of-electromancy.rhw2014"]={title="Charm of Electromancy",subtitle="Recompensa - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\nThis Charm has 3 charges. You can expend 1 charge from this Charm to cast the XPHB spell. Once all its charges are expended, the Charm vanishes from you."},
}
